  {"a":"kennen","b":"aatrox","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk him while his Q knockups are still his only damage and he has no W chain-pull setup yet."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a third Mark of the Storm stun-locks him out of his R combat-stat window — your single biggest all-in spike in this lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the Q-W-E-R combo into a kill before his drain heal and Death's Dance let him out-sustain it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His threat window: a full-build Aatrox with R active and Q sweetspots can survive your stun and out-drain you in extended melee once Maelstrom is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip him with Thundering Shuriken and stack Mark of the Storm so the third stack stuns before he lands a sweetspot Q","Hit level 6 even or ahead and burst him with Slicing Maelstrom while his R combat stats are still on cooldown","Kite his Q knockups with Lightning Rush, never standing still in melee where his W chain-pull can drag you into a full combo"],"foe":["Land the sweetspot tip of his Q knockups to flip an extended trade and proc his passive heal on you","Catch you with W chain-pull, then E-dash in and R for the combat-stat all-in while you're locked","Survive your level 6 burst and drag the game past two items where his drain and Death's Dance out-sustain your magic"]},"early":"Aatrox is weakest exactly when I'm strongest — levels 1-3 he only has his Q knockups and no W chain-pull setup, so I poke with Thundering Shuriken and chip with Electrical Surge autos to start stacking Mark of the Storm. Never eat the sweetspot tip of his Q; sidestep into the inner ring or dodge entirely, because each connected sweetspot heals him through his passive. Stack two marks with Q plus a W on-hit and I can land a real trade or even a stun on him if he steps up to last-hit.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay mine on poke, but his level-3 combo is real now, so I respect the W chain-pull — if he lands it he E-dashes in and the full Q sequence flips the trade and procs his heal. Hold my distance and keep marking. At 6 I take over: Slicing Maelstrom plus a third Mark of the Storm stun-locks him before he can pop R for the combat stats, and that's the one window where I reliably blow him up. Save Lightning Rush to either close the gap for the stun or peel out if he gets the chain-pull first.","late":"My peak is the first-item spike — Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns the R combo into a clean kill before he completes Death's Dance. After two items it tilts back: a full-build Aatrox heals through my burst with his passive drain, survives the stun, and out-trades me in extended melee once Maelstrom is on cooldown. So I close this out on my 6-and-first-item window, then stop trying to solo-duel him and pivot to teamfights where my AoE R stun-locks his whole side.","whys":["You out-poke a level-1 Aatrox with Thundering Shuriken and Electrical Surge while his only tool is a Q knockup he can't reliably land — chip and start stacking marks.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack to a Mark of the Storm stun before he has a W chain-pull to answer, so you own this overstep window.","His level-3 combo comes online and a sweetspot Q flips the trade with his heal — keep poking but it's a genuine skill-check on dodging his knockup now.","You still out-range his Q and any extended trade he forces costs him more than your chip, as long as you never get caught by the W pull.","Slicing Maelstrom into a third mark stun-locks him out of his R combat-stat all-in — this is your hardest pre-item window and you win almost any duel here.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the full Q-W-E-R combo into a kill before his drain heal and Death's Dance can out-sustain your magic burst.","Full-build Aatrox heals through your burst, survives the stun, and out-drains you in melee once Maelstrom is down — close before this or pivot to teamfights."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"akali","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real poke trade and chunk her before she has Shroud — punish every last-hit she walks up for."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus the Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks her even if she Shrouds, since your R keeps ticking marks on the cloud and stops her from dashing out clean."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill — if you have a pink ward for her W Shroud, her one escape window evaporates and you blow her up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Akali has 2+ items her R recast + Shroud reset lets her dodge your R channel and burst your squishy body the instant Maelstrom is down — this is her takeover."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm before she can drop W Shroud to break the chain","Hit your level 6 R and stun-lock her through the Shroud so she can't dash out with E or R","Bring a control ward for her Twilight Shroud and close the lane on your 6 / first-item spike"],"foe":["Drop W Twilight Shroud to go untargetable and break your Q mark chain and dodge your R","Wait out your R channel, then E-dash in and R-execute your low-HP body once Maelstrom is down","Farm safely under tower and scale to 2+ items where her reset burst outpaces you"]},"early":"Akali has no Shroud at level 1 and a weak early — so do you, but your Q out-ranges everything she has and your mark chain hurts. Throw Thundering Shuriken at her every time she steps up to last-hit, and weave Electrical Surge autos to stack marks toward the third-stack stun. Don't dive in mindlessly; she can E-dash away, but if she eats two marks and you W-proc the third, you stun and chunk her before she can answer.","mid":"From 4-5 keep chipping with Q but respect her Shroud now that it's up — don't waste R on a cloud she's hiding in unless you've forced her out. At 6 you're at your single biggest spike: your full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock locks her in place, and because Slicing Maelstrom keeps ticking marks it can re-stun through the start of her Shroud. Bait her W early, hold your R for after it, and a control ward removes her only clean escape. Kill her here.","late":"Once Akali hits 2+ items she takes the matchup back. Her R recast and Shroud reset let her wait out your Maelstrom channel, then E-dash onto your squishy caster body and execute you the moment your R is down. Don't try to solo-duel her late — your job is to use your global R and AoE engage in teamfights where she can't isolate you, and to have already won lane on your 6/first-item window so her scaling never gets to matter.","whys":["Akali is a weak level-1 and her W Shroud isn't up yet, and your Q out-ranges her — poke her off the wave and start stacking marks.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a poke trade and threaten a two-spell mark stun she can't yet Shroud away.","You own the wave here — chain Q-W marks toward the third-stack stun before she has the Shroud uptime to break the chain.","You keep the poke edge and she still can't all-in you safely; chip her with Q and refuse to dash in where her E could trade back.","Akali's level 6 R gives her a two-part dash plus execute and a Shroud-backed escape, and she can wait out your Maelstrom channel then burst your low-HP body — this window is hers.","Her first AP item turns her reset burst lethal: she E-dashes in, R-executes, and Shrouds out before your R comes back, so she controls the trade.","Your global-range R and AoE engage win the teamfight even as she out-duels you in a sidelane — group and peel rather than trying to 1v1 her."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"akshan","win":["Kennen","Skill","Akshan","Akshan","Kennen","Akshan","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real Thundering Shuriken poke trade before his E swing gives him kite range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a Mark of the Storm stun-lock is your hardest all-in — catch him before his E grapple resets the gap."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt turns your full R combo into a kill on a squishy Akshan who can't pool the burst."},{"when":"Late","text":"His passive camo revive plus roams off E swings make him a snowball threat — close the side lane before he gets uncatchable."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken (Q) to stack Mark of the Storm before he kites out on his E swing","Hit your level 6 R all-in window while his E grapple cooldown is down and he can't escape the stun-lock","Use Lightning Rush (E) to close his kite range, not to chase blind into his revive camo"],"foe":["Kite-skirmish with E grapple swings, dodging your Q so Mark of the Storm never reaches the third-stack stun","Poke you down with Q/W from range and abuse your squishy body before you commit","Roam off E mobility and stall lane so his camo passive and revive snowball the map"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are your cleanest window — Akshan has to step into your Thundering Shuriken (Q) range to last-hit, and a second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chain Mark of the Storm into a real poke trade before his E grapple gives him kite distance. Don't waste E chasing his swing; hold it to close range only when you can actually land the third mark and stun. The danger is overstepping into his Q/W return poke on your fragile body, so trade with Q range, not auto range.","mid":"Levels 4-5 swing toward him — once Akshan has his E swing mobility and Q/W poke online he kite-skirmishes your short cooldowns and chips your low HP from outside your stun range, so respect his trades and farm. Then level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom plus a Q-W-E (or Flash) stun-lock chains Mark of the Storm faster than he can grapple away, and that all-in wins almost any pre-item duel. Bait his E swing, then commit your R when he has no escape.","late":"Late game is a knife-edge. Your first-item R combo still blows him up if you catch him, but his passive camo, the revive, and constant E-swing roams make him a map threat that survives the one window your R isn't up. Close the side lane on your 6/first-item spike and pivot to teamfighting, where your AoE R stun-lock is far more reliable than chasing a camouflaged Akshan around the map.","whys":["You force him into your Thundering Shuriken (Q) range to CS and chip with Electrical Surge autos while his E swing isn't enough to fully escape yet.","Even — your level-2 poke is real, but his Q/W return damage on your squishy body makes the trade a wash.","His E grapple swing now gives him the kite range to dodge your Q and deny the third Mark of the Storm stack.","He skirmishes your short cooldowns with E mobility and pokes your low HP from outside your stun-lock range.","Slicing Maelstrom plus a Q-W-E stun-lock chains three marks faster than his grapple can reset the gap — you win the all-in.","His E-swing kite and camo revive let him survive your R window and out-poke you when Maelstrom is on cooldown.","Your Hextech Alternator R combo bursts his squishy frame before he can pool to camo — your last clean kill window before he roams off."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"ambessa","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Ambessa","Skill","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you mark-stun Ambessa if she steps up to W you, punishing her short melee range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ambessa's biggest window: her R repositions through your channel and her chain-CC combo can interrupt your Slicing Maelstrom before it stacks three marks."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your full Q-W-E-R stun-lock into a kill before she can dash out — your peak relative strength."},{"when":"Late","text":"If she gets ahead her sustained bruiser DPS out-fights your squishy body once R is down, so close before her 2-3 item power."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and Electrical Surge autos to chip Ambessa down before she can close the gap","Hold E (Lightning Rush) as a disengage to escape her dash-in chain-CC rather than spending it to engage","Stack three Mark of the Storm before she uses her dash to reposition out of the stun"],"foe":["Weave her dashes around your Q skillshots so they whiff and she takes no poke","Land her chain-CC to lock you down and interrupt your R channel before three marks land","Reach a 2-3 item bruiser spike where her sustained DPS out-trades your squishy caster body"]},"early":"Ambessa has no real ranged tool, so this is your zone: tag her with Q every time she walks up to last-hit and let Electrical Surge autos add chip. The danger is her dash-heavy combo closing the gap, so don't shove blindly into a position where she can W-burst you against the wave. From level 2-3 you can punish any overstep — second Q point plus W on-hit means an over-eager Ambessa eats a three-mark stun and a real trade before her dashes can carry her out.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a chip-and-respect stretch — keep poking with Q but don't burn E to engage, because she will dash in and chain-CC you the moment you commit. Hold E as your escape. The danger flips at 6: her R lets her reposition through your Slicing Maelstrom and her CC chain can interrupt the channel before you stun-lock her, so this is the one window she owns. Don't drop R hoping to all-in a full-health Ambessa with her dashes and ult up — bait those out first.","late":"Once you hit first item your burst takes over: Alternator/Rocketbelt turns the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock into a kill she can't dash out of, and your magic damage chunks her bruiser HP. That is your window to close. Don't let it become a long game — if Ambessa gets even, her sustained DPS and chain-CC grind down your squishy body the moment your R is on cooldown, so end the lane on your item spike and pivot to teamfights where your AoE R peels.","whys":["She has no ranged poke, so you freely chip her with Q and Electrical Surge autos while she can only walk up and take it.","Your second Q plus W on-hit lets you three-mark-stun her if she steps in to trade, and her short dashes can't escape the stun in time.","It's even — she can dash around a single Q to dodge it, but you out-range her if you keep your spacing, so the trade hinges on whether she lands her gap-close.","You still out-poke a pre-ult Ambessa, but hold E to disengage her dash-in rather than committing it, since she punishes any whiffed engage.","Her R repositions through your Slicing Maelstrom and her chain-CC interrupts the channel before three marks land, so she owns the level-6 all-in.","Your Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt spike cashes the R combo into a kill that her dashes can't escape — keep forcing the all-in here.","Your first-item burst still blows her up before her bruiser scaling matters, so close the lane on your spike before her 2+ item DPS reclaims it."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"aurora","win":["Kennen","Skill","Aurora","Aurora","Skill","Aurora","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real Thundering Shuriken poke trade before she has her E blink reset up to punish."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock — caught flat, she has no blink reset to escape three Marks of the Storm."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her first item (Lich Bane / Liandry's into your squishy body) is her threat peak: she pokes your low HP down and W-exiles to dodge your R channel."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Mark of the Storm chains plus your engage R reclaim it — once you can flash-R onto her, her blink can't reset out of a full stun-lock."}],"wants":{"you":["Land your level 2-3 Q poke and Electrical Surge on-hit before her E reset is online","Hit your level 6 spike and force a Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock while she's flat","Bait her E blink and W exile early, then commit your Mark stun-lock the instant they're down"],"foe":["Use her E blink reset to dodge your Q and disengage every time you E-in to stack Marks","Poke your squishy body with Q and root you, then W-exile to dodge your Slicing Maelstrom channel","Stall to her first AP item where she out-pokes and out-bursts your low-HP caster body"]},"early":"Aurora's whole answer to you is the E blink — it dodges your Thundering Shuriken and bails her out the moment you Lightning Rush in to stack Marks of the Storm. Don't waste Q at long range into a champion who can just blink the projectile; wait for her to step up to last-hit, then chip with Q plus Electrical Surge autos. Your level 2-3 window is real: a second Q point and W on-hit can land a genuine poke trade before her E reset is reliably available, so punish any greedy CS step there. Respect her Q poke and root — if she lands the root, she gets a free burst rotation into your fragile body.","mid":"At 4-5 you cede the hard-commit window — she has her E reset and W spirit up to dodge your E-in and exile out of any Mark chain, so you're chipping and respecting, not all-inning. Level 6 flips it hard for one window: Slicing Maelstrom plus Q-W-E-Flash-R is a stun-lock she cannot blink out of if you catch her flat, so look to force that all-in the instant her E and W are on cooldown. Don't channel R into an Aurora who still has her W exile — she'll phase out of the storm and leave you stunned-out and burned.","late":"She reclaims her first-item spike — Lich Bane / Liandry's pokes your low-HP body down from range and her E blink plus W exile let her sidestep your R channel, so a 1v1 sidelane into a fed Aurora is a losing trade. Your path back to parity is the teamfight: stop dueling her and use your AoE Slicing Maelstrom plus global threat to stun-lock her carries in a 5v5 where she can't blink out of every Mark. At 2+ items with Flash up you can still hard-engage her — a flash-R lands all three Marks before her blink reset answers — so pick the fight, don't take the poke war.","whys":["You out-poke a level-1 Aurora — one Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge autos chip her before her E blink reset matters, and she has no burst yet.","It's even — your level 2-3 Q poke is real, but her E blink dodges the projectile and resets, so neither lands a clean commit.","She gets her E reset and Q poke online — she blinks your Lightning Rush engage and pokes your squishy body without taking the Mark stun.","Her level-3 power plus E blink and W exile let her dodge every Mark chain you start, so you're chipping while she controls the trades.","It's a coin-flip at 6 — your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock kills her if she's flat, but her E blink or W exile escapes it if either is up.","Her first AP item out-pokes and out-bursts your low-HP caster body, and she blinks and exiles out of your R channel.","You reclaim it in teamfights — a flash-R lands all three Marks of the Storm before her blink resets, and your AoE peels for your team."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"camille","win":["Kennen","Skill","Camille","Camille","Kennen","Camille","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Your Thundering Shuriken (Q) outranges everything Camille has at level 1 — free chip before her Q true-damage proc is even threatening."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R) + Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks her through her E hookshot — your single best window to delete her before items."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Camille's Sheen/Stride spike: her E stun into W true-damage cone and Q proc out-trades your magic burst once her R isolates you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her R (The Hextech Ultimatum) walls you into a 1v1 her items now win — group, peel with R, never sidelane her alone."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken (Q) pokes and stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun before she can E-in","Hit your level 6 Slicing Maelstrom (R) all-in while she is on E hookshot cooldown","Buy Mercs/MR early so her W true-damage cone and Q proc do not blow up your squishy body"],"foe":["Hold E hookshot to dodge your Q and engage only after your R has finished channeling","Land her Q true-damage proc and W cone heal to out-sustain your poke in extended melee","Reach 1-2 items so her R isolation turns the lane into a duel her stats now win"]},"early":"Level 1-2 are yours: Thundering Shuriken (Q) outranges everything Camille owns, so chip her each time she walks up to last-hit and stack Mark of the Storm with your Electrical Surge (W) on-hit autos. The thing to respect is her E hookshot — if she stuns you into her Q-proc-W-cone combo your fragile body folds fast, so never throw a Q from inside her E range. By level 3 she has her full Q-W-E and out-trades you in melee; back off and poke from max range instead of contesting the wave toe-to-toe.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — her level-3 combo plus Q true-damage stacks out-damage your poke if she catches you, so keep stacking marks from range and don't get greedy on the wave. Then level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom (R) into your Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks her through her hookshot, and if she E's in you channel R and her own engage feeds the third-stack stun. Bait her E first, then Flash-R the all-in — this is your cleanest kill window in the whole lane.","late":"Once Camille hits one or two items the lane turns against you: her E stun into W true-damage cone heal and Q proc out-sustains your burst, and her R (The Hextech Ultimatum) walls you into the exact 1v1 her stats now win while your R sits on cooldown. Don't try to sidelane-duel her — you're a squishy caster and she's a scaler. Pivot to teamfights where your AoE R and global threat stun-lock her whole backline instead, and use R to peel the second she Ult-isolates a carry.","whys":["Your Thundering Shuriken (Q) outranges Camille's entire level-1 kit — free poke with no counterplay before she has E.","Even Skirmish: your Q chip is matched by her Q true-damage last-hits, and neither of you can safely commit yet.","Her level-3 Q-W-E combo out-trades you in melee — a Hookshot knock-up into Tactical Sweep chunks your low-HP body.","She owns the hard-commit window: a fed Camille all-in with W heal and Q true damage beats your poke if she lands E.","Slicing Maelstrom (R) plus your three-mark stun-lock blows her up before items — channel R when she E's in and her own engage feeds your stun.","Her Sheen/Stride spike arrives: E stun into W cone and Q proc out-trades and out-sustains your magic burst once her R isolates you.","Genuinely even late: she scales to win the isolated 1v1, but your AoE R and global engage keep you relevant in any teamfight."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Kennen","Skill","Skill","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Before she has W, one Thundering Shuriken plus an Electrical Surge auto chunks her squishy body — the only window where you out-trade her cleanly."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Her second Q (Twin Fang on poisoned targets) and W grounding come online and the lane flips to a poison war you can no longer win with raw Q poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her R face-stun answers your Slicing Maelstrom all-in — she stuns you mid-channel and Twin-Fangs you to death before your stun chain locks her."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With Liandry's/Rylai's she perma-slows and out-DPSes you through Mercs; your R cooldown is a death window in the sidelane."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken (Q) and Electrical Surge autos at level 1-2 before her W grounding and poison stacks come online","Use Lightning Rush (E) only when her R face-stun is down — never E in while she can stun-cancel your dive","Build Mercs early and roam/teamfight off your AoE R instead of trying to out-duel her in the sidelane"],"foe":["Stack poison with Noxious Blast then Twin Fang you down while kiting on her passive move speed","Hold Petrifying Gaze (R) for the instant you Lightning Rush in or channel Slicing Maelstrom","Slow you with Miasma so your step-up and your retreat both die, then Twin Fang your squishy body"]},"early":"Level 1 is your one clean window: she has no W yet, so a single Thundering Shuriken plus an Electrical Surge auto actually chunks her before she can poison-trade back. Take it, then respect the flip. Once she has W (poison) and her Twin Fang resets on grounded, poisoned targets, every prolonged trade favors her sustained DPS over your single-Q chip. Do not throw a Q and then walk up to auto-stack a mark — she just grounds you with W so you can neither E in nor E out, and Twin-Fangs the marked target down.","mid":"This stretch is hers, not yours. Her W grounding is the whole problem: it cancels your Lightning Rush engage AND your escape, so the moment you commit a mark stun she roots your dash and out-DPSes you with poison Twin Fang. At 6 it gets worse, not better — her Petrifying Gaze face-stun out-ranges and pre-empts your Slicing Maelstrom, so if you R-in she stuns you mid-channel and bursts your squishy body before the stun-lock ever lands. Bait her R with a fake E step, never a real one.","late":"You lose the sidelane 1v1 outright — she's a hard scaler and you're a short-cooldown squishy with R on a long timer. With Liandry's and Rylai's she perma-slows you out of E range and melts you through Mercs while her passive move speed keeps her ahead of your Q. Stop trying to duel her. Your value is the AoE R as a teamfight engager: stun-lock her backline with the rest of your team, not her face in a side bush where the ground-and-poison kills you every time.","whys":["Before she has W or poison stacks, your level-1 Q plus an Electrical Surge auto out-chunks her squishy body — the one stage you cleanly own.","Her W grounding and Twin Fang are still single-pointed, so it's a genuine poke-vs-poison coin flip neither of you wins outright.","You keep a Q-poke edge but her poison sustain heals it back and her W grounding starts shutting off your E — call it even.","Her level-3 poison combo and W grounding now out-trade and out-sustain your single-Q chip, and grounding kills your E commit.","Her Petrifying Gaze face-stun pre-empts your Slicing Maelstrom — she stuns you mid-channel before your mark stun-lock lands.","Her Liandry's/Rylai's first item out-DPSes and perma-slows your squishy caster body the moment your R is down.","Full-build Cassiopeia kites on passive move speed and Twin-Fangs you through Mercs — you cannot win this sidelane, only teamfight."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"chogath","win":["Kennen","Skill","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Land a Thundering Shuriken and Electrical Surge auto before he has a Feast stack — your only window where his HP pool isn't already insulting your magic damage."},{"when":"Lvl 2","text":"A second Q point plus W on-hit can land a two-mark poke, but he can sidestep Q with his huge body untouched and just W-silence you mid-stack."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His threat window, not yours — Rupture knockup into Feral Scream chains into Feast, and your Slicing Maelstrom does chip damage to a tank instead of bursting a squishy."},{"when":"Late","text":"Feast-stacked Cho'Gath with 1000+ bonus HP eats your full Q-W-E-R combo and answers with a true-damage R execute that ignores every point of your survivability."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken pokes from max range and stack Mark of the Storm before he closes, never standing in Rupture range","Punish him levels 1-2 before any Feast stacks pad his HP and his magic-flat MR makes your kit irrelevant","Roam and teamfight on your level 6 R rather than trying to solo-kill a scaling tank in lane"],"foe":["Land Rupture knockup then Feral Scream to silence your next cast while Vorpal Spikes slows you down","Eat free Feast stacks off the wave and minions to balloon his HP past your burst","Reach 2+ items where his true-damage R execute deletes you regardless of how you build defensively"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are the only sliver of this lane that's yours: a Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge on-hit autos can chip Cho'Gath before he has a single Feast stack to insult your magic damage. But respect his Rupture — if you step in to stack a third Mark of the Storm and he knocks you up, his Feral Scream silence stops the next cast, though it cannot cancel a storm already up. Poke from max Q range, never commit your E-in, and don't trade into the knockup.","mid":"From level 3 on, this slips away. Cho'Gath out-sustains your poke off Feast and minion HP, and your level 6 R does pitiful chip to a tank instead of bursting a squishy — your single biggest spike is wasted into a HP sponge. Don't burn Flash-R to all-in him; you can't kill through his stacks, and a whiffed engage hands him a Rupture into Feral Scream on your fragile body. Use 6 to roam mid or skirmish, not to duel the thing you can't kill.","late":"This is hopeless 1v1 and you know it — a Feast-stacked Cho'Gath with 1000+ bonus HP shrugs off your entire Q-W-E-R rotation, and his R is true-damage percent-HP that executes your squishy caster body no matter how you build. Never sidelane into him; never get caught alone. Your only value now is teamfights: peel from range with R's AoE stun-lock and let your team kite the giant, because face-to-face he simply eats you.","whys":["You can land a Thundering Shuriken and Electrical Surge auto before any Feast stack exists to pad his HP — your one clean poke window.","A second Q and W on-hit threaten a two-mark trade, but his oversized body dodges Q and his W silence answers, so it's a genuine coin-flip.","From here he out-sustains your poke off Carnivore and minion HP, and his Rupture knockup into Feral Scream beats your stun chain.","He hits his level-3 Rupture-W-E combo while you concede hard-commit windows — your poke can't out-damage a tank's Feast sustain.","Your R channel does chip to a tank instead of bursting a squishy, so his single biggest counter-window arrives exactly when yours should — he owns it.","Even with first-item burst you can't blow up a Feast-stacked tank, and his flat MR plus HP blunts your all-magic kit.","Feast-stacked with 1000+ bonus HP he eats your full combo, and his true-damage R execute ignores every defensive item you buy."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"darius","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk Darius from range before his E-pull is even up — your cleanest free-poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom turns your Mark of the Storm into a full stun-lock — R-Q-W chains three marks and shreds him before his bleed stacks or R execute matter."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill — your magic burst blows him up through his lack of MR."},{"when":"Lvl 1-3 melee","text":"Darius's biggest threat: if you facecheck into E-pull range he yanks you in, stacks Hemorrhage with empowered Q, and the bleed plus true-damage R execute deletes your squishy body."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken from max range to chip Darius and stack Mark of the Storm without entering E-pull range","Reach level 6 and chain three marks with R-Q-W for the stun-lock all-in before he can E-Q you","Kite with Lightning Rush move speed and slow so his empowered Q can never connect at the rim"],"foe":["Land Apprehend (E) to pull your fragile body into Hemorrhage and empowered Q range","Stack five bleeds for Noxian Might, then sit on you with the move-speed boost so you can't kite","Drag the fight past 9 minutes where his all-in and Noxian Guillotine reset out-trade your poke"]},"early":"Darius's whole early game is the E-pull — Apprehend yanks you into Hemorrhage bleed and his outer-blade Q, and your squishy body cannot survive that exchange, so never last-hit inside E range. Stay at the tip of Thundering Shuriken: poke him, stack Mark of the Storm, and let Electrical Surge chip him every few autos from outside his reach. He has no way to close the gap if you respect the pull, and by level 3 your two-point Q plus W on-hit out-damages anything he can do back.","mid":"This stretch is a tug-of-war until 6. Levels 4-5 you keep the poke edge but must respect his level-3 E-Q-bleed combo — if he gets a clean pull he wins that all-in outright, so kite with Lightning Rush and never trade inside pull range. At 6 it flips hard: Slicing Maelstrom plus a Flash or E-in stun-locks him before Noxian Guillotine ever comes up, and the AoE storm stacks three marks faster than his bleed can kill you. That R window is your single biggest spike — force the all-in there.","late":"Once you have your first item your magic burst blows Darius up — he buys almost no MR, so Hextech Alternator into your R-Q-W combo deletes him before his bleed or R execute matters. But this stays a knife's edge: if your R is down and he lands one E-pull with Noxian Might stacked, his bleed plus Guillotine reset still erases your squishy frame. Close the game on your 6 and first-item spikes, group for teamfights where your AoE R peels for the team, and never sidelane a fed Darius 1v1 with your ult on cooldown.","whys":["You out-range him with Thundering Shuriken and Electrical Surge autos while his E-pull is not even available yet — poke for free from outside Apprehend range.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit chunks him hard, and at level 2 he can't pull-combo you if you hold the tip-of-Q spacing.","His level-3 E-Q-Hemorrhage all-in finally matches your poke, so if he lands a pull he trades even — respect the bleed and it stays a skill duel.","You keep the ranged poke edge and kite his empowered Q with Lightning Rush slow, denying the pull-in that is his only answer.","Slicing Maelstrom chains three Marks of the Storm into a full stun-lock before Noxian Guillotine or his bleed can kill you — you own this all-in window outright.","Your Hextech Alternator burst blows him up through his near-zero MR, but a clean E-pull into Noxian Might still trades, so the first-item duel is a coinflip on his pull landing.","With your R down a Noxian Might Darius out-sustains and resets on your squishy body — close before this, then pivot to teamfights where your AoE R rules."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"drmundo","win":["Skill","Kennen","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your cleanest window: a second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit can chip him before his passive regen and Q cleavers come online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom normally wins the all-in, but Mundo pops Maximum Dosage and heals through your whole R channel — you stun-lock and he survives."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Mundo's spike, not yours: Spirit Visage plus MR turns your Liandry's/Rocketbelt burst into chip while his percent-HP Q out-trades you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once your team has MR shred and you pivot to teamfight peel, his R is a single big heal you can wait out instead of soloing him."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 2-3 window with Q poke plus Electrical Surge before his passive regen snowballs","Keep your distance and only mark-stun him when his Q cleaver is on cooldown","Roam and teamfight off your R instead of trying to solo-kill a Spirit Visage Mundo"],"foe":["Soak your Q poke, heal it with his passive, and farm to Spirit Visage plus MR","Land percent-HP Q cleavers on your squishy body to out-trade your pokes","Reach 6 and use Maximum Dosage to heal through your R and walk you down"]},"early":"Early is your one real edge, but it's thin. At level 1 you both do nothing — chip with a Q at max range and last-hit with Electrical Surge on-hit, don't step into his Q cleaver. Your level 2-3 window is the cleanest you'll get: a second Q point plus W lets you land a poke trade or even a two-spell mark before his passive regen and percent-HP Q come online. Bank that lead now, because his Q heals back chip you can't keep up with once he points it.","mid":"This stretch belongs to Mundo and you have to accept it. His percent-HP Q cleaver hits your squishy body for a flat chunk no matter how far ahead you are, and his passive plus E sustain eat your poke. At 6 your full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock looks lethal — and it just isn't here: he pops Maximum Dosage mid-channel, heals through your entire storm, and the move speed lets him walk you down after. Don't suicide your R into him 1v1; save it to peel or to catch his jungler.","late":"You never solo this Mundo — once he has Spirit Visage and MR your all-magic kit barely scratches him, and his R is a heal you can't burst through alone. Your value flips to the map: roam with your R, dive squishies in fights, and let your team bring the MR shred and the second wave of damage that actually beats his single big heal. Treat the sidelane as a stalemate, group, and win the game everywhere he isn't.","whys":["Level 1 is even — one Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip, but he does nothing back yet and your fragile body can't commit either.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lands a real poke trade before his passive regen and Q cleaver come online — your cleanest window.","His percent-HP Q cleaver chunks your squishy body and heals back your chip, so he starts out-trading you the moment he points it.","He out-sustains your poke with passive plus E and shrugs your all-magic kit, conceding nothing while you hit no hard-commit window.","Your R stun-lock looks lethal but Maximum Dosage heals through the whole channel and the move speed lets him walk you down after.","Spirit Visage plus MR blunts your Liandry's/Rocketbelt burst into chip while his percent-HP Q keeps out-trading you — his spike, not yours.","Once your team brings MR shred and you peel off your R instead of soloing him, his single big R heal is something you can finally wait out."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"fiora","win":["Fiora","Fiora","Fiora","Skill","Skill","Skill","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Fiora's W parry eats your Q stun-starter or your E-in and stuns you back, so every early mark you throw is on her terms, not yours."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom is your one pre-item even window — R stun-locks her so she cannot proc vitals or Q out, but she can still W the channel's first tick to break it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes your Q-W-E-R into burst, but a Fiora who parries your R or your E-engage flips the all-in and procs four vitals on your squishy body."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once you have two items and a sidewave R+Zhonya's pattern, your AoE and disengage finally let you kite her vitals — your only owned window all lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes from max range so you never feed her a target ability to W-parry","Hold R until her W is on cooldown, then stun-lock her so she cannot Q-dash out or proc vitals","Survive to 2+ items where Zhonya's plus your AoE R let you peel her dash and kite the duel"],"foe":["Bait out your Q, E or R and W-parry it for the stun, turning your own engage into her kill window","Q-dash onto your squishy body and roll vitals for percent-max-HP true damage you cannot itemize against","Drag the lane to extended melee where her sustain and items out-duel your short-cooldown caster body"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are hers, not yours. Every spell you throw to start a Mark of the Storm chain — the Q poke, the E dash-in — is a target she can W-parry, and her parry stuns you mid-cast and refunds her cooldowns. So poke ONLY with max-range Q at the wave, never step into a position where an E-engage looks tempting, because she is waiting to parry it. Your body is fragile and her Q-dash plus vital procs chunk you faster than your two-spell mark trade chunks her.","mid":"Level 6 is the one window you can call even — Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks her so she can't Q-dash away or stand still to roll vitals, and the AoE stacks marks fast. But she will hold W for the channel: if she parries your R's first tick she breaks the lock and the all-in is hers. So bait her W with a Q or a feint E FIRST, then commit R. Through Levels 4-5 it's chip-and-respect — you keep the Q poke edge but she owns every hard-commit window the second her dash and vitals are up.","late":"This is finally your window, and the only one. With two items and Zhonya's you stop being a body she runs down and become a kiter: R for the AoE stun, E to disengage her dash, Zhonya through her vital burst, and your magic damage doesn't care about her early MR-less build. Play it as a sidelane peel and a teamfight engage, not a raw 1v1 — she still wins the clean duel, but you've stopped giving her free parry targets and your AoE finally outscales a single-target duelist.","whys":["Her W can parry your very first Q or E and stun you back, so you have no safe way to start a mark chain at level 1.","With a second point and her Q-dash up, she parries your poke and rolls a vital before you can stack a third mark for the stun.","Her level-3 Q-Q-vital combo out-trades your two-spell mark trade and your fragile body can't sit in the extended melee she forces.","It's chip-and-respect — you keep a max-range Q poke edge but she owns every all-in window her dash and parry are up for, so it nets even.","Maelstrom stun-locks her out of dashing and vital-rolling, but she can W the channel to break it, so the 6 all-in is a coinflip on her parry, not yours.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt R-combo can blow her up, but a parried R or E flips it into four vitals on you — the burst race is genuinely even.","Two items plus Zhonya's let your AoE R and E-disengage finally kite her dash and out-team-fight a single-target duelist, the one window your magic out-scales her."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"galio","win":["Kennen","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your Q and Electrical Surge autos out-range his Q tap before he stacks any magic resist — chip him while he can only farm."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Once his W taunt is online he reduces your damage and turns your mark-stun into a free counter-engage, so your trades flip negative here."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His ult is a global flash-engage knock-up — he can leave lane to game-wide impact while your R only matters where you stand."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His MR stacking plus his W damage-reduction taunt blunt your all-magic burst right as your Liandry's/Alternator combo should be peaking."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-1 poke war with Q and Electrical Surge autos before any MR comes online","Stack three Marks of the Storm for the stun the instant his W taunt is on cooldown","Roam or shove and crash before his global R lets him out-impact you across the map"],"foe":["Walk up and W-taunt mid-trade so your mark-stun and burst get reflected back","Stack magic resist early to make your all-AP kit chip for nothing","Hold his global R to swing a fight bot or mid while you are stuck top"]},"early":"Level 1 is the one window that is yours: your Q (Thundering Shuriken) out-ranges his short Q tap, and your Electrical Surge autos chip harder than his passive magic-damage hits before he buys a single point of MR. Land Q at max range and weave in marked autos, but do NOT step in to chase a third Mark of the Storm — the second he hits level 2-3 his W (a taunt that reduces incoming damage) flips everything. If you commit your mark-stun while his W is up, he just taunts you, eats reduced damage, and walks away ahead.","mid":"This is his stretch, not yours. His W taunt is the answer to your whole combo — it shuts off your E-in stun-lock, reflects your aggression, and lets him trade back through your burst. Only all-in when you have personally seen his W go on cooldown. At 6 the threat isn't even your lane: his R is a global flash-engage knock-up, so he can vanish to win a fight bot or mid while your Slicing Maelstrom only matters where your feet are. Track his R timer and ping it the moment he steps back to base or starts roaming.","late":"It evens out late because you both become teamfight pieces rather than duelists. Your R + Flash + three-mark stun-lock still wins a fight if you catch his carries before he can W-taunt-peel, but his stacked magic resist means you can't solo-delete him — focus the squishies behind him, not the Galio wall. He answers your engage with his own R and his damage-reduction taunt, so the side that lands its ult on the right target first wins. Don't ult into his W; bait the taunt, then channel.","whys":["Your Q out-ranges his Q and your Electrical Surge autos out-chip his passive before he has any magic resist — the one window you clearly own.","His W taunt comes online and reduces your trade damage while flipping your mark-stun attempt into a free punish.","With W plus a second Q he reduces your poke damage and out-trades you through your own burst — respect the taunt.","He concedes nothing here: every time you E-in to stack marks his W taunt cancels the engage and turns it around.","His R is a global flash-engage knock-up that out-impacts your locally-bound Slicing Maelstrom — he wins the map at 6.","His MR stacking and W damage reduction blunt your Alternator/Liandry's spike exactly when your all-in should peak.","Both of you become teamfight tools — your stun-lock engage trades evenly with his taunt-peel and global R, so it comes down to ult timing."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"gangplank","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Skill","Gangplank","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge (W) on-hit lets you out-poke his barrels and threaten a two-mark trade before he can chain a third keg."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R) into a Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks him through his barrel chain and ignores his crit-stacking passive entirely."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill, but he's also hitting Sheen/Trinity and his global R starts swinging map state."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full-build Gangplank barrel-chains from screens away, Remove Scurvy cures your three-mark stun outright, and crit autos out-DPS your squishy body."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm before he detonates his barrel chain, then E-in for the third-stack stun","Hit level 6 and force the R + Q-W-E stun-lock while his Remove Scurvy (W) is on cooldown","Close the lane on your 6/first-item spike and roam — every minute you wait, his global R and crit scaling pull ahead"],"foe":["Chain barrels (Q) into a detonation combo to poke your low-HP body down before you stack three marks","Hold Remove Scurvy (W) to cure your three-mark stun and heal off the poke you banked","Survive to 2+ items where crit autos, barrel chains, and global R (Cannon Barrage) out-scale your squishy caster pattern"]},"early":"Gangplank's whole early game is the barrel chain (Q places a keg, autos or another keg detonate it) and you don't want to eat a fully-chained explosion, so weave behind minions and punish him in the gaps. Your edge here is real: a level 2-3 Q poke plus Electrical Surge (W) on-hit chips faster than his single-keg pokes, and he can't dodge your long-range Q the way a mobile laner can. Don't blow E to chase — if you over-step into a primed barrel he free-trades you, so poke, stack a mark or two, and back off before his keg lands.","mid":"At 6 you take the lane: bank two stacks with Q and W, then E-in (or Flash-R) and Slicing Maelstrom locks him in place while your storm stacks the third mark for the stun — and all of it is magic, so his crit-armor body doesn't save him. The catch is Remove Scurvy (W): 22s at rank 1, it cures the stun outright and heals, so bait it before you commit the R all-in or your lockdown fizzles. Through levels 4-5 it's a chip-and-respect stretch — don't hard-commit without R up, just keep the poke lead.","late":"This is where you lose if you let it get here — Gangplank is a hard global scaler and you are a squishy short-cooldown caster. Once he has Sheen/Trinity, Infinity Edge crit autos, and barrels detonating from screens away, he chunks you before you ever stack three marks, and his W cleanses the only lockdown you have. Your job is to have ended the lane on your 6 and first-item spike: snowball, then pivot to teamfights where your AoE R peels and engages, because you will not out-duel a fed Gangplank in the sidelane.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s, but your Q poke plus Electrical Surge autos out-chip his single un-chained keg — last-hit and deny without burning E.","Your second Q point and W on-hit let you land a real poke trade his barrels can't match, and immobile GP can't dodge your shuriken.","With Q-W you can two-mark him on an overstep and threaten the stun, owning the wave while his crit passive and barrel chain are still weak.","He hits his level-3 barrel-chain detonation combo and Remove Scurvy comes online to cleanse and heal, so it's a chip-and-respect stretch — don't hard-commit.","Your R unlocks the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock, but a held Remove Scurvy cures the stun itself and heals, so the window turns on whether he saved that 22s cleanse.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into kill pressure, but he's also spiking Sheen/Trinity and his global R starts tipping the map in his favour.","He out-scales hard — full-build crit autos, screen-range barrel chains, and Cannon Barrage burst your squishy body while W cleanses your stun, so play safe and let your team handle him."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"gnar","win":["Skill","Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Gnar","Gnar"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Gnar's level 2-3 is his cleanest window — boomerang (Q) plus Hyper (W) on-hit out-poke your fragile body before you can stack three marks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom flips the all-in: E onto him, cast R, and the storm restacks Mark of the Storm to stun-lock him out of mini form."},{"when":"Rage bar full","text":"Mega Gnar's Wallop (W) stun and GNAR! (R) wall-slam, plus the bonus tankiness — transform mid-trade and he stuns your E-in flat."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill — force the all-in the instant his rage bar is empty and he's stuck in mini form."}],"wants":{"you":["E-in or Flash onto mini-Gnar when his rage bar is empty, then R to stun-lock before he can transform","Land Q-shuriken poke and W-marks to reach the third-stack stun while he's small and squishy","Force your level 6 all-in on a marked Gnar before Mega form's Wallop stun can drag you off your 550 storm"],"foe":["Kite in mini form with boomerang (Q) hops and Hyper (W) auto-poke, never letting you stack three marks","Bank rage so Mega Gnar's Wallop (W) stun lands the moment you E-in to all-in","Out-poke your low-HP body levels 2-3 and use his second wind-up to deny your stun chain"]},"early":"Gnar's boomerang (Q) and Hyper (W) on-hit out-range your Q-shuriken trades while you're at your most fragile, so don't walk up to throw a single Q and eat two boomerang catches for it. Last-hit at the tip of Q and only commit a poke when his boomerang is mid-flight or on cooldown. The catch you must respect: at levels 2-3 he can stack Hyper bonus-magic autos faster than you can build Mark of the Storm to your third-stack stun, so trading straight up loses — chip and reset your marks instead.","mid":"This is where you claw it back. At 6 your Slicing Maelstrom turns a marked Gnar into a stun-lock kill: E-in to apply a mark, cast R to restack Mark of the Storm fast, and burst him before he can boomerang away — but ONLY when his rage bar is empty and he's stuck in mini form. The whole mid game hinges on the rage bar: if it's full, Wallop's 7s stun and the GNAR! wall-slam pin you while the storm burns down, so wait it out and fight his small, squishy form.","late":"You need to have closed it. Once Gnar hits two items he's a Mega-form frontline who survives your R window and CCs your team while staying out of E range in mini form. Your squishy caster body can be focus-killed the moment R is down, and GNAR! slams you into a wall to cut the retreat you have no dash for. Pivot to teamfight engager — flank and R the backline rather than dueling a transformed Gnar in the sidelane, because he reclaims the straight 1v1 here.","whys":["Both of you are fragile level 1 — your Q-shuriken poke and his boomerang roughly trade, so it reads even until someone's spells come online.","Gnar's level 2-3 spike beats you: Hyper (W) on-hit autos out-poke your low-HP body before you can stack three marks for the stun.","His boomerang (Q) catch plus Hyper out-ranges your trades and his second wind-up denies your mark chain — he owns this window.","You regain footing — bank Q-poke and reset your marks around his boomerang cooldown, neither side can hard-commit cleanly yet.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your E-in, R stun-lock all-in on a mini-form Gnar, but his rage bar threatens GNAR!, so it's a knife-edge even window.","Your first-item burst wants to cash in, but once his rage bar fills, Wallop and GNAR! stun you and drag you off the 550 storm radius, flipping it.","Two-item Mega Gnar survives your R and CCs you down once it's on cooldown — he out-scales your squishy caster pattern, so kite him to teamfights."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"gragas","win":["Kennen","Skill","Skill","Skill","Gragas","Gragas","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"You poke first — one Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips Gragas before he has a Body Slam to close, and his only answer is to drink his pool."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Two Q points and W on-hit let you stack Mark of the Storm for a stun on an overstepping Gragas, but his Body Slam-into-Q displaces you out of the third mark."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gragas's biggest threat: Explosive Cask blasts you out of your own 550 storm radius, and his W damage reduction lets him eat the ticks and walk you under tower."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Gragas peaks with Rocketbelt/Cosmic Drive — Body Slam plus Cask burst trades evenly with your R combo and his pool out-sustains your poke."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Thundering Shuriken at max range so Electrical Surge on-hit poke beats his pool sustain before he reaches you","Stack three Marks of the Storm to land a stun while his Body Slam is on cooldown, then E-in to burst","Hold Slicing Maelstrom until his 100s Explosive Cask is spent, so it cannot blast you off your own storm"],"foe":["Drink Drunken Rage to out-sustain your Q poke and soak the lane until 6","Body Slam into you the instant you step up to throw a Q, displacing you before the third mark stuns","Save Explosive Cask to blast you out of your own storm or off him mid-stun-lock"]},"early":"Lane is a poke race and you draw first blood on it. Hit Thundering Shuriken at max range and let Electrical Surge's on-hit chip away every time he steps to last-hit — his only sustain is Drunken Rage, and your magic out-paces a single pool early. The danger is stacking marks: the moment you walk up to apply a third Mark of the Storm, his Body Slam dash displaces you and his follow-up Q chunks you, so build stacks from range and don't commit the E unless his dash is down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay a chip-and-respect stretch — you keep the poke edge but his level-3 Body Slam-into-Q combo punishes any step-up, so pile Marks of the Storm from distance and refuse the all-in until that 14s dash is on cooldown. At 6 the window flips to him: Slicing Maelstrom only strikes the 550 around you, and Explosive Cask launches you straight out of that, while Drunken Rage's reduction lets him stand in it and walk you to tower. Only ult after you've baited his Cask.","late":"His first item is his strongest patch — a Rocketbelt or Cosmic Drive Gragas Body Slams in, reduces your R's damage with Drunken Rage, and Casks you off your combo, and his pool out-sustains the poke that carried your early. But once you have a real AP item and your R is up, you reclaim the duel: Q-W to stack marks, E-in for the stun, and Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him before his single dash can reset. Pivot to teamfights — your AoE R peels and your global threat matters more than dueling a fed Gragas in the sidelane.","whys":["You poke first — Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips him before he has Body Slam, and his only reply is to burn Drunken Rage to heal it.","His level-2 Body Slam can dash onto you the instant you step to stack a third mark, so the mark race is genuinely even here.","With two Q points and W on-hit you can stun an overstep, but his Body Slam-into-Q displaces you out of the third Mark of the Storm just as often.","You keep a poke edge but his level-3 combo punishes every step-up, so this stays a coin-flip chip-and-respect window.","At 6 his Explosive Cask blasts you clean out of your own 550 storm radius and Drunken Rage's reduction eats the ticks — he owns this all-in.","His Rocketbelt/Cosmic Drive spike plus Cask burst and pool sustain trades evenly-to-ahead against your R combo — this is his peak.","With a real AP item and R back up, your Q-W mark stack into E-in stun-locks him before his single dash resets — you reclaim the duel and the teamfight."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"garen","win":["Kennen","Skill","Garen","Garen","Skill","Garen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Your Q poke and Electrical Surge on-hit out-range his autos before he can silence-cancel anything — free chip while he can only walk up."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Garen's Q-silence-into-E-spin combo is his trade window; eat one E tick and you lose half your bar with no stun to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom flips the lane — Q-W-E into R stun-locks him before his W tenacity matters, and his R execute can't fire mid-stun."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Garen reclaims the duel with Stridebreaker/Sundered Sky sustain; his W eats your burst and R executes you out of your own combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes and Electrical Surge on-hit to chip Garen before he reaches you, since his only gap-close is raw move speed","Hit Level 6 and Q-W-E-R stun-lock him in one window before his W tenacity and item sustain come online","Hold E as an escape, not engage — bait his Q-silence-into-E spin, then disengage out of the spin radius"],"foe":["Walk you down with passive regen up, then land the Decisive Strike silence so you cannot cast Q, W, E or R at all","Trade short with E-spin while his Q silence is on you, then disengage before you stack the third mark","Survive your Level 6 all-in with W damage-reduction + tenacity and R-execute your low-HP body once your R is down"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are genuinely yours — Q (Thundering Shuriken) plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-range Garen's autos, and all he can do is walk forward with no gap-closer, so chip him freely and deny his passive regen. The lane flips at 3 the moment he gets E: his Q-silence-into-spin is a real short trade, and the silence shuts off your R, W and E mid-cast. Never throw a Q from inside his auto range when his Q is up — eating one silence-into-E tick costs you half a bar with no stun to fire back, since you can't reach the third Mark of the Storm stack yet.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — he has his full Q-E-W combo and you don't have R, so chip with Q from max range and refuse to stand in spin radius when his silence is up. Then 6 is your equalizer: Q-W-E to pre-stack marks, then Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through the third stack before his W tenacity can shrug it, and his R execute can't fire while he's stunned. That single window is why this lane reads even instead of losing — land it on cooldown, because outside of it he wins the short trade.","late":"Once Garen has Stridebreaker or Sundered Sky he reclaims the duel — his W cuts your burst, passive regen heals the poke between fights, and his R true-damage execute deletes your squishy body the instant your R is down. You don't out-sidelane him, so stop dueling and become the teamfight engager: your AoE R and global threat win 5v5s and let your team peel his all-in. Look for flanks and group fights, not a 1v1 he now out-sustains.","whys":["You out-range him with Q poke and Electrical Surge on-hit while he has only autos and no gap-closer — pure free chip.","His Q silence and E spin aren't online yet, but neither is your stun — trade Q for Q and it stays even.","Garen gets E: his Q-silence-into-spin short trade beats you because the silence cancels your kit and you can't reach the third-mark stun.","No R yet means you concede his hard-commit window — he Q-silences and spins you down, so chip from max Q range and don't stand in spin radius.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through his W tenacity and blanks his R execute mid-stun, but his full combo answers if you whiff — genuinely a coin-flip window.","His first-item sustain (Stridebreaker/Sundered Sky) plus W damage-reduction lets him survive your burst and R-execute you once your R is down.","He out-sustains the 1v1 with passive regen and items, but your AoE R and global pressure win the teamfight — so it evens out as a group-stage threat, not a sidelane duel."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"graves","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Your Q (Thundering Shuriken) out-ranges his shotgun autos — chip him on cooldown before he stacks his powder for the burst."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through Quickdraw, but Smoke Screen cuts your sight and slows you — Flash on top before he kites out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt turns your three-mark stun into a kill, and magic damage ignores the armor he stacks as a tanky ADC."},{"when":"Mid-Late","text":"His biggest threat: a fed Graves shotgun-bursts your squishy body in one E-reposition before you build marks — respect his all-in when his E is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q (Thundering Shuriken) at max range to chip him before he closes shotgun distance","Hit your level 6 R into him while his E dash and smoke are on cooldown","Build to a magic-damage burst item so his ADC armor and tankiness don't save him"],"foe":["Cut your vision and slow you with Smoke Screen (W) so your marks never reach three stacks","E-dash-reposition out of your stun radius and shotgun-burst your low-HP body","Stack armor/HP as a tanky ADC and scale his shotgun crit past your one-combo window"]},"early":"Graves wins the trade if you walk into shotgun range, so poke him only with max-range Q (Thundering Shuriken) and let Electrical Surge autos chip when he steps up to last-hit. His True Grit gives him resistances stacking in combat, but your magic damage cuts through it, and at levels 1-2 you out-range his shotgun cone — keep throwing Q on cooldown and don't chase, because his E dash punishes overextension. Bait Smoke Screen (W): it cuts your sight and slows, and it is 26s at rank 1.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep the poke edge but respect his E-dash burst — don't stand still loading a third mark where he can reposition behind you and shotgun. At 6 your Slicing Maelstrom is the all-in: Q-W-E to stack Mark of the Storm, then R to stun-lock him through his dash and smoke. Flash on top first if he holds E, because a free Graves dashes out the back of your 550 storm and smokes your vision of him.","late":"Your first item is the spike that closes this lane — Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your three-mark stun into a kill, and because your whole kit is magic damage, the armor and HP he stacks as a tanky ADC don't blunt it the way they would an AD top. Force the all-in on your 6/first-item window while he's still squishy; if he gets two items and items of crit, his shotgun bursts your fragile body the instant your R is on cooldown, so pivot to teamfights and peel with R rather than trying to outscale his sidelane DPS.","whys":["You out-range his shotgun autos at level 1 — chip with Q and Electrical Surge while he has no E to close the gap.","A second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade his shotgun can't return from outside his range.","His E dash comes online and lets him reposition behind your marks to shotgun-burst — neither of you owns this cleanly, so play the range game.","You keep the Q poke edge while he can't all-in without his E, so chip him down and respect the dash window.","Your R stun-locks him, but Quickdraw and the Smoke Screen sight-cut answer it — your Flash timing against his escape, so it reads even.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt turns your three-mark stun into a kill, and your magic damage ignores the armor he stacks.","Your first-item burst still blows up a tanky-ADC Graves before he gets two crit items — close it here while marks and R win the all-in."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"gwen","win":["Kennen","Skill","Skill","Kennen","Gwen","Gwen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real mark-stun on Gwen before her E dash and Snip Snip rhythm come online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Gwen's spike, not yours: Hallowed Mist blocks targeting from outside, so she W's as your storm lands — step into the cloud with her or it hits nothing."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your Q-W-E-R stun-lock into a real kill before her mist cooldown is reliably up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two-item Gwen out-sustains your burst, mists your R on reaction, and Q true-damage shreds you the second your stun-lock is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip her with Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm before she gets a wave to E-dash off of","Punish her short range at levels 2-3 with a W-accelerated mark stun while she has no mist","Force the kill on your 6 / first-item all-in before Hallowed Mist's cooldown is reliable"],"foe":["Drop Hallowed Mist as your R lands so the storm and your marks whiff from outside","Farm safe with Snip Snip (Q) and her E reset, then scale to two items","Bait your stun-lock, mist it, and Q-true-damage you down once your R is on cooldown"]},"early":"Gwen's range is short and she rarely spends an early point on the mist, so levels 1-3 are yours to bully. Land Q (Thundering Shuriken) on her approach to stack Mark of the Storm, and at level 2-3 weave Electrical Surge autos in to pop the third-stack stun before she can E-dash away. Don't dump everything chasing her through minions where Snip Snip (Q) out-trades a whiff — chip, stun, back off. If she does take W, it is 22 seconds.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay a poke edge — keep marking her with Q and W and respect her E reset if she dashes in. The trap is the mist: she can only be hit by enemies standing inside it, so a Gwen who W's mid-combo blanks your storm unless you Lightning Rush in after her. Bait the 22s mist or all-in before she drops it — Q-W-E-Flash-R only lands the full stun if you are in the cloud with her.","late":"This is where she takes over, so the game has to be closed before it. Two-item Gwen out-sustains your squishy caster pattern: she mists your R on reaction, Q's true damage straight through your MR, and her E attack-speed shreds your low-HP body the moment your stun-lock is on cooldown. Don't try to 1v1 a scaled Gwen in the sidelane — group, save R as a teamfight peel/engage, and let your 6/first-item lead on the map carry the game instead of dueling her.","whys":["You out-range her with Q (Thundering Shuriken) and she has no mist yet — chip her and start stacking Mark of the Storm while she can only farm.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lands a real mark stun on a short-range Gwen who has no E reset charge yet to escape it.","Once she has E (Skip 'n Slash) the dash-reset trades even with your poke, so this is a genuine skill window before her 6 spike.","You keep the poke lead pre-6 — mark her with Q and W and punish any step-up before Hallowed Mist exists to bail her out.","Her spike, not yours: Hallowed Mist blocks you from outside the cloud, so unless you step in with her, your whole stun-lock whiffs.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your Q-W-E-R combo into a kill, but her mist can answer it on cooldown, so it's a skill check on baiting the cloud.","Pre-mist your R combo still bursts her, and your map lead from early closes it before two-item Gwen's sustain and Q true damage take over."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Kennen","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"His turrets (H) wall you off the minions and his W rockets out-poke your single Q — his cleanest window, not yours."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom turns the corner: E onto him, R stun-locks through his turret cover and you stack three marks faster than he can E-grenade out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a one-shot — force the all-in on his E (stun grenade) cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"His turret farm and shroom-free zone control reset every wave; if you stall past your item spikes he out-pokes and out-zones you again."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his E stun grenade, then E-in and chain Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun before he can re-zone","Hit level 6 and convert every all-in with R + Flash through his turret cover","Roam mid/bot with E and R the moment he shoves you under turret — your global threat beats his immobility"],"foe":["Set up a turret triangle so you can never walk to a minion without eating rockets","Land the CH-2 grenade's direct hit to break your step-up and reset the zone","Shove you under tower with turrets + W and freeze you off CS to deny your level 2-3 spike"]},"early":"His turrets are the whole problem early — they wall you off the minions and zone the wave, so every Q you throw to last-hit also feeds his rockets (W) back into your fragile body, and one Q poke from you loses that exchange. Don't facecheck the turret triangle to force a trade; CS at max Q range and respect that his E stun grenade is a free interrupt on any step-up. You can't punch through three turrets and an E at level 1-3, so eat a little chip and hold the wave for your level 6.","mid":"Level 6 flips it. Once Slicing Maelstrom is up you stop trading single Qs and start all-inning: E-in (or Flash) onto him, R stun-locks him through his turret cover, and your AoE marks chunk both him and his turrets while he's stunned. Bait the E grenade first — if he burns it to disengage, you E onto him on its cooldown and the stun chain finishes the kill. He has no escape past a short-range E, so the moment he steps up to wave-clear or you catch him off his turret line, that's your window.","late":"After your first-item spike (Alternator/Rocketbelt or Liandry's) your R combo one-shots him, so close the lane while you out-burst him. The danger is letting it stall: late, his turret farm and zone control reset every single wave and he out-pokes your short-cooldown caster body again, so don't sit in lane trading. Use your global threat instead — when he shoves you under tower, E-roam mid or bot and snowball off your R, because a parked Heimer who can't follow is exactly the matchup you punish on the map.","whys":["His turret triangle and W rockets zone you off CS while your one Q poke and Electrical Surge autos can't punch through three turrets — his window.","A second Q point doesn't matter when his turrets out-DPS your step-up and his E stun grenade interrupts any commit — he still owns it.","He has turrets, W rockets and a ready E grenade; you have no stun and a squishy body, so he keeps zoning you off the wave.","Your poke edge returns but his turret cover blunts your single-target chip — neither of you can hard-commit, so it reads even.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the E-in R stun-lock that chains Mark of the Storm through his turrets faster than he can E-grenade out — you own this all-in.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt R combo one-shots him, but he can rebuild the turret zone between trades, so it's down to whether you force the all-in on his E cooldown.","His turret farm and zone control reset every wave and out-poke your short-cooldown caster late, but your global E/R roam threat keeps it even — take the map, not the duel."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"illaoi","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Illaoi","Skill","Illaoi","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q poke plus W on-hit chips her low-base-health body while she's stuck slamming the wave with E unavailable to punish you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom over a Test of Spirit lets you stun-lock her and burst the spirit vessel before her tentacles cash in."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Her E (Test of Spirit) is the threat window: if she rips your spirit you must sprint from your own slammed tentacles or she heals huge and chunks you."},{"when":"Late","text":"In her tentacle field her W + R turn a fight she shouldn't win into a sustain bomb, so never duel her on top of grasping tentacles."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q + Electrical Surge pokes from max range so you never stand in her tentacle field","Hit your level 6 and R-stun her on top of a missed or used E (Test of Spirit)","Dodge her E entirely so she can never rip your spirit and farm tentacle slams off you"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit (E) to drag your spirit out and force you to flee through her tentacles","Pull you onto a wall of slammed tentacles where her W and R out-sustain everything","Stack tentacles in lane so any all-in you commit gets answered by AoE thumps and healing"]},"early":"Illaoi is glued to the wave early — her tentacles only spawn on cooldown and she has no dash, so levels 1-3 are your cleanest poke window. Throw Thundering Shuriken (Q) and weave Electrical Surge (W) on-hit autos to chip her low base health while she's busy slamming minions; her sustain only goes nuclear once tentacles are up around you. The one rule: never stand inside a cluster of grasping tentacles when you commit autos, and respect that her E (Test of Spirit) is a long skillshot — sidestep it and she has almost no kill pressure on you.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are the danger stretch, not because she out-trades your poke but because Test of Spirit (E) flips the lane: if she rips your spirit, you have to literally run from your own marked tentacles or eat massive AoE damage and feed her healing. Don't facecheck for the E and don't greed a trade near three tentacles. At 6 you reclaim it — Slicing Maelstrom (R) over a used or whiffed E stun-locks her and lets you stack Mark of the Storm to burst the spirit vessel before her tentacles finish their thumps; that's your one clean all-in window.","late":"Late game you stay a fragile caster and she becomes a tentacle fortress — inside her field her W (Harsh Lesson) and R (Leap of Faith) tentacle storm out-sustain and out-AoE anything you throw, and if she lands E in a teamfight you're dragged into the worst possible ground. Never side-lane duel her on top of tentacles; your job is to flank from range, R the backline, and let your team peel her off the field. If you can't kill her on your 6/first-item spike, treat her as a split she wins and play for objectives elsewhere.","whys":["She's stuck slamming the wave with no dash — your Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip her low base health for free at level 1.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit out-pokes a tentacle-less Illaoi who can't punish you without standing on top of you.","It evens out as her tentacles come online — keep poking but respect that one Test of Spirit (E) flips the trade entirely.","Her E rips your spirit and forces you to flee your own marked tentacles, eating AoE and feeding her sustain — this is her window.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks her over a used E and you burst the spirit vessel before her tentacles cash in — your spike answers hers.","If her tentacles are up and your R is down, Harsh Lesson and her field out-sustain your squishy body and reclaim the duel.","Neither wins cleanly late — you can't duel her on tentacles, but from range your R-flank and her need to land E keep it a coin-flip."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"irelia","win":["Kennen","Skill","Irelia","Irelia","Kennen","Irelia","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Q + W on-hit lets you stack two marks for a poke trade before her Q dash chains come online."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Her Q reset + E (Flawless Duet) stun combo lands — once she gets her E root on you she out-trades in melee."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom + E-in stun-locks her through her dashes — your single best all-in window; Defiant Dance blunts no magic."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her first item (Trinity/Sundered Sky) plus stacked attack speed turns fights her way — commit on her 16s E, never off it."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes from max range so you never feed her Q a minion or champ to dash-reset on","Hit your level 6 R and stun-lock her with Mark of the Storm before her W can block the burst","Count your marks and step out at two, so her E stun never lands mid-third application"],"foe":["Q-dash through the wave or onto you to gap-close and land her E stun chain","Heal your whole poke back with Bladesurge resets off the wave and off you","Stack her passive shred in an extended melee trade where your squishy body loses"]},"early":"Level 1 you out-range her — sling Q from max distance and chip with Electrical Surge autos, but don't step into her Q-dash range to throw it. The trap here is her Q resets: never let her dash off a low minion or off you into a reset, so poke when the wave gives her no dash target. By level 2-3 your Q + W mark stacking lets you win a quick poke trade, but the moment she has her E stun up, respect it — if she Q-dashes in and lands Flawless Duet, she out-trades your fragile body in melee.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are her window — she hits her Q-reset-into-E-stun rhythm and heals it all back off Bladesurge, so don't commit while her 16s E is up. Hold Lightning Rush to move OUT as she dashes IN, breaking the chain before the stun lands. Then level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom plus your E-in stun-locks her through her dashes — that's your cleanest all-in, and Defiant Dance reduces physical damage, so it does nothing against your kit at all.","late":"Her first item (Trinity Force / Sundered Sky) plus passive armor shred reclaims the extended-trade window — if you fight her with R down, her sustain and DPS grind your squishy body out, so don't sidelane-duel her on cooldown. But you spike back at your AP item: once Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt lands, your R combo bursts her faster than her W can block or heal, and your AoE stun-lock makes you the better teamfight and 2v2 threat. Close around your item spikes — pick her off with R before she snowballs into a true late-game duelist.","whys":["You out-range her at level 1 — Q-poke from max distance and deny her any minion to Q-dash-reset on while she has no stun yet.","Even window: your Q-W marks chip her, but her Q dash and W block trade back — neither commits without the level advantage.","Her Q reset into E (Flawless Duet) stun chains onto you, and in melee her shred out-trades your fragile caster body.","She owns the hard-commit window — Defiant Dance cuts physical damage only, but her E stun punishes any overstep while your R is down.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks her through every dash — your full Q-W-E-R mark combo wins this all-in even into her W.","Her first item and passive armor shred reclaim the extended trade — fighting her with R on cooldown loses to her sustain and DPS.","Your AP item turns the R combo lethal — you burst her past her W and out-teamfight her AoE-stun before she scales into a late duelist."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"jax","win":["Kennen","Skill","Jax","Skill","Jax","Skill","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Open with a Thundering Shuriken (Q) the moment Jax steps to last-hit — pure ranged poke he cannot dodge with E yet."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Jax's biggest early threat: Q-into-target then E Counter Strike eats your autos and stuns, turning his W empower into a kill if you are caught flat-footed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Jax's R Grandmaster-at-Arms gives huge resists and third-hit magic damage — his all-in beats yours in raw melee if Counter Strike eats the autos you need."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"With Liandry's/Rocketbelt online your Mark-of-the-Storm burst chunks even a resist-stacked Jax — kite the E, then R-stunlock from max range."}],"wants":{"you":["Land free Thundering Shuriken (Q) pokes while Jax is stuck CSing, building Mark of the Storm chip he cannot heal","Refuse to auto into a raised Counter Strike (E) — wait it out, then activate W to detonate marks and stun","Fight at max range with R Slicing Maelstrom and kite his Q-leap so he never lands his full empowered combo"],"foe":["Bait your E-in or auto, then pop Counter Strike (E) to dodge it and stun you mid-combo","Q-leap onto you the instant you step up for poke and W-empower a burst before you stack marks","Drag the fight long past level 6 where R resists and on-hit empower out-sustain your squishy caster body"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: Jax has no Counter Strike point yet, so open with Thundering Shuriken (Q) every time he walks up to last-hit and let Electrical Surge autos chip — he eats free Mark of the Storm with no way to dodge. The danger arrives at 2-3 once his E is up: never throw an auto into a raised Counter Strike, because he stores those dodges into a stun and Q-leaps for an empowered W burst. Poke with Q at max range, sidestep his leap, and only commit autos when his E is on cooldown.","mid":"This is the respect stretch — Jax's level-3 combo (Q-leap, E stun, W on-hit) out-trades your fragile body if he catches you, and at 6 his Grandmaster-at-Arms (R) hands him resists and third-hit magic damage that beat your all-in in straight melee. Don't try to win a toe-to-toe here. Keep chipping with Thundering Shuriken from range — it lands through Counter Strike, which only dodges attacks — and hold Lightning Rush as an escape, not an engage.","late":"Once you have a first item and especially at 2+ (Liandry's, Rocketbelt or Hextech), your Mark-of-the-Storm burst reclaims the lane — magic damage ignores the armor Jax stacks, and a full Q-W-E-R stun-lock chunks him before his empowered autos and R sustain can answer. Fight at max range: pre-stack a mark or two with Q, dodge his leap, then R Slicing Maelstrom to lock him down. You also out-teamfight him hard, so group and let your AoE storm peel while he is forced to splitpush alone.","whys":["Jax has no Counter Strike yet, so your Thundering Shuriken (Q) and Electrical Surge autos chip him free while he last-hits.","His E point arrives and a raised Counter Strike can dodge your commit and stun back, so the level-2 trade is genuinely even.","Jax's level-3 combo — Q-leap into E stun into empowered W — out-bursts your squishy body if he lands it, so this window is his.","You keep a poke edge with Q but his E reset and leap threat make any hard commit a coinflip, so it reads even.","Grandmaster-at-Arms (R) gives huge resists and third-hit magic damage, beating your pre-item all-in in straight melee — his window.","Both spike: your first item cashes the R stun-lock into burst while his empowered autos peak, so it stays a skill matchup.","Magic damage ignores his stacked armor — your Mark-of-the-Storm burst and AoE R reclaim the duel and stomp the teamfight."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Jayce","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Jayce owns the early range war — a gate-boosted Shock Blast outranges Thundering Shuriken and chunks your squishy body before you can stack Mark of the Storm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom flips it: Q-W-E-Flash-R chains three marks for the stun-lock and his ranged-form HP bar melts inside your storm."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a real kill — your single best window to close before he out-pokes you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Jayce's hammer-to-cannon poke + E knockback keep him at range; once your R is down he chunks you from outside your engage and you fall off as a squishy."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 1-3 poke and reach 6 with even-ish HP, then Q-W-E into Flash-R for the stun-lock all-in","Use Lightning Rush (E) move speed + brief tankiness to close the gap when his Acceleration Gate Q is on cooldown","Win on your 6 / first-item spike and snowball before his ranged poke and E knockback take over the sidelane"],"foe":["Land Shock Blast through his own Acceleration Gate to poke your low-HP body before you stack three marks","Swap to hammer and Thundering Blow you off him, then gate back out to his poke range","Drag the lane long so his hammer-cannon poke and range advantage grind you down once your R is on cooldown"]},"early":"Jayce out-ranges you outright here — his Shock Blast fired through the Acceleration Gate (Q) reaches further than your Thundering Shuriken and hurts far more on your fragile body, so you cannot win the raw poke war. Last-hit at max Q range, take the safe CS, and refuse to walk up to throw a shuriken you'll lose the trade on. You have no stun yet and one missed dodge to his gated Q can cost you a third of your bar — respect it and stack Mark of the Storm only when he steps in for a hammer trade.","mid":"Level 6 is your one true equalizer — Slicing Maelstrom finally gives you a hard all-in his poke kit can't answer once you're on him. Bait his cannon-stance E knockback (it's his only disengage from your Lightning Rush), then E-in, W to accelerate the marks, and Flash-R to stun-lock inside the storm where his squishy ranged form melts. At first item (Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt) that combo turns into a kill — this is your peak, so look for the all-in the moment his Q poke is down and his E is on cooldown. Outside of that window he still pokes you out, so don't trade autos in lane, trade with the full R commit.","late":"This is your hardest stretch and the only place you reclaim ground — but only because Jayce is also a squishy poke champ, not because you out-scale him. Once your R is on cooldown he sits at cannon range and chunks you with gated Shock Blast before you can close, and a swap to hammer gives him Thundering Blow to shove you back off. Your edge is that Lightning Rush passes straight through his minions and your AoE R wins any teamfight where you can Flash onto him — so group and peel rather than dueling him in the sidelane, and never face his poke down a wave without R up.","whys":["Shock Blast fired through his Acceleration Gate out-ranges Thundering Shuriken and bursts your squishy body before you have a stun — farm at max range.","He keeps the range lead at 2 — his gated Shock Blast pokes you out while your single Q point can't threaten a mark stun back.","His level-3 hammer combo plus cannon poke out-trades your two-spell mark attempt; you still have no R to punish an overstep.","Through 4-5 he pokes you on a chip-and-respect pattern — his Q poke and E knockback deny every Lightning Rush gap-close you try.","At 6 it's genuinely even — your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock all-in answers his poke, but his E knockback and superior range can still pre-empt the engage.","His own poke spike with first item keeps the lane at range — but your Hextech Alternator R combo finally trades blow-for-blow, so it's his edge by a hair, not a stomp.","Late you claw it back: he's a squishy poke champ too, and your AoE R + Lightning Rush tankiness win the flash-engage teamfight he can't kite once you're on him."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"karma","win":["Karma","Karma","Karma","Karma","Kennen","Karma","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Her Mantra is online from level 1, so RQ Soulflare plus Inner Flame out-ranges my single Thundering Shuriken and I have no Lightning Rush yet to dodge or close — eat the zone, soak XP, and don't trade into a poke war my energy bar can't fund."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"My one clean window: a second point in Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets me layer two Marks of the Storm and, if she oversteps to drop a Soulflare in melee, E-in to detonate the third stack and stun-burst before her shield resets."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"My only unmatched spike: Slicing Maelstrom on a 120-second cooldown, 550 range, while Karma gains nothing at 6 — Mantra was hers from level 1. Spend it on her step-up or a 2v2 dive, never on her shove."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Her Liandry's/Seraph's spike sharpens RQ burst and shield value so she out-pokes and out-shields me again, and my squishy caster body can't all-in through it — this is the window I most need to have already snowballed a roam."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait an overstepped RQ Soulflare or a missed root, then E-in to detonate the third Mark of the Storm and stun-burst her before Inspire's shield comes back","Stack Marks with Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit so the stun is ready the instant she walks into my E range to last-hit or zone","Roam with my level-6 Slicing Maelstrom 2v2 dive instead of farming a lane I lose — punish her low base mobility on the map, not in lane"],"foe":["Pelt me with Inner Flame and zone with RQ Soulflare at max range so I bleed and burn energy without ever reaching E range","Hold Focused Resolve to root me the second I commit a Lightning Rush, before I land three Marks for the stun","Snowball the level 1-to-first-item poke lead into plates and towers behind Inspire's move speed before my R and AP teamfight scaling come online"]},"early":"Karma out-ranges me here and I have nothing to close the gap until Lightning Rush comes online, so respect her early. Her Mantra is up from level 1, meaning her Inner Flame poke and an RQ Soulflare zone both out-distance my single Thundering Shuriken, and my energy bar can't fund a straight poke war back. My one real opening is level 3: a second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets me chain two Marks of the Storm, so if she oversteps to drop a Soulflare in melee, I E-in, detonate the third stack for the stun, and burst her before Inspire's shield refreshes. Until then, soak XP through the zone and never throw a Q into her face to squeeze chip — that's how I lose the energy war.","mid":"This is her takeover, not mine. By levels 4-6 she's chaining Inner Flame into RQ Soulflare to perma-shove me off the wave and tax plates behind Inspire's move speed, and my Slicing Maelstrom does nothing to farm a lane I can't physically reach her in. My R is an all-in and 2v2 dive tool, so the move is to stop trying to win the 1v1 — ward up, soak what I can, and look to roam with my level-6 Maelstrom flank onto a sidelane or skirmish where her low base mobility can't escape the AoE stun. If I do commit a Lightning Rush in lane, expect a Focused Resolve root waiting; only go when I can land all three Marks before she peels.","late":"She keeps the lane edge into her first item — Liandry's/Seraph's sharpens RQ burst and shield value, so she out-pokes and out-shields my squishy caster body all over again, and I can't all-in through it. My win condition was never the sidelane duel; it's the teamfight. A Flash-into-Slicing-Maelstrom on her clustered backline is game-ending, and my global R threat and elite peel matter far more than this lost lane. So I trade lane for tempo: catch a roam off her shove, group, and look for the multi-target stun-lock where my AoE outweighs her enchanter utility — never face-check into a Karma who pokes me to half before I can ever E onto her.","whys":["Her Mantra is up at level 1, so RQ Soulflare plus Inner Flame out-ranges my single Thundering Shuriken and I have no Lightning Rush yet to dodge or close it.","Her energy-free poke and Gathering Fire Mantra refunds out-pace my energy-gated Q and Electrical Surge chip before I can afford to keep spending.","My cleanest early window: a second Q point plus Electrical Surge stacks two Marks, so if she oversteps a Soulflare I E-in and detonate the third for a stun-burst.","She ranks Q and chains RQ Soulflare to perma-shove me under tower, taxing plates behind Inspire's move speed while I can't reach her.","Slicing Maelstrom is the one spike she can't answer — Mantra was hers from level 1, so 6 gives her nothing. Flash-R her step-up.","Her Liandry's/Seraph's sharpens RQ burst and shield value, out-poking and out-shielding my fragile body, and she can pre-hold Focused Resolve to root my Lightning Rush.","She out-pokes and out-items me lane-for-lane, so my edge is the teamfight Flash-Maelstrom stun, not a sidelane duel I lose to her shields."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"kassadin","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kassadin","Kassadin","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm for the third-proc stun before Kassadin has a blink or his Q silence-shield to answer."},{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"He has no Riftwalk and a tiny HP pool — every Thundering Shuriken is free poke he can only soak, and an overstep gets him stun-locked."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Kassadin's spike, not yours: Riftwalk lets him blink out of your E-engage and your R channel, and each cast ramps his cost so chasing burns your energy for nothing."},{"when":"Late","text":"His Void Staff/Rod-of-Ages spike out-scales you — full-AP Kassadin one-combos your squishy body, so the game must already be closed."}],"wants":{"you":["Shove and trade Q poke into him levels 1-3 before Riftwalk exists, building toward the third Mark of the Storm stun","Land a level 2-3 mark-stun when he steps up to last-hit, then W-Q to chunk a third of his HP","Snowball the early lead into towers and roams so his level 16 scaling never arrives"],"foe":["Survive to 6 and use Riftwalk to dodge your E-in and blink out of your R stun-lock window","Soak Q poke behind Void Stone's magic reduction and Null Sphere's shield, then farm to Rod of Ages and Void Staff","Hit his item spike and roam mid/skirmish where his blink burst beats your cooldown-bound kit"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours to abuse: Kassadin has no Riftwalk yet and one of the squishiest early bodies in the game, so chip him with Thundering Shuriken from 950 range and stack Mark of the Storm. Every ability you cast adds one and the third stuns, so Q into W on-hit when he steps up to last-hit, then E in for the third and the free burst trade. Respect Null Sphere only while it is up — a 9-second shield that eats the magic damage your whole kit deals — and bait it on the wave first.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay even-ish — keep poking and banking the wave on your side, but the clock is ticking. At 6 the lane flips: Riftwalk means he can blink out of your E-engage and straight out of your R channel, and his Q shield plus passive eat the magic damage your whole kit is built on. Do not greed a stun-lock all-in he can just blink — that wastes your R and your energy. Instead use this window to shove, crash waves, and roam with your global threat before his items come online.","late":"This is Kassadin's game if it gets here. Once he finishes Rod of Ages and Void Staff he out-scales you hard — full-AP Riftwalk burst deletes your low-HP caster body before you stack three marks, and his blink ignores your stun chain entirely. Your job was to end on your 6/first-item window; if you didn't, stop trying to duel him in the sidelane. Group, peel with R in teamfights, and let your team answer the scaling assassin you can no longer pin down 1v1.","whys":["Kassadin is a famously weak, blink-less level 1 with a fragile body, so your single Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip him for free while he can only farm.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real mark-stun if he oversteps — he has no Riftwalk yet to escape the third Mark of the Storm proc.","With your full early kit you out-poke and out-trade a pre-6 Kassadin whose only defense is a Q shield that can't cover the wave and the poke at once.","The lane levels out — you keep a poke edge but he banks farm behind his shields, so trade around his Q cooldown and hold your lead rather than forcing.","Riftwalk unlocks: he blinks out of your E-in and your R channel, and his shields blunt your all-magic burst, so his single biggest defensive spike answers your single biggest all-in.","His first AP item (Rod of Ages / Void Staff line) ramps his burst and effective HP while your squishy caster pattern plateaus — he reclaims kill pressure here.","Full-AP Kassadin out-scales you outright: his blink burst one-combos your low-HP body before you stack three marks, so you can no longer win the 1v1."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"kayle","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Skill","Skill","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm for a stun and chunk a melee-range pre-6 Kayle before she has waveclear."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock all-in — Kayle has no R invuln yet, so this is your cleanest kill window of the whole lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a real burst that blows up a still-squishy Kayle before her two-item ranged form."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kayle's level-11 ranged form plus a 120-second Divine Judgment turns the duel — she kites you out of Q range and your burst lands for zero."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack three Mark of the Storm with Q-W to stun and burst Kayle while she is still melee and immobile","Hit level 6 and force the Q-W-E-Flash-R all-in before her two-item ranged spike","Snowball the early lead into plates and a roam so the game ends before her level 11 ranged form"],"foe":["Survive to level 11 when her ranged-form upgrade lets her auto you out of Q range","Use her E waveclear to farm safe under tower and deny your poke without dueling","Save Divine Judgment so your Slicing Maelstrom burst lands on an invulnerable target"]},"early":"Kayle is melee and defenseless levels 1-3, so this is yours to take. Land Q (Thundering Shuriken) for free poke and let Electrical Surge on-hit autos stack Mark of the Storm — get the third stack and the stun, then walk her down. Don't overstay for a stack you can't finish, but every CS she walks up for is a free Q. She can't trade back and has no escape, so deny her last-hits and shove her off the wave.","mid":"Levels 4-6 are about converting before her items. She is still meleed and can only farm with E waveclear, but watch she doesn't just sit under tower and soak XP to level 11. At 6 your Slicing Maelstrom turns a mark stun into a full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock — she has no R invuln yet, so this is a near-guaranteed kill if you catch her stepping for CS or a plate. Force it; her whole game is surviving this window.","late":"Once Kayle hits two items and her level-11 ranged-form upgrade, the lane flips hard. She auto-attacks you from outside Q range, Starfire Spellblade gives ranged waveclear, and Divine Judgment makes her invulnerable for the whole storm, so your 120-second ult lands for zero. Your squishy caster body can't duel a fed scaler — close on your 6/first-item spike, pivot to teamfights where your AoE peels and engages, and let your team handle her side lane. Do not 1v1 her after she scales.","whys":["Kayle is melee and weak at level 1, and your Q poke with Electrical Surge autos chips her freely while she has no way to trade back.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm for a stun on a melee Kayle who has no escape or DPS yet.","Three marks land the stun and you burst a still-squishy Kayle, who can only farm with E and cannot punish your poke pre-items.","Levels 4-5 are even — she farms safe with E waveclear under tower soaking XP, and you respect her tower while waiting on your 6 spike.","At 6 we both spike — my Slicing Maelstrom on 120s against Divine Judgment on 160s, an invulnerability that eats the whole storm.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt burst can still kill her, but her first item and R invuln are coming online, so the spike edge is shrinking to even.","Her level-11 ranged form and R invulnerability flip the duel — she kites your short body out of Q range and negates your stun-lock, so she owns the late game."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"kled","win":["Skill","Kled","Kled","Kled","Kennen","Kennen","Kled"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Kled's mounted Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) yanks you in and his remount aggression wins the all-in before you can stack three Marks of the Storm."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R) plus a Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks Kled and can burst him off Skaarl into his dismounted state — your one clean kill window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into real kill pressure on Skaarl, the moment your burst most reliably overwhelms his courage shield."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Kled remounts and out-sustains your magic once R is down — his Skaarl HP regen and bonus AD reclaim the duel as you plateau."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge the Bear Trap (Q) pull, then chip with Thundering Shuriken from max range so he never lands a mounted trade","Hit level 6 even in HP and chain Q-W-E marks into Slicing Maelstrom (R) to stun-lock and burst Skaarl off him","Win on your 6/first-item spike and pivot to teamfights before his remount sustain takes over"],"foe":["Land Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) to drag you into mounted auto range while you are still building marks","Bully the early levels with Skaarl's bonus AD and force you off the wave before your stun comes online","Get dismounted safely, regen courage, and remount to out-sustain your burst in the extended late-game duel"]},"early":"Kled owns this stretch and you have to respect it. His Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) pulls you straight into Skaarl's beefed-up autos, and a mounted Kled simply out-trades your fragile body before you've stacked three Marks of the Storm. Do NOT walk up to throw a Thundering Shuriken (Q) inside his pull range — last-hit from max distance, weave in Electrical Surge auto-chip when he's busy on the wave, and never let him land the trap. If he dismounts (loses Skaarl), that's your only early window to commit a mark trade — punish the weaker dismounted state.","mid":"Level 6 flips it your way for one window. With Q-W-E you stack marks fast, and Slicing Maelstrom (R) stun-locks him long enough to blow up Skaarl — burst him into the dismounted state where he's squishiest, then E away. Bait his Q pull first; once Bear Trap is on cooldown, E-in, W to detonate marks, R to stun-lock. Your first-item Alternator/Rocketbelt makes this combo lethal. But know it's a timer — if you whiff the all-in or he remounts, you've handed the lane back.","late":"This is Kled's game and you have to accept it. He remounts, his Skaarl HP and bonus AD let him eat your burst and keep coming, and once Slicing Maelstrom is on cooldown you're a squishy caster he runs down. Your magic doesn't out-sustain his courage regen in an extended duel. Close the lane on your 6/first-item spike or you don't get a second chance one-on-one — pivot to teamfights where your AoE R and stun-lock peel for your team instead of dueling him in the sidelane.","whys":["You're both fragile turn-one, but a single Thundering Shuriken (Q) poke and Electrical Surge autos let you chip without committing — last-hit at max range and don't eat a Bear Trap.","Kled's mounted Skaarl autos plus Bear Trap on a Rope (Q) out-trade your no-stun body the instant he pulls you in.","His remount aggression and bonus AD bully the wave before you can chain three Marks of the Storm into a stun.","He hits his power trades on Skaarl while you're still conceding hard-commit windows — chip and respect the pull.","Slicing Maelstrom (R) plus your Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks Kled and bursts Skaarl off him — your single biggest spike.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt turns the R combo into a kill on the dismounted Kled — force every all-in on this timer.","He remounts and out-sustains your magic once R is down: Skaarl's regen and bonus AD reclaim the duel — close before this or pivot to teamfights."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","K'Sante"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm and poke K'Sante down while his W block is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks him before he can ult-isolate you — your hardest all-in and biggest spike."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes your R combo into real kill pressure — his percent-HP passive doesn't save him from full burst."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"K'Sante reclaims the lane: his R strips his own resists, gap-closes with the dash, and isolates you for an all-in you can't kite."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm while his W block is down to chip him before trades","Hit level 6 and E-in with R to stun-lock him before he can W-dash or R-isolate you","Close the game on your 6 / first-item spike before his fighter scaling and resists come online"],"foe":["Block your Q poke and key marks with W, then dash in to close the gap","Bait your R cooldown, then R to strip his resists and isolate you for the kill","Survive lane and scale into the 2+ item fighter who eats your magic burst and runs you down"]},"early":"Level 1 is even — one Q and your Electrical Surge autos chip, but you're squishy and Ntofo Strikes slows you at 450 range every 3.5 seconds, so don't overcommit. The real opener is levels 2-3: a second Q point plus W on-hit lets you build Mark of the Storm and land hard poke while Path Maker, his 14-second charge-dash, is down. Bait it — it stuns and the damage is true, so armour and MR are no answer. Never stand in melee with Path Maker up.","mid":"Levels 4-5 you keep the poke edge, but respect his Q knockup combo — don't stand in melee where he can W-dash + Q you into a wall. Level 6 is your takeover: Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks him through his own engage, and your full Q-W-E-Flash-R chains three marks faster than he can react. Force the all-in here before his resists stack — your magic ignores his armor, and he can't out-sustain the stun window pre-item. This is the window you must win the lane in.","late":"Once K'Sante hits 2+ items he flips this lane on you. His R strips his own resists and isolates you for a 1v1 your squishy body can't survive — and the dash closes any gap you try to kite with E. When your R is down you have no answer to his all-in. So end it early: snowball your 6 and first-item spike, take plates and pressure, and pivot to teamfights where your AoE R peels and engages rather than dueling him in a sidelane he now owns.","whys":["You're both fragile at level 1, but Ntofo Strikes reaches only 450 on a 3.5s cooldown — last-hit from 950 and don't commit.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit stacks Mark of the Storm for a real poke trade while his W block is on cooldown.","You own the wave and out-poke him here — bait his Ntofo block, then land Q and the mark stun on an overstep.","You keep the poke edge, but Path Maker is a 600-range dash that stuns for true damage — never stand in melee.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks him before he can R-isolate you — your full mark chain wins this pre-item all-in outright.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's turns your R combo lethal — magic ignores his armor and his passive can't tank full burst.","K'Sante out-scales hard: his R strips his resists, dashes onto you, and isolates you for a duel you lose — close before this."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"lillia","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm fast and chunk her before she has W/E to kite — your cleanest poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom is your spike: Q-W-E in stacks marks and the R stun-lock blows up her squishy body before her R sleep can reset the fight."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns the full mark combo into a kill — your peak window to delete her before she stacks AP."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once she has Liandry's/Riftmaker her DOT passive and W/E kiting let her run from your stun chain — your R-down windows get dangerous."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q at range to start Mark of the Storm, then W and E-in for the third-stack stun","Hit your level 6 and force the R stun-lock all-in before she can kite with W speed","Use R + first item to delete her squishy body in the 2v2 dive before she scales"],"foe":["Kite your 170-range E with Blooming Blows' stacking Move Speed and a Swirlseed slow","Land Lilting Lullaby's sleep on you the moment you E-in to commit","Stack her passive DOT and AP items to out-scale your fragile caster body"]},"early":"Lillia has no point-and-click on you early, so your job is to land Q at max range and start chaining Mark of the Storm before she has W and E up to kite. At levels 2-3 a Q plus W on-hit can stack you to the third-mark stun on an overstepping Lillia, and her DOT passive can't out-trade the burst. Watch her W (the big-radius slam) — it's her main damage and slow, so don't walk straight at her; angle your E-in so the contact mark lands when she's already committed to a W.","mid":"This is your lane. Through levels 4-6 you out-poke her squishy body and at 6 your Slicing Maelstrom is the whole matchup: Q-W to pre-stack marks, E-in to stun, R to lock her and chunk before Lilting Lullaby flips the trade. Force the all-in while Watch Out! Eep! and Swirlseed are down — she has no dash, only the Move Speed off Blooming Blows, so a clean E-Flash catches her. Her sleep does not interrupt the storm, but eating it mid-fight still hands her the trade.","late":"You win the lane on your 6 and first-item spikes, but late Lillia is the problem — her passive DOT, W slow and E bounce let her kite your stun chain, and any time your R is down she can run you over. Once she has Liandry's and Riftmaker she out-sustains your poke and your squishy caster body folds to her DOT. Close the game on your power windows and pivot to teamfights where your AoE R stun-locks her team rather than dueling her in the sidelane.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 — your single Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip, but with no stun and a fragile body neither commits, so it reads even.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit stacks Mark of the Storm to the stun before she has W/E up to kite — you own this poke window.","With Q, W and E online you can land a real mark stun on an overstepping Lillia, and her DOT passive can't out-trade your burst.","You keep the poke edge at 950, but Blooming Blows stacks her Move Speed and its edge deals true damage — resistances don't answer it.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that blows up her squishy body before her R sleep can reset — your biggest spike.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill on her low-HP frame — this is your peak relative strength, force every all-in.","Once she stacks Liandry's/Riftmaker her DOT and W/E kiting out-sustain your poke and run from your stun chain — play your R windows tight and let teamfights answer her."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"lucian","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"Even start — your Q poke trades with his double-shot passive, but his Q+W combo out-ranges you, so just chip and farm without overstepping."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Your cleanest early window: second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit can land a Q-W three-mark stun if he steps up to trade or last-hit, and his E is his only out."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your biggest spike — Q-W-E-Flash R stun-locks Lucian's squishy body and Slicing Maelstrom burns him down before his Culling can fire."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a one-shot — his low HP pool has no answer to your magic burst through his lack of MR."}],"wants":{"you":["Land a third Mark of the Storm with Q-W to stun and burst before his E dash resets","Hit your level 6 and force the R all-in while his Culling and E are the only tools that can save him","Snowball your first-item burst into a kill before his Galeforce/zhonyas-less mid game lets him kite"],"foe":["Bank Lightslinger double-shots to shorten Relentless Pursuit before I commit","Kite back with Q-W double-shot poke and his passive double-tap, never letting you E onto him","Survive your 6 / first-item spike and scale into a Navori kiting carry your stun can't reach"]},"early":"Lucian out-ranges your raw poke — his Q (Piercing Light) and W (Ardent Blaze) combo plus the double-shot passive will chip you if you walk up to throw a Q, and your body is just as squishy as his. Last-hit with the tip of Thundering Shuriken and don't burn E (Lightning Rush) chasing a kite he'll just dash out of. Your real edge is levels 2-3: a second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun if he steps up to trade or contest a melee minion, and his E is his only escape from the lock.","mid":"This is your takeover stretch. From 4-5 you keep a poke edge while he respects your stun, and at 6 Slicing Maelstrom turns every all-in lethal: Q-W to two marks, E or Flash in to land the third-stack stun, then R stun-locks his low-HP body while it ticks him down before his Culling (R) can output. Bait his E dash before you commit — once it's on cooldown he has no way out of your mark chain. With Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt your burst simply deletes him; he carries no MR and his HP pool can't survive the full combo.","late":"Once Lucian has two-plus items — Navori, attack speed, a kiting build — he reclaims the floor: he double-shots and dashes around you, and if you whiff the engage or your R is down he bursts your squishy caster body faster than you can chase. Your game is to close this on your 6 and first-item spike, not to out-duel a fed kiting Lucian in the sidelane. Pivot to teamfights where your AoE R stun-locks his whole backline; never facecheck him in a straight 1v1 once he's online, and group so your global threat matters more than the lane he wants to scale in.","whys":["Both of you are fragile level 1 — his Q-W poke and double-shot passive out-range your single Q, so neither commits and it reads even.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit can land the three-mark stun if he steps up to trade, and his E dash is his only escape from it.","You own the wave and the trade here — a Q-W mark stun chunks his squishy body and he has to burn E to survive your chip.","You keep the poke edge while he respects your stun; he can't all-in a marked Kennen without eating the third-stack lock.","Slicing Maelstrom is my biggest spike — the stun-lock burns his low-HP body down, though every immobilise arms two Lightslinger shots.","Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a one-shot — he has no MR and his HP pool can't survive your magic burst.","He out-scales the duel — a 2-item Navori Lucian kites and double-shots your squishy body once your R is down, so close before he's online."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade or even a two-spell Mark stun on a Malphite who steps up to last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus your full Q-W-E stun-lock blows up a Malphite whose armor stacking does nothing against your all-magic burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes the R combo into a clean kill — his armor and W shield ignore none of your magic damage."},{"when":"Lvl 6 (his)","text":"His one real threat is R: an unstoppable Unstoppable Force engage that flash-blinks onto you and chains into jungle ganks, so respect his all-in range past 6."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke him with Thundering Shuriken (Q) freely — his armor stacking does nothing against your magic damage","Stack three Marks of the Storm with Q-W-E to stun and burst him before his W shield matters","Hold E (Lightning Rush) and Flash to dodge his R engage, then turn and all-in once it is on cooldown"],"foe":["Land Seismic Shard (Q) slows to chip you and close the gap on your squishy body","Let Granite Shield recharge between pokes and bait an extended trade he survives","Hit level 6 and flash-engage Unstoppable Force (R) onto you, ideally into a jungle gank"]},"early":"Free real estate early — Malphite stacks armor, and every point of it does nothing against your all-magic kit. Poke him down with Thundering Shuriken (Q) from max range and let Electrical Surge autos chip when he walks up to last-hit. At level 2-3, a Q into W-on-hit can land a two-spell Mark of the Storm trade or even tag the third stack for a stun if he oversteps. Just keep your fragile body out of Seismic Shard (Q) range so he can't slow-and-walk you down.","mid":"This is your lane to take. By levels 4-5 continuous Q chip keeps Granite Shield from ever recharging, so his effective HP never resets. At 6 you own the window outright: Q-W to pre-stack marks, E (Lightning Rush) in for the third-stack stun, then Slicing Maelstrom on a flat 120s for the kill — stacked armour does nothing to magic. Respect two things only: Ground Slam every 7 seconds, whose attack-speed cut delays your Surge marks, and a 130-second Unstoppable Force flash-engaged into a jungle gank.","late":"Your edge holds longer here than in most lanes because Malphite never out-scales you in a 1v1 — he's a tank who wants to teamfight, not duel. But once he has his R up on a short cooldown he becomes an engage threat on you anyway: he flash-Rs to lock you down for his team and you're a squishy caster with no R to answer if yours is down. Keep stun-locking him in fights with Slicing Maelstrom and pivot to teamfight engager — you're the better fight-starter, just don't get caught alone when his Unstoppable Force is up.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you have one Q poke and Surge autos but no stun and a fragile body, and his Seismic Shard slow can punish an overstep, so neither of you commits.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade or two-spell Mark stun, and his armor does nothing to stop the magic damage.","You own the wave against an immobile armor-stacker here — Q chips freely and his Ground Slam shield can't out-sustain your magic poke.","You keep the poke edge, but Ground Slam's attack-speed cut starves the Electrical Surge marks that feed your stun — poke, don't melee.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the full Q-W-E stun-lock all-in, and his W shield plus armor are worthless against your AoE magic burst — you win this duel outright.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes the R combo into a kill; armor reduces none of it, so this is your cleanest blow-up window on his tanky body.","He never out-duels you, but with R up he flash-engages Unstoppable Force to lock you down for his team — play with your team and don't get caught when his ult is off cooldown."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"maokai","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three Marks for a stun and chunk him while his only answer is a saplings-and-sustain shove."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks him through his W root attempt — your hardest all-in and a free 2v2 dive top."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into real burst — his armor stacking does nothing against your all-magic kit."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"His threat: a hidden Twisted Advance out of fog roots you for his jungler to collapse, and he is untargetable for the whole dash in."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack Mark of the Storm with Q poke and W on-hit to stun him before he ever lands W","Hit your level 6 and force the R + E-in all-in while he is still itemless and immobile","Build magic burst (Alternator/Rocketbelt) so his armor and sustain mean nothing and close before 25 min"],"foe":["Land Twisted Advance to root you and hold you there for his jungler to collapse","Stay healthy on passive sustain and saplings, shove with Q knockback, and stall to teamfights","Avoid your three-Mark stun window and trade only when your E and R are on cooldown"]},"early":"Maokai is immobile with no dash until W, so levels 1-3 are exactly your kind of lane — chip him with Thundering Shuriken and let Electrical Surge on-hit stack Marks. The one thing to respect is his W: it's a dash-root, so don't sit in a straight line at melee range where he can guarantee it. Bait the W or trade from range with Q, because his saplings and passive heal can't out-damage your poke, and once you reach a three-stack stun he has no mobility to escape the follow-up.","mid":"This is your lane to take over. Your Q cooldown drops toward 4 seconds, and stacking Mark of the Storm with Q-W stun-locks him while his armour stacking does nothing against your all-magic damage. At 6, Slicing Maelstrom plus an E-in blows up an itemless tank or wins a 2v2 dive top-side — but hold your burst until Twisted Advance is spent, because he is untargetable through the dash and everything aimed into it is wasted.","late":"You own the lane outright, but Maokai's whole job is to survive yours and become a teamfight tank — saplings, Sap Magic sustain, and a 525-range dash-root engage for his team. Cash your 6-and-first-item spike into a lead and a tower so his scaling never matters. Late, one hidden Twisted Advance out of fog pins you for a collapse, so start fights with your AoE R from range rather than diving him 1v1 once his peel is online.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your single Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip, but with no stun yet and a fragile body you don't commit into his sapling shove.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you build a three-Mark stun on an immobile tank who can only answer with saplings and sustain.","With Q-W up you out-poke him freely and his armor stacking is useless against your all-magic damage — last-hit and stack Marks.","You keep a clean poke edge; his W root is his only real trade, so bait it and chunk him while he has no mobility to disengage.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks an itemless Maokai — but Twisted Advance is untargetable, so burst after it, not into it.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into burst that ignores his armor entirely — force every all-in here.","He survives into a teamfight tank and a W engage for his team — close the game on your spikes and play R from range, never facecheck his root."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"mel","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three marks for the stun the moment she steps up to poke — punish her immobile body before she has W/E zoning."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in is your hardest all-in — she has no dash to leave with, and the storm is no projectile for Rebuttal to reflect."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your Q-W-E-R mark combo into a one-rotation kill on a squishy mage."},{"when":"Mel R window","text":"Her Rebuttal reflects your Q and R back at you — never throw a shuriken or channel maelstrom into the reflect; bait it first."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-shuriken pokes and stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun while her body is exposed","Bait Rebuttal's 38-second cooldown, then E-in and drop Slicing Maelstrom for the stun-lock all-in","Close the lane on your 6 and first-item spike before her execute zoning scales"],"foe":["Poke you down from max range with her Q so your low-HP body can't commit the E-in","Hold Rebuttal's 38 seconds to reflect a Thundering Shuriken back at you","Zone the wave with W/E and finish you with her execute once you're chipped"]},"early":"Two ranged AP mages, but you out-trade her up close — she has no dash, and once Solar Snare is spent nothing stops your walk-up. At level 1 trade Q for Q and respect her 950 range. From 2 onward, a second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit stacks three marks for a stun the moment she oversteps; punish her immobile body before her zoning is online. Two rules: never throw Q into Rebuttal, which reflects it back at your squishy frame, and never step in with her 11-second root up.","mid":"This is your takeover. You keep a poke edge through 4-5, then 6 is the kill window — bait her Rebuttal, then E-in and channel Slicing Maelstrom, stacking marks to stun-lock her with no dash to escape and no CC to break the channel. Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the full Q-W-E-R rotation into a one-combo kill on her squishy body. Force every all-in here on her R cooldown.","late":"You own the duel all game — she cannot survive your stun-lock once you reach her — but she scales into execute zoning and reflect peel for her team. Win lane on your 6/first-item spike so her range never matters, and in fights hold Thundering Shuriken until Rebuttal's 38 seconds are spent; Lightning Rush and the storm pass through it untouched. Never let Overwhelm stacks sit on you at low HP.","whys":["Two ranged mages trade Q for Q at level 1 — you have the stun upside but a fragile body, so don't commit yet.","Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit stacks three marks for a stun on an overstepping Mel before her zoning is online.","Full kit up — your Q poke plus mark-stun beats her immobile body, and she has no dash to escape the third proc.","You keep a poke edge through this stretch; chip with Q and respect her execute, trading only when her Rebuttal is down.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks a Mel with no dash — but Solar Snare roots from 1000 range, so bait it first.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your Q-W-E-R mark combo into a one-rotation kill on her squishy frame.","She scales into execute zoning and reflect peel — you still win the duel, but close the game before her range decides it."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Kennen","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Skill","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser","Mordekaiser"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1","text":"One Q poke plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips Morde before his W shield is online — the only window he can't heal it back."},{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"His Q (Obliterate) hits far harder on an isolated target and W (Indestructible) shields then heals; once E lands, every melee trade refills his bar."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His Realm of Death (R) drags you into an isolated 1v1, steals your stats, and his W heals through your burst — your stun-lock all-in is exactly what his ult counters."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Morde's Riftmaker/Rylai's turns the realm into a guaranteed kill, while your Liandry's/Rocketbelt combo can't out-DPS his shield + lifesteal in melee range."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q (Thundering Shuriken) pokes from max range and refuse to fight inside his E-pull line","Stack Mark of the Storm and W (Electrical Surge) for a stun ONLY when his W shield is on cooldown","Rush Oblivion Orb — Indestructible heals your chip back — and play roams over his 1v1"],"foe":["Land E (Death's Grasp) to drag you into auto range where his Q (Indestructible) does isolated bonus damage","Hold R (Realm of Death) for your level 6 all-in to steal your stats and win the isolation","Force extended melee trades so his W shield-heal and Riftmaker out-sustain your burst"]},"early":"Level 1 is your one clean window — chip him with a single Q (Thundering Shuriken) at max range and let Electrical Surge autos add up before Indestructible (W) exists to heal it back. Once he hits 2-3 his Q (Obliterate) gains its isolated bonus damage and Death's Grasp (E, 700 range, 16s at rank 1) pulls you straight into it, so never stand in the pull line for a CS. Poke from the edge of your 950, stack Mark of the Storm passively, and commit a stun only while his W is down — otherwise he shields it and walks you down.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a genuine coinflip: you still out-poke him with Q from range, but the second you get E-pulled into melee his W shield-heal eats your trade and his Q chunks you back. Keep the wave moving and farm with Q tip rather than dueling. At 6 do NOT trust your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock here — his Realm of Death (R) yanks you into a stat-stealing 1v1 where your squishy body and his sustain mean you lose the very all-in that wins you most lanes. Hold your own R for teamfights, not for his isolation.","late":"This is his window and you have to respect it. With Riftmaker or Rylai's his realm is a free kill on your low-HP caster, and once your R is on cooldown he runs you down with no answer. Don't sidelane against him — your value is roaming with global R threat and being the teamfight engager who peels and bursts squishies, not the duelist he drags into a box. Group, force 5v5s where his single-target ult is wasted, and let your AoE stun-lock matter where his isolation can't reach you.","whys":["Both of you are fragile at level 1, but your Q poke plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips him before his W shield can heal it — the one stage he can't sustain through.","At 2 his point-blank Q gains isolated bonus damage and his W shield-heal comes online, so any trade he pulls you into he wins back instantly.","His E-pull plus Q now does real isolated damage and his W refills through your poke — committing a stun here just feeds his sustain.","It's a true split: you out-poke from range with Q, but he out-trades the moment his E drags you into melee, so neither owns it.","His Realm of Death drags you into a stat-stealing 1v1 where his W heals through your stun-lock burst — the exact all-in your kit relies on is what his ult counters.","His Riftmaker/Rylai's turns the realm into a guaranteed kill while your first-item burst can't out-DPS his shield and lifesteal in melee.","Full-build Morde out-sustains and out-duels your squishy caster once your R is down — stop sidelaning and win through teamfight engage instead."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"nasus","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Nasus","Kennen","Nasus","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack three Marks of the Storm and stun him off a Q he tries to last-hit through."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into E-in stun-locks him before his Q stacks matter — your single best kill window and the one stage you truly own."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Wither is the problem item-for-item: 15s at rank 1, it cripples your move and attack speed mid-R and blunts the burst you rely on."},{"when":"Late","text":"A free-farmed Nasus with stacked Q, R lifesteal and size eats your squishy caster body — your R on cooldown means you lose the duel outright."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke at 950, outside Wither's 700, and step back on his Q wind-up — Siphoning Strike is an auto reset","Hit your level 6 and E-in Slicing Maelstrom all-in while he is still pre-Wither and low on Q stacks","Deny his Q last-hits early and end the lane before his stacks and R make him unkillable"],"foe":["Soak Q stacks safely under tower and only ever fight you with Wither up to kill your kite","Survive your level 6 R window, then W your move and attack speed to nothing in every trade","Free-farm to a stacked Q and Fury of the Sands, whose damage ignores the MR you stacked"]},"early":"Level 1 is a coinflip — one Q and your Electrical Surge autos chip, but his body is sturdier than yours and there is no stun yet, so just farm. Levels 2-3 are your real edge: with a second Q point and W on-hit you can stack three Marks of the Storm and pop the stun on an overstepping Nasus, then chunk him before he can do anything back. Do NOT walk into his auto range to throw that Q — last-hit at max Q distance, because his only answer here is to soak stacks, and the longer he free-farms the worse this gets.","mid":"Level 6 is the one window you own outright — E-in, R, and the full Q-W-E-Flash stun-lock will burst a pre-Wither Nasus who has no escape, so this is your kill timing, take it. But the moment he is also 6, Wither flips the math: it slows your move and attack speed mid-channel, so your Slicing Maelstrom stops kiting and his Q starts landing on you. After your R is down you are a squishy caster standing next to a juggernaut — disengage, do not greed a second trade into Wither.","late":"This is where the 42.77% lives — if Nasus free-farmed through your early windows he is now a stacked-Q, R-lifesteal monster and your short-cooldown caster pattern plateaus. You cannot duel him in the sidelane: Wither shuts off your kite, his E shreds your resists, and one Q with stacks deletes your HP bar while your R is on cooldown. Your only path is to have closed it on your 6/first-item spike — otherwise pivot to teamfights and AoE-peel for your carries, because the 1v1 belongs to him now.","whys":["Level 1 is even-to-weak for you — one Q poke and Surge autos chip, but with no stun and a fragile body neither of you commits.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack three Marks and stun him off any Q he steps up to last-hit.","You still own the poke trade here — chain the mark stun on an overstep and burst him before he can soak stacks safely.","Once he hits his stacks and you concede the hard-commit window, a pre-6 Kennen has to chip and respect rather than all-in into his sturdier body.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in stun-locks a pre-Wither Nasus with no escape — your single biggest spike and the one stage you flatly own.","Wither (700 range, 15s at rank 1) answers your first item: it slows move and attack speed mid-R, so his Q lands while your kite dies.","He out-scales hard — stacked Q, E shred and R lifesteal eat your squishy caster body the moment your R is on cooldown."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"nautilus","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Nautilus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade and chip his big HP bar before his Q hook range matters."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus your three-mark stun answers his all-in: bait Titan's Wrath (flat 12s) out first, then R him before E and his R knockup chain."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Liandry's turns your Q-W-R into real burst that punishes him hard for ever landing a hook on you."},{"when":"Late","text":"His Q hook plus point-blank R knockup is a guaranteed pick on your squishy body the moment he buys MR and your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke from max range and save Flash for his hook — you have no dash, and E is not one","Bait Titan's Wrath (12s) out, then hold R to punish his hook instead of eating Q-E-R","Build Liandry's/Alternator and dodge his Q hook so your magic burst out-damages his tankiness"],"foe":["Land Q (Dredge Line) to pull your fragile body in for the full E-AoE plus R knockup chain","Stack MR/armor and survive your R window, then run you down once it's on cooldown","Use his passive root on autos to lock you in melee where your squishy caster body loses"]},"early":"Nautilus has one engage button and it's Q (Dredge Line) — if it misses, the hook goes on a long cooldown and you get a free window to step up and poke. At level 2-3 your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you chip his huge HP bar without ever entering his auto range, where his passive (Staggering Blow) roots you. Last-hit at max Q range, never walk into hook range to throw a shuriken, and respect that even one landed Q pulls you into his whole E-AoE-into-melee plan.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect-the-hook stretch — you keep the poke edge, but if he Q-hooks you he can E-AoE and auto-root to lock you in melee where your fragile body loses. Level 6 flips it: with Slicing Maelstrom up, his hook engage actually feeds you — when he Q-pulls in, drop R and your three-mark stun-lock blows him up before his R knockup and E chain matter. Bait the hook, then E-in, W to ripple all your marks, and R the moment he commits.","late":"This is where the lane turns on him. Once Nautilus buys MR (Mercs/Force of Nature) and tanks up, he survives your R window, and his Q hook plus point-blank R knockup is a guaranteed pick on your squishy caster body the second your ult is down. You can't trade blow-for-blow with a fed tank, so don't sidelane into his hook — group, use your R as a teamfight engage/peel from the backline, and let your AoE burst matter in 5v5 rather than dueling him alone.","whys":["Dredge Line reaches 1150, further than your 950, but it is his only engage at 14s — last-hit behind minions, give no hook angle.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit out-pokes his single-target hook before his HP bar or root matter.","You chip his big health bar with ranged Q-W marks while he can only threaten if his Q hook lands.","He hits his level-3 hook-into-E-AoE combo and your squishy body loses if you get pulled into melee, so respect the engage here.","Slicing Maelstrom plus your three-mark stun-lock answers his hook all-in — drop R when he Q-pulls in and burst him before his R knockup chains.","Hextech Alternator/Liandry's turns your Q-W-R into real burst that punishes every hook he lands on you.","A fed tank with MR survives your R and his Q hook plus point-blank R knockup is a free pick on your squishy body — group and dont sidelane into his engage."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"neeko","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit chunks her every time she steps up to last-hit — Q (Blooming Burst) reaches 800 against your 950, so it cannot answer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a marked Neeko is lethal — your R stun-locks through her body before she can channel her own R (Pop Blossom)."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt turns your three-mark stun into a full kill on a Neeko caught with Tangle-Barbs down — 12s at rank 1."},{"when":"Lvl 6+","text":"Her threat window: a hidden Tangle-Barbs root (E) from a clone (W), then a self-buffed Pop Blossom — if it lands first you eat the full combo."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Q poke war — outrange her Blooming Burst and stack Mark of the Storm before she ever lands a root","Sidestep her Tangle-Barbs (E, 12s at rank 1), then E-in, third-mark stun and R burst before it returns","Spot the W clone — never throw your stun combo at a fake and never facecheck brush where her real body roots you"],"foe":["Land a long Tangle-Barbs (E) root to lock your fragile body for her full Pop Blossom burst","Use W clone to bait your Q/E commitment, then hit you with the real root from an angle you didn't expect","Survive to 6 and roam/scale — set up picks on you or your team with clone-disguised flanks"]},"early":"Your Thundering Shuriken (Q) out-ranges her Blooming Burst (Q), so win the poke war outright — chip her every wave and stack Mark of the Storm on her squishy body. The one thing that beats you is her Tangle-Barbs (E) root: never walk in a straight line at her, because a root on you is a free poke combo back. Watch for the W clone — if a \"Neeko\" is sitting oddly still it's a fake, so don't waste your E ball chasing it. At level 2-3 your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you trade through anything she throws.","mid":"This is your lane to take over. Keep stacking marks with Q and W-on-hit poke, and the moment she's chunked, E-in for the third-mark stun and burst — she has no escape and no sustain to answer it. At 6, Slicing Maelstrom is the killshot: a marked Neeko caught in your R is stun-locked before she can ever finish channeling Pop Blossom (R), so all-in her on cooldown. Just respect that her R is a hard-CC interrupt — if she lands her root and self-buffs first, her burst can blow you up too, so make sure you stun her before she commits.","late":"You both stay squishy, so this never becomes a duel problem the way a bruiser would — it becomes a pick game. Once teams group, the danger is a clone-disguised Neeko flanking from fog with a root into Pop Blossom, which one-shots you if you're caught alone. Trust your own R as the bigger teamfight tool — your AoE stun-lock peels her engage and your global threat lets you punish her splitpush. Hold flash for her root, keep vision so she can't W-flank you, and you out-impact her in every fight.","whys":["You both have fragile bodies and no stun yet — one Q poke each, so it reads even until your kit comes online.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-trades her short-range Blooming Burst every time she steps to CS.","Q-W mark pressure two-spell stuns an overstepping Neeko, but Tangle-Barbs roots from 1000 — further than your Q.","You keep the poke edge — chip her down and respect only her Tangle-Barbs root, sidestepping it to deny her combo.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks a marked Neeko through her body before she can ever channel Pop Blossom — you own the all-in.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your three-mark R combo into a clean kill while Tangle-Barbs is down.","You both stay squishy so it flattens to a pick game — her clone-flank root into Pop Blossom can one-shot you if you're caught alone."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Kennen","Skill","Olaf","Kennen","Skill","Olaf"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real poke trade and chip Olaf before his axe-stack lifesteal comes online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom is your one clean all-in window - the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock can burst Olaf before he has the HP and lifesteal to face-tank it."},{"when":"Olaf R","text":"Ragnarok makes him CC-immune, so your Mark of the Storm chain does nothing while Reckless Swing's true damage runs you down - never fight into his ult."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Olaf has lifesteal and bruiser HP he out-sustains your magic poke, ignores your stun under R, and deletes your squishy body the moment your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes from max range and stack Mark of the Storm to stun before Olaf can axe-stack onto you","Hit your Level 6 and force the Q-W-E-Flash-R all-in BEFORE his lifesteal and HP scale","Rush your AP item for the one window your burst beats his bulk — MR does nothing to Reckless Swing"],"foe":["Land his axe (Q) for the slow, then walk you down and stack the move speed/attack speed buff","Build lifesteal and bruiser HP so he out-sustains your poke and tanks your stun combo","Save Ragnarok (R) for your all-in so he is CC-immune through your entire mark stun chain"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash - one Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip him, but your body is fragile, so don't commit. Your real early window is Level 2-3: a second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack marks for a stun trade and chip him before his lifesteal ramps. Dodge Undertow (Q, 1000 range, 9s) - if it misses he has no slow and cannot stick to you, and remember that walking over the thrown axe resets that cooldown for free. Never let him land the slow and walk onto your low-HP body.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his to grab - he hits his level-3 combo and out-sustains your poke through lifesteal, so this is a chip-and-respect stretch where you give ground if he commits. Then Level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock, and that is your single best window to blow him up before his HP and lifesteal make him unkillable. The catch is Ragnarok - if his R is up, he is CC-immune and your entire mark stun does nothing, so bait or wait out his ult, THEN all-in. Force your kill on the 6 spike or you lose the lane.","late":"This is where you lose. Once Olaf has lifesteal and bruiser HP your magic poke heals off instantly, he face-tanks your combo, and Reckless Swing's true damage ignores the MR you bought while Ragnarok makes him immune to your stun chain - your one win condition is dead. As a squishy short-cooldown caster you get deleted the moment your R is on cooldown. Don't sidelane the 1v1 - you can't win it. Close on your 6/first-item spike, then group and use your AoE R as a teamfight engager where Olaf catches one person, not your team.","whys":["Level 1 is even-to-weak for you - one Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip, but with no stun and a fragile body you don't commit while he axe-stacks.","Your cleanest early window: a second Q point plus W on-hit lands a real poke trade or a two-spell mark stun before his lifesteal scales.","It evens out - he can answer with his level-3 axe combo and lifesteal sustain, so you chip and respect rather than commit.","Olaf grabs this stretch - he hits his combo, out-sustains your poke through lifesteal, and walks you down once the axe slow lands.","Your biggest spike: Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that can burst him before his HP and lifesteal make him untouchable.","It's a coin-flip on his Ragnarok timer - your AP item cashes the R combo into a kill, but if his R is up the stun does nothing.","He out-scales you hard: lifesteal and bruiser HP face-tank your poke, Ragnarok ignores your stun and shields, and you melt when your R is down."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"ornn","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Ornn","Kennen","Skill","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three marks and stun Ornn before his Brittle combo is online — your cleanest poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-locks him for an all-in, but bait his W (Bellows Breath) CC-immunity and E knockup first or the channel gets cancelled."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into real kill pressure before his tank resists stack up."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ornn's self-forged MR plus R double-knockup interrupting your channel flips the duel — his Brittle empowers his whole team and you bounce off."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun with Q-W before he can land his E pillar knockup","Punish his 800 range with Q poke and Electrical Surge autos while he farms with his Q","Hit your level 6 / first-item spike and convert it into a kill before his MR comes online"],"foe":["Activate W (Bellows Breath) for CC-immunity and a shield to walk through your stun chain","Land E (Searing Charge) pillar knockup or R to cancel your R channel and E-in","Stack tank MR and Brittle so your all-magic burst bounces off and you fall off"]},"early":"Ornn is short-range and has no sustain, so abuse it: chip with Q (Thundering Shuriken) and let Electrical Surge autos add up while he last-hits with Volcanic Rupture (Q, 800 range, 9s). At levels 2-3 a Q plus W-on-hit can stack three marks and stun him before his Brittle setup exists — that is your cleanest punish. The catch: he can pop W (Bellows Breath) to become CC-immune and shielded, so bait that bubble before you commit your mark chain, and respect that he is tankier than the squishies you usually bully.","mid":"Levels 4-5 he hits his level-3 power and his E (Searing Charge) into a pillar gives him a knockup that cancels your E-in and the start of your R, so respect his all-in window and chip from range. At 6 you reclaim the lane: Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-locks him for your hardest all-in, but you must bait his Bellows Breath CC-immunity first or the stun does nothing, and dodge his E pillar that would interrupt your channel. Your first item (Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt) is your peak — force the all-in here.","late":"This is where Ornn takes over and why the lane reads TRICKY. He self-forges Mercury's-style MR and tank items without backing, so your all-magic burst bounces off, and his R (Call of the Forge God) double-knockup plus Brittle interrupts your R channel and empowers his whole team to blow you up once your storm is down. Close it on your 6/first-item spike — pivot to teamfight engager and peel, because in a straight late-game duel his resists and CC outlast your short-cooldown caster body.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 — you have one Q poke and no stun, he has no Brittle setup yet, so it's a Skill last-hitting stretch.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit can stack three marks and stun a short-range Ornn before his combo exists.","You own the wave and out-poke him with Q while Electrical Surge chips, and he can't sustain it back.","Searing Charge into his own pillar knocks you up and cancels your channel, and at 14s he holds it for every commit you make.","Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-locks him for an all-in once you bait Bellows Breath — your biggest spike beats his pre-item body.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt burst still chunks him before his MR stacks, but his natural tankiness keeps it from being a clean kill, so it's even.","He self-forges MR and uses R's double-knockup plus Brittle to interrupt your channel and outlast your magic — he owns the late."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"pantheon","win":["Skill","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Pantheon's W point-click stun into Q empower is his hardest window — never get caught at melee range before you have your escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your Q-W-E-R stun-lock all-in that out-bursts a squishy Pantheon and ignores his armor."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt turns the R combo lethal — this is your peak, blow him up before he can W-stun and disengage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Pantheon's tankier item build can't trade with your magic burst, but his R global means you must group — own this if you closed on your spike."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive his level 1-3 W-stun window with safe Q farming from max range","Reach 6 and stun him out of Aegis Assault — the third mark cancels his channel","Snowball your first-item magic spike since his armor does nothing vs your kit"],"foe":["W point-click stun you the instant you step into melee, then Q-empower burst","Win the levels 1-3 trades before your R and items come online","Hide behind Aegis Assault to blank your burst, then all-in on a missed Q"]},"early":"Pantheon owns the first three levels and you have to respect it. Shield Vault (W) is a point-click stun dash at 600 range — there is no skillshot to dodge — so the second you step up to auto or chase a mark, he stuns and bursts you with an empowered Q. Farm with the tip of your Q (Thundering Shuriken) and let Electrical Surge autos chip only in his 13s W window. Aegis Assault (E) makes him invulnerable from the front, so never feed autos into the shield — lead with Q. Eat a little poke; you don't have the stun chain or the body to fight him yet.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even — keep landing Q pokes and stacking marks from range while you wait for your spike. At 6 the lane flips hard: Slicing Maelstrom plus your Mark of the Storm chain means you can E-in (or Flash), drop R, and stun-lock him while your AoE storm and magic burst delete a squishy Pantheon who has no MR and an armor-heavy early build that does nothing against you. Bait Shield Vault (13s) and Aegis Assault (22s at rank 1), then commit everything. This is the window to turn his early lead around.","late":"You out-scale him cleanly — Pantheon falls off into items while your first-item magic spike (Hextech Alternator, Rocketbelt or Liandry's) makes your R combo blow up his squishy frame. He can't itemize armor out of your all-magic kit, and he has no sustain to survive your stun-lock. The catch is his R global: he roams and teamfights, so don't tunnel on sidelane and let him impact the map. Group with your R as the AoE engage and you win every fight where you land the stun chain.","whys":["Both of you are fragile level 1, but his point-click W stun makes any melee step lethal — last-hit with Q from range and don't commit.","He hits his level 2 W-stun-into-Q-empower power spike before your mark chain exists — respect melee range hard.","Level 3 he has his full combo and you still have no stun-lock; farm with Q and his passive blocks your auto pressure.","Levels 4-5 even out as your Q poke chips him down from range while he can't safely all-in a kiting Kennen.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your Q-W-E-R stun-lock — you out-burst a squishy, no-MR Pantheon and his armor build is wasted vs magic.","Your Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt first item cashes the R combo into a kill — this is your peak and his armor does nothing.","He falls off into items while your magic burst scales — out-trade him, just respect his R global so he can't roam free."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"poppy","win":["Skill","Skill","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade from range — her W dash-block is dead weight against a champ who never dashes in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your stun-lock, and a mark landing mid-Keeper's Verdict cancels the channel — her R never leaves the ground."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Liandry's cashes the R combo into burst that chunks her through armor — magic damage ignores the tank items she just bought."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Poppy stacks MR (Mercs/Force of Nature) and tank HP, she eats your stun window, E-pins you to terrain, and your squishy body falls off the duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q from max range and stack Mark of the Storm — her immobile body cannot dodge or close on it","Fight in open lane away from walls so her E has no terrain to pin you against and stun-combo you","Hit your level 6 and burst her on the Q-W-E-R stun-lock before she buys MR"],"foe":["Wait for you to step up, then Heroic Charge you into a wall for a free stun and a Hammer Shock all-in","Buy Mercury's Treads and Force of Nature so your all-magic kit barely scratches her","Stack tank HP and resists to survive your level-6 R window, then ult (R) to peel and disengage"]},"early":"Poppy's W (Steadfast Presence) is wasted against you — Lightning Rush is not a dash for it to stop, so sit at Q range and chip. Her real threat is Heroic Charge (E, 475 range, 14s at rank 1): hug a wall and she pins you against it for a stun into a Hammer Shock slow zone, so fight in the open lane where that E only shoves you back. Don't spend Lightning Rush chasing her; you want it up for her engage.","mid":"This stretch is a poke war you win on the scoreboard but not the all-in. Keep stacking marks with Q and Electrical Surge autos, but respect Heroic Charge — a wall pin flips the fight, since she chains the stun into a Hammer Shock zone and out-trades your fragile body. At 6 Slicing Maelstrom is the spike: with her E down, your stun-lock lands first, and a mark mid-Keeper's Verdict cancels her channel outright.","late":"This is where she takes over if the game drags. Poppy buys Mercury's Treads and Force of Nature, stacks tank HP, and suddenly your all-magic kit barely dents her — she survives your R window, E-pins you to the nearest wall, and her ult (R) knocks you out of position. You can't out-duel a resisted tank as a squishy caster. Pivot to teamfights: use R to peel and chain-stun her dive, but don't sidelane-duel her past two items.","whys":["One Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip her, but with no stun yet and a fragile body you don't commit — she just walks the wave, so it reads even.","Her W dash-block is useless against you, but you only have one point in Q and no real burst, so neither side wins the trade outright yet.","A second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade her immobile body can't dodge, and she has no way to close the gap on you.","You keep the poke edge, but near a wall her Heroic Charge (14s) pins and stuns you into a Hammer Shock zone, so respect and chip.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that bursts her before she can E-pin you — your single biggest window.","Hextech Alternator/Liandry's cashes the R combo into burst that chunks her through armor, since your magic damage ignores the tank items she rushed.","Once she stacks MR (Mercs/Force of Nature) and tank HP she eats your stun window, E-pins you to terrain, and your squishy caster body loses the extended duel."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"quinn","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Quinn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack two marks and stun her if she steps up to last-hit in melee range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom + Lightning Rush is your hardest all-in — E onto her, R stun-locks through her E vault, and she can't kite a channel that follows her."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your full mark-stun combo into a one-rotation kill on her squishy ranged body."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items she reclaims the lane — Harrier nimble auto-resets and E knockback let her perma-kite you the moment your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q from max range to chip and bank a Mark of the Storm before you ever commit","Catch her with E-into-R at 6 so the storm keeps ticking after Vault peels her off","Snowball your level 6 / first-item burst window before her Harrier kite and roams take over"],"foe":["Vault away the instant you E-in, then blind your autos with Blinding Assault (Q, 1025)","Kite back with Harrier nimble move speed and poke your low-HP body before you stack three marks","Survive lane and roam — turn her sidelane and mid pressure into a lead your R can't answer"]},"early":"Vault (E, 12s at rank 1) is the whole problem — it knocks her clear and interrupts you right when you E-in to start a mark chain, so don't burn Lightning Rush unless it is down. Her Q blinds and reaches 1025 to your 950, so trade when it is spent, not on cooldown. One Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge autos still out-trades her Harrier poke. At 2-3 punish her: if she steps up to last-hit, a Q plus W stacks two marks and the stun threat alone forces her off the wave.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — she has the range and the move speed to dance around you while her E resets the trade, so keep banking Q poke instead of committing without your stun set up. Level 6 flips it: Slicing Maelstrom is a channel that keeps striking her as she moves, so E-in, R, and stack your three marks for the stun before her E vault can peel you off. If she Flashes or vaults the engage, R still tags her in the AoE — bait the E first, then all-in.","late":"This is where you lose if the game drags. Past two items Quinn is a full ranged carry with Harrier auto-resets and E knockback, and once your R is on cooldown she perma-kites your squishy body and never lets you close the gap. You have to cash your 6 / first-item spike into a lead and a tempo advantage, then pivot to teamfight engager and roam — do NOT try to out-duel her in a side lane late, because her kite and your fragile HP pool mean she wins that 1v1 every time her vault is up.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 — your single Q poke and her Harrier autos roughly trade, so neither commits without a mark stun or her E up.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge lets you two-mark and threaten a stun if she steps into melee to CS.","With Q-W online your poke and stun threat own the wave; she has to give up farm or eat a mark chain.","She has the range and move speed to kite trades with Harrier and reset with E, so without your stun set up you respect and chip.","Slicing Maelstrom is your spike — E-in and R stun-lock her through the vault and blind, winning any pre-item 2v2 or duel.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill her squishy ranged body can't survive — your peak window.","She out-scales as a ranged carry: Harrier kite and E knockback perma-shred you once your R is down, so close before two items."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"renekton","win":["Renekton","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Renekton's biggest window: empowered W (Ruthless Predator) point-click stuns you and his Cull the Meek heals through your chip, so never sit in his dash range early."},{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"With Q maxed and W on-hit you out-range his all-in: Thundering Shuriken pokes free and a third Mark of the Storm stuns him as he tries to E-W onto you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your hardest spike: Q-W-E-Flash into Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him before fury and his W-stun can answer, blowing up a squishy pre-armor Renekton."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill, exactly as Renekton's two-dash point-click pattern starts falling off into items."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Thundering Shuriken and stack Mark of the Storm so a third proc stuns him the instant he dashes in","Reach level 6 and burn Slicing Maelstrom with Flash to stun-lock him before his fury W can answer","Trade only in his W window (16s at rank 1), and buy Oblivion Orb early — Cull the Meek heals your chip back"],"foe":["Land a fury-empowered W stun into Slice and Dice while you have no mark stun banked","Use his two E dashes to close your poke range and all-in your squishy body before level 6","Snowball the level 1-5 window and end before your R + first item spike takes over the lane"]},"early":"Renekton owns the very first levels — his empowered W (Ruthless Predator) is a point-click stun and Cull the Meek heals through your Q chip, so do not sit in dash range trying to win a level-1 fight you lose. Farm with the tip of Thundering Shuriken and start banking Mark of the Storm stacks from range. By level 3, with Q maxed and Electrical Surge on-hit, the math flips: you out-range him, and if he E-dashes in for his combo a third mark stuns him before his fury W ever lands.","mid":"This stretch is yours. Chip him down with Q from outside his dash range and only let him close when his empowered W is on cooldown — then weave an auto mark and stun him on the third proc. At 6 your Slicing Maelstrom flips every all-in: Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-locks a pre-armor Renekton and your AoE magic burst ignores the little armor he has. Bait the W stun, sidestep his E-dashes, and commit R the moment his fury combo is spent.","late":"You stay ahead — Renekton is a falloff bully, not a scaler, so once you survive his level 1-6 window your magic burst and teamfight R only grow relative to him. Cash your first-item spike (Alternator/Rocketbelt or Liandry's) into a kill and pivot to fights, where your AoE stun-lock peels and dives far harder than his single-target dash. Just respect that if he snowballs the early game his point-click combo can still one-shot your squishy body, so close the lane before he forces a Mercs-and-armor sidelane stalemate.","whys":["Renekton's empowered W (Ruthless Predator) point-click stuns you and Cull the Meek out-heals your Q chip, so the level-1 melee window is genuinely his.","His W is an auto reset, so the wind-up is the tell — a second Q point plus an auto mark answers a dash-in, and it stays a coin flip.","Q maxed with Electrical Surge on-hit out-ranges his all-in, and a third Mark of the Storm stuns him the instant he E-dashes onto you.","You hold the poke edge and trade strictly around his W cooldown, kiting his dashes with Lightning Rush before Cull the Meek heals the trade back.","Slicing Maelstrom plus Q-W-E-Flash stun-locks a pre-armor Renekton, and your all-magic burst ignores his low early armor.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill exactly as his two-dash point-click pattern starts falling off into items.","He is a falloff bully with no scaling, so your magic burst and teamfight R keep growing relative to him as long as you closed his early window."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"riven","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Riven","Kennen","Kennen","Riven"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk her every time she walks up to last-hit, before her 3-Q combo is online."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks her mid-combo: bait her Q3 knockup and E or Flash-R the instant she commits, and the storm chains marks through her shield."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill that her E shield cannot fully eat through your magic burst."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Blade of the Exile falls to 60s at rank 3 against your flat 120 — with bruiser items she gets two ult windows for every one of yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and Electrical Surge autos every time she steps to CS so she is low before she can ever commit her combo","Hold Lightning Rush as a stun-finisher and disengage, not an opener, so you can E out the moment she Q3-knockups","Bait her E shield and W stun with a fake step, then Q-W-E-R stun-lock her on her own cooldowns and close before 2 items"],"foe":["Wait out your three Mark of the Storm stacks, then Q1-Q2 in, W stun, and Q3 knockup before you can react","Use Valor (E, 10s) to block your Q poke and dash clear of the storm before it stacks marks","Sidestep your skillshot Q to deny stacks, then scale to bruiser items and reset on your low-HP body"]},"early":"Riven is a melee with no ranged answer to your Q, so this is free chip — throw Thundering Shuriken every time she walks up to last-hit and let Electrical Surge autos add up. The danger is her gap-close: do NOT burn Lightning Rush chasing a poke, because her three Q dashes plus W stun will catch you the moment your E is down. Keep her at Q range, build Mark of the Storm passively, and she is the one bleeding HP before level 3.","mid":"Level 6 is your window. Riven wants to all-in with Q1-Q2 in, W stun, Q3 knockup, E shield — so bait that commitment, then the instant she sticks to you Flash or E-R her: Slicing Maelstrom chains Mark of the Storm through her shield and stun-locks her out of her own combo. Pre-6 (levels 4-5) respect her — her full combo can delete you if you have no E up, so chip and back off. Once Hextech Alternator lands, your R combo blows through her E shield and she dies in the storm.","late":"This is where Riven flips the lane. Once she has bruiser items and your R is on cooldown, her three-dash Q stun and combo reset out-duel your squishy caster body — you cannot win a straight sidelane 1v1 against a fed Riven. So you must have closed the game on your 6-and-first-item spike. Stop trying to duel her and become the teamfight engager: hold R for her dive, peel with your stun chain, and let your AoE win the fight your single-target duel cannot.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — your single Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip her, but with one ability and a fragile body neither commits, so it reads even.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade before her 3-Q combo exists, and she has to walk into your range to farm.","You out-poke a melee Riven who still cannot reach you without burning all three Q dashes, so you own the wave and her HP bar.","Her level-3 combo lands here: Broken Wings (13s) into Ki Burst stuns and trades back hard if your E is down, so chip and respect.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks her mid-combo: bait the Q3 knockup, then E or Flash-R and the storm chains marks through her E shield.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt spike cashes the R combo into a kill her shield cannot fully absorb — force every all-in on this window.","She out-scales the duel: a bruiser-item Riven sidesteps your Q, eats your R cooldown, and resets her combo on your low-HP body — pivot to teamfights."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"rumble","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Rumble"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you win the ranged poke war before his Flamespitter ever reaches you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a Mark of the Storm stun-lock blows him up before he can stack Danger Zone heat and turn on the all-in."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your Q-W-E-R combo into a kill while he is still a pre-Liandry's bruiser."},{"when":"Late","text":"Rumble's Equalizer ultimate zones you off objectives and his overheated Flamespitter out-DPSes you in any extended fight once your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the Q poke war from max range so his Flamespitter and harpoon never connect","Hit Level 6 and chain three Marks of the Storm into an R stun-lock before he reaches Danger Zone heat","Close the game on your 6 and first-item burst before his Equalizer zoning takes over fights"],"foe":["Land both harpoons to shred your MR and hold you in a 3-second Flamespitter cone","Manage his heat bar to enter Danger Zone and overheat-empower his Flamespitter on the trade","Scale to Liandry's plus Equalizer and zone you off every objective fight"]},"early":"Rumble has no ranged answer to your Q at level 1, but neither of you wants to commit yet, so chip with Thundering Shuriken from max range and let Electrical Surge autos add free poke. The whole early game is keeping his Flamespitter cone off you — never walk into the short range where his harpoon (E) can slow you into the flame. By level 2-3 your second Q point plus W on-hit wins the poke war outright, because his only retaliation is a flame cone you can simply stand outside of.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — if he hits Danger Zone heat his Flamespitter out-DPSes you in melee, so don't let an E-harpoon stick you in the cone. Bait his W (Scrap Shield) move-speed, then strike. At 6 you take over: stack three Marks of the Storm, then E-in or Flash-R Slicing Maelstrom to stun-lock and burst him before he can overheat or drop Equalizer on himself to escape.","late":"This is where Rumble reclaims the matchup as a scaling AP bruiser. His Equalizer ultimate is a long zoning wall that walls you off objectives and chunks your squishy body, and with Liandry's plus an overheated Flamespitter he out-sustains and out-DPSes you the moment your R is on cooldown. Win the lane on your 6 and first-item spike and pivot to teamfight engage — never sit in a sidelane duel against his flame and zone.","whys":["Neither of you commits at level 1 — chip with Q from range, but his Flamespitter has no answer to you yet so the lane is even.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit wins the ranged trade his short Flamespitter cone cannot contest.","You own the poke war here — keep landing Q from outside flame range and he cannot retaliate without walking into your marks.","Danger Zone heat plus two harpoons that slow and shred your MR can stick you in the cone, so respect it and only poke.","Slicing Maelstrom into a triple Mark stun-lock blows him up before he stacks heat or escapes with Equalizer.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your R combo into a kill while he is still a pre-Liandry's bruiser.","The Equalizer falls to 80s against your flat 120, so he zones every objective while Flamespitter out-DPSes your body."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"ryze","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Ryze"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you out-poke a Ryze who has to walk up to last-hit melee-range minions."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Q-W-E-Flash into Slicing Maelstrom chains three Mark of the Storm stacks and stuns him inside Rune Prison's 615 root range."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill before Ryze finishes his second mana item."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Once Ryze stacks mana his Spell Flux into Rune Prison root chain out-DPSes your squishy body when R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip with Thundering Shuriken (Q) and Electrical Surge autos every time he walks up to CS","Hit level 6 and land the full Q-W-E-Flash-R three-mark stun-lock before he buys MR","Close the game on your 6 and first-item spike before his mana-item scaling takes over"],"foe":["Farm safely at range and never eat a third Mark of the Storm stun stack","Land Spell Flux into Rune Prison to root and chunk your low-HP body","Reach two mana items where his Spell Flux root chain out-trades your R"]},"early":"Ryze has to walk up to melee-range minions to last-hit early, and that is exactly where your Thundering Shuriken (Q) plus Electrical Surge auto on-hit punish him. Throw Q on its 7s cooldown and weave an empowered auto to stack Mark of the Storm, but do not facecheck a forward Ryze who can land Spell Flux (E) and then root you with Rune Prison (W). At levels 2-3 a clean Q plus W-into-auto builds to a third-stack stun on an overstepping Ryze, and Overload alone does not save him from what follows.","mid":"From level 4 you keep the poke edge, but his Spell Flux into Rune Prison roots you for a full burst rotation, so trade only while that 10-second W is down. Level 6 is your takeover: Q-W to pre-stack two marks, E (Lightning Rush) or Flash onto him, then channel Slicing Maelstrom to slap a third stack and stun him before the root lands. He cannot out-trade that combo, so force the all-in the moment you hit 6 and have your first AP component.","late":"This is where Ryze flips the lane. With two mana items every spell resets Overload's flat 5s cooldown, so Spell Flux into Rune Prison chains roots and bursts your squishy caster body the instant Slicing Maelstrom's 120s starts. Your job is to have already won: snowball the lane on your 6 and first-item windows, take plates and roam, and pivot to a teamfight engager. Do not 1v1 a six-item Ryze in the side lane, peel and AoE stun-lock for your team instead.","whys":["Both of you are weak level-1 squishy casters with one ability each, so it is a poke trade decided by who steps wrong rather than a real lead.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-pokes a Ryze forced into melee CS range before he can spam root resets.","A pre-stacked Q-W into auto chains a third Mark of the Storm stun, and with Overload his only answer he eats the whole follow-up.","You hold the poke edge while Rune Prison (W) sits on its 10-second cooldown, so you control the wave and chip him with free Q.","Slicing Maelstrom plus Q-W-E-Flash three-stacks Mark of the Storm and stuns him before Rune Prison's 615 range can root you.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your R combo into a kill before Ryze completes his second mana item.","With two mana items his Spell Flux into Rune Prison root out-DPSes your squishy body the moment your R is down, so he takes over."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"sejuani","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Sejuani","Kennen","Skill","Sejuani"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk her before she has Frost Armor and W stacks — your cleanest poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a marked Sejuani is a guaranteed stun-lock all-in — your one window where her tankiness can't save her."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes the R combo into real burst, but Liandry's is also doing the work because she stacks raw HP."},{"when":"Late","text":"Her R (Glacial Prison) flies 1300 units, hard-CCs you out of your own R channel, and Winter's Wrath into Permafrost pins you for her whole team."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q + Electrical Surge pokes early before Frost Armor and W stacks come online","Hit level 6 and bait Arctic Assault (Q, 18s) before committing your R stun-lock","Close the game on your 6 / first-item spike — sidelane and dive squishies, never duel her late"],"foe":["Stack Frost with Winter's Wrath (W), then land the Permafrost (E) stun on your fragile body","Stack raw HP and resistances so her chip and chain CC outlast you in extended fights","Survive to teamfights and land R (Glacial Prison) across the map to cancel your R channel"]},"early":"Sejuani has almost no early kill threat on you — her damage is chip and CC, not burst, so the level 1-3 window is yours to poke. Throw Q (Thundering Shuriken) at her every time she steps to last-hit and let Electrical Surge on-hits add up; her one gap-closer is Arctic Assault (Q), 650 range on 18s, and Frost Armor's MR breaks the moment you damage her. The one thing to respect is Winter's Wrath stacking Frost on you — at max stacks Permafrost stuns, and that is how she chunks your retreat.","mid":"Level 4-5 she gets sticky: Winter's Wrath slows on a 9s cooldown and fills Frost stacks until Permafrost stuns you, so a tank who can actually walk you down starts flipping short trades — poke from 950 instead of dueling. Level 6 is your reset button: a clean Slicing Maelstrom into a triple-marked Sejuani stun-locks even a tank, so bait out Arctic Assault (Q, 18s), then E-in and R for your one window where her armor and HP don't matter. Her charge stops on the first champion it hits, so it never carries her past you into a second target.","late":"This is where Sejuani takes the lane back hard. She builds full tank, Winter's Wrath into a Permafrost stun pins your squishy body for her team, and her R (Glacial Prison) is a 1300-range hard CC that cancels your Slicing Maelstrom channel the instant you commit. You cannot 1v1 her once she has two items, and in fights she peels you off her carries with the E stun and ults you out of your own R. Win this on your 6 and first-item spike, then pivot to a teamfight engager — never sidelane into her.","whys":["She has no early burst and Arctic Assault costs 60 mana on an 18s cooldown, but your fragile level-1 body means you get one Q poke in — set the lane up.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hits out-chip a Sejuani with no sustain, and chip poke keeps Frost Armor's MR broken.","You own the wave and the poke trade here — she can only soak Q damage and stack W slowly with no way to punish you back.","Winter's Wrath slows and stacks Frost until Permafrost stuns, letting a tank finally walk you down, so concede the step-in window.","Slicing Maelstrom into a triple-marked Sejuani stun-locks even a tank — bait Arctic Assault (Q), then R for a kill her armor can't stop.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes your R combo into burst, but it's a coin-flip window since she's stacking raw HP your magic struggles to finish.","She out-scales you outright — Winter's Wrath into a Permafrost stun pins you and Glacial Prison hard-CCs you out of your own channel, so don't duel her late."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"sett","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Sett","Skill","Sett","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-2","text":"Your Q poke plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips Sett free before he has Haymaker charged or a grit lead."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Sett's biggest threat window: he E-grabs you, lands a full-charge W true-damage smash, and your squishy body folds."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom stacks marks fast, but The Show Stopper hurls you clear of your own 550 storm, so it reads even."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His grit-bruiser items (Bami/Heartsteel) out-sustain your Hextech burst once he survives the stun window."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip with Thundering Shuriken and Electrical Surge autos before he charges Haymaker","Build three Mark of the Storm stacks to stun him while his E grab is on cooldown","Stay out of E-grab range so he can never connect his W true-damage smash"],"foe":["Land Knuckle Down into E grab-stun to lock you for a full Haymaker","Bait your E-in, then Show Stopper you clear of your own storm","Soak your poke with grit and out-sustain you into bruiser items"]},"early":"Sett has no dash and no early waveclear, so your Thundering Shuriken plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips him for free at levels 1-2 — last-hit at 950 and refuse to walk inside Facebreaker's 490. Every point of poke he eats is stored as Grit for Haymaker's shield, so trade in bursts and step out before the bar fills. Never let a minion sit on his far side: enemies on both sides of him turn the pull from a slow into a stun.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window, not yours: Facebreaker into a full-Grit Haymaker smash kills a fragile body a bruiser would survive. Keep building Mark of the Storm from range and commit the third-stack stun only while that 16s E is down. At 6 it's a coin flip — your R stacks marks and stun-locks, but The Show Stopper carries you 400 units clear of your own storm, so don't burn ult while his grab-and-slam is up. Hold it for the fight after.","late":"This stays a true even matchup. Your magic damage ignores his armor and your R is elite peel and AoE in 2v2s and teamfights, which is your real lategame value here. But Sett's grit scaling and bruiser items let him eat your poke and survive the stun window, so you will not solo-kill a fed Sett in the sidelane. Pivot to a teamfight engager: hold R for his dive, mark-and-stun him off your carries, and let your burst matter in the group fight rather than chasing a 1v1 you can't reliably close.","whys":["Sett has no dash and no early waveclear, so your Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip him for free before Haymaker is charged.","A second Q point plus W on-hit lets you build a real mark trade he can't answer without stepping into your poke for the E grab.","Once Facebreaker is online it's a knife-edge: alone you are only slowed, but with a minion on his far side the pull stuns — trade at range.","Sett owns this window — Facebreaker's 490 pull into a full-Grit Haymaker deletes your squishy body if you ever step into that range.","Your Maelstrom stacks marks and stun-locks, but The Show Stopper carries you clear of your own 550 storm, so 6 reads even.","Sett reclaims this — his Bami/Heartsteel grit out-sustains your Hextech Alternator burst once he survives the stun window.","It stays even: he can't catch you for free and you can't solo-kill his grit-scaled body, so your R becomes teamfight value instead of a 1v1 win."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"shen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Skill","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real Shuriken poke trade while Shen has no Shadow Dash yet to punish you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into the Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks Shen before he can taunt you off it — your cleanest kill window all game."},{"when":"Shen R","text":"Stand United (R) shields and teleports an ally across the map, but it is a channel — a third Mark of the Storm stun cancels it outright."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Liandry's turns your stun-lock into a real kill; Spirit's Refuge (W) blocks basic attacks only, so keep marking him with Q."}],"wants":{"you":["Shuriken (Q) poke him whenever Shadow Dash (E) is on cooldown so he eats chip he cannot taunt back","Bait his Spirit's Refuge (W) bubble, then chain three Mark of the Storm procs into the level-6 R stun-lock","Track his global Stand United (R) so you never overextend into a free top-side dive"],"foe":["Land Shadow Dash (E) taunt to drag you into his team while your R burns down","Time Spirit's Refuge (W) to block your auto marks and deny the third-stack stun","Survive even and use Stand United (R) to win every cross-map skirmish instead of the 1v1"]},"early":"Shadow Dash is an 18-second cooldown at rank 1 and Twilight Assault costs 140 mana, so levels 1-3 are your cleanest window — Thundering Shuriken (Q) his last-hits and let Electrical Surge autos chip him while his mana is thin. Once E is up, every trade is about its cooldown: poke freely when it's down, give nothing when it's up because a taunt drags you into everything. Spirit's Refuge (W) blocks basic attacks only, so inside it keep stacking marks with Q rather than walking in.","mid":"Level 6 is your spike and the one window you clearly own: Q-W to stack marks, E in (or Flash), and Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him before he can Shadow Dash off it. Shen trades evenly the rest of mid-game — he's tanky, he sustains, and his taunt flips any extended fight, so don't autopilot all-ins while that 18s E is up. The real danger isn't the 1v1; it's Stand United (R) shipping him across the map on a 200s cooldown, so a dive onto a Shen who already R'd out is wasted.","late":"This goes even because Shen scales into exactly what you don't — a global, peel-tank teamfighter who is tankier than your magic burst can kill once he has items and MR. Your squishy short-cooldown caster body wants the pick before he reaches the fight, so play engager off your R and force fights while Stand United's 200s cooldown is running. Better still, if he starts the channel across the map, land your third mark and cancel it. If you can't kill him, chunk his carries through the taunt window instead.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — your one Q poke chips but a fragile body and no stun means you can't commit, and Ki Barrier shields his first cast.","Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real poke trade while Shen still lacks the Shadow Dash taunt to punish your step-up.","Your full mark kit is online and his only threat is one taunt on an 18s rank-1 cooldown — hold the wave near you and chip him while it runs.","It's a chip-and-respect stretch: you keep the poke edge but Shen's taunt flips any extended trade, so you bank small leads rather than all-in.","Slicing Maelstrom into the Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks Shen before he can taunt off it — your single biggest spike and cleanest kill window.","Your Alternator/Liandry's burst cashes the R combo, but Spirit's Refuge blocks basic attacks — Q and R still land through it — so it stays even.","Shen out-scales you into a global peel-tank your magic can't blow up — play engager off your R and skirmish, because Stand United decides the map."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"singed","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Singed","Kennen","Kennen","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a real poke trade or a two-spell mark stun if he steps up to last-hit through his poison."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-locks him out of his own kit — the only window where Slicing Maelstrom holds still a champion whose entire answer is walking away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Liandry's cashes the R combo into burst that beats his HP before Rylai's lands — your cleanest kill window all game."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Fling, Poison Trail and Rylai's let him run you down on R cooldown; Noxious Slipstream hands him speed off every champion he passes and you cannot outrun that."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes and Electrical Surge chip from max range so you never stand in the poison trail","Track his Fling and only commit your E-in mark-stun all-in when it is on cooldown","Hit your level 6 Slicing Maelstrom and burst him with first item before his sustain and move speed take over"],"foe":["Land Fling to toss you into Mega Adhesive, where the landing roots you cold","Drag you through the poison trail so its tick damage wins every trade you make","Build Rylai's/move speed and proxy-farm so he out-scales and runs your squishy body down on R cooldown"]},"early":"Singed never trades back early, so this is your window to chip — Q from 950 and let Electrical Surge on-hit autos do work, but never stand in his poison trail to do it or the tick outruns your chip. The trap is Fling: it is only 125 range, so if you E-in to stack your third Mark of the Storm he flips you into the poison and under tower. At level 2-3, if he steps up to last-hit, a Q plus W on-hit lands your third-mark stun before he reacts.","mid":"At 4-5 he gets slippery — Noxious Slipstream speed and poison let him sidestep your Q and you can't commit without burning E, so chip and respect Fling here. Level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through the poison, and Q-W-E-Flash-R is the one combo that holds him still long enough to kill. Never commit on top of Mega Adhesive: flung into that goo you are rooted, not slowed.","late":"This is where he reclaims the lane. Once he has Rylai's and Liandry's, your poke can't out-damage the HP he stacks, and Noxious Slipstream plus the slow run your squishy body down the moment Slicing Maelstrom's 120s is running. You cannot duel him in a sidelane late — pivot to teamfights where your AoE R peels and engages for your team, and let your carries deal with a Singed who just wants to fling and proxy. Close on your 6/first-item spike or this is his game.","whys":["You both have weak level 1s — one Q and Electrical Surge autos chip him, but with no stun and a fragile body you don't commit into a champ who just walks away.","A second Q point plus W on-hit lands a real poke or a two-spell mark stun if he oversteps to last-hit — take it only when Fling is down.","Full kit online, and an immobile-ish Singed with no dash can't dodge your Q chip or escape the mark chain if he steps into the wave on your side.","His move speed and poison let him sidestep your Q and concede nothing, and committing E here just feeds his Fling-into-poison flip, so respect the window.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through the poison and Q-W-E-Flash-R is the one all-in that pins a champion who otherwise just walks away.","Hextech Alternator/Liandry's turns the R combo into real kill pressure that beats his pre-Rylai's sustain — this is your peak, force it now.","With Rylai's and Liandry's the HP he stacks out-grinds your poke, and Noxious Slipstream plus the slow runs you down on R cooldown — don't sidelane him."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"sion","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Sion","Kennen","Kennen","Sion"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chip a stationary Sion freely and even land a two-spell mark stun if he steps up to charge Q."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into an immobile Sion is your hardest all-in — Q-W-E stacks Mark of the Storm and R stun-locks him before he can charge a knockup."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's converts your R combo into real kill pressure on Sion before his HP and MR balloon out of burst range."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Sion's biggest threat window — a full-charge Decimating Smash knocks you clear of your own storm, and Glory in Death keeps him swinging and healing after he dies."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q pokes on a stationary Sion every cooldown and use Electrical Surge autos to chip him while he can't dodge","Hit your level 6 and dump Q-W-E-R to stun-lock and burst him before he builds MR and HP","Punish him the instant he winds up Decimating Smash — he is rooted in place charging it, so chip from 950"],"foe":["Land a fully charged Decimating Smash to knock you clear of your own storm","Buy early MR and stack HP so your all-magic burst stops one-shotting him","Survive your level 6 window and use his zombie passive to keep trading after you commit"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — your single Q against his slow charged Q means neither of you commits — but from 2 the poke lane is yours. Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips a target this immobile for free, and he has to stand still to charge Decimating Smash, so punish every wind-up from 950 range. Own the wave through 3. Then downshift at 4-5: the charged knockup and Roar of the Slayer's armour shred turn real and he can genuinely trade back, so stop hunting hard commits and keep the chip ticking from max range.","mid":"Level 6 is your biggest spike of the game, even into a tank: E in, Q-W to stack Mark of the Storm, and Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks an immobile Sion before he can charge a knockup. First item doubles down — Hextech Alternator or Liandry's cashes that R combo into real kill pressure while his HP and MR are still low. One rule: never walk into a charging Decimating Smash — it is 10s at rank 1, so make him swing it at a minion and commit after. Kill him now and often; every death delays the tank stats that put him out of burst range.","late":"At 2+ items the duel is his — his HP and MR balloon out of your all-magic burst range, Soul Furnace shields and then detonates for max-health magic, and even a won fight leaves Glory in Death swinging and healing off your max HP. Stop dueling him. Your late job is teamfights: flank with Lightning Rush, land a multi-man Slicing Maelstrom on the carries behind him, and let your team handle the frontliner. Unstoppable Onslaught rolls 7500 units and hits harder the further it travels — hold Flash for that, not for damage.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — your single Q poke and his slow charged Q cancel out, so neither commits and it reads even.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-chips an immobile Sion who can only shield, and you can punish a charge wind-up with a two-spell mark stun.","You own the wave and the poke against a stationary target who can't escape your Q or kite your marks before he has MR.","Decimating Smash's charged knockup and Roar of the Slayer's armour shred become real threats, so concede the hard-commit window and just chip.","Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-locks an immobile Sion and bursts him with magic before his HP and MR scale — your biggest spike, even into a tank.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes your R combo into kill pressure while Sion's resists are still low enough for your magic to chunk him.","Sion's HP and MR, a charged Decimating Smash that knocks you clear of your own storm, and Glory in Death mean a built tank out-survives everything you throw — teamfight instead."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Swain"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lands a poke trade Swain's Death's Hand can't sustain, and he has no dash to escape if he oversteps to place Vision of Empire."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock — you blow up a dashless Swain before his Demonic Ascension drain can out-heal your burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill — chunk him from range with Q and only commit when his E pull is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Swain's biggest threat: Nevermove roots on its return trip, and the recast pulls you into Demonic Ascension where the drain out-heals everything you deal."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke Swain down with Q and Electrical Surge autos he can't heal back before level 6","Wait out his E pull, then E-W-Q-R stun-lock him while he has no dash to escape","Burst him on your 6/first-item spike before his R drain and soul stacks come online"],"foe":["Land Nevermove's return-trip root, then recast to pull you into his drain","Stack Death's Hand poke and Vision of Empire bombs on your fragile body","Drag fights long so Demonic Ascension drain out-sustains your short-cooldown burst"]},"early":"Swain is immobile with no dash, which is exactly what your Q wants — chip him with Thundering Shuriken from 950 and stack Electrical Surge autos he can't out-sustain pre-6. Respect Nevermove (E): the wave is harmless going out and roots on the way BACK, and he can then recast to drag you in, so never stand still in its return line. At level 2-3, if he oversteps to place Vision of Empire, punish — he can't dodge your poke and can't run from it.","mid":"This is your window. By 6 your Slicing Maelstrom turns a clean all-in lethal: bait or sidestep his E, then E onto him, stack Mark of the Storm with W, and R to stun-lock — a dashless Swain can't escape the chain and your burst beats his drain before Demonic Ascension ramps. The discipline is the E: a landed Nevermove lets him pull you into his own drain radius, so all-in only on its 12s cooldown. Your Alternator/Rocketbelt spike is your peak — force the kill here.","late":"Win the lane on your 6/first-item spike, because late game tilts back toward Swain. Once he has Demonic Ascension up with soul stacks and Liandry's, an extended AOE fight feeds his drain and out-heals your short-cooldown burst, and one landed Nevermove drags you into the middle of it. Buy Grievous Wounds before that: Ravenous Flock heals him and permanently raises his max HP, so unanswered chip funds him. Don't sidelane-duel him late.","whys":["Level 1 is even — you have one Q poke and Surge autos but a fragile body, and Swain's Q chip trades back, so neither commits.","Second Q point and Electrical Surge on-hit land a poke trade his Death's Hand can't answer, and he has no dash to escape yours at 950 range.","You own the wave against an immobile Swain here — chain Q-Surge marks and punish any overstep for a W bomb.","You keep the poke edge through 4-5; Swain has no level-3 burst combo to reclaim the window, so chip him and respect his E.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock — a dashless Swain dies before his Demonic Ascension drain out-heals it.","Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill, and Oblivion Orb stops Ravenous Flock healing it back.","At 2+ items Swain reclaims it — soul-stacked drain healing, and one landed Nevermove drags you into that drain, out-lasting your burst. Close before this."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Sylas"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a three-mark stun if he steps up to last-hit in Q range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your Slicing Maelstrom all-in beats his pre-item healing, but Hijack takes the storm from 950 range — bait his R first, or fight without yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt turns your Q-W-E-R combo into a kill before his Q-W heal can out-sustain it."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Full-build Sylas out-heals your burst, and Hijack on a 30s rank-3 cooldown outscales your short-cooldown caster — your kill window has closed."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q from max range and stack Mark of the Storm so an E-W stun lands before he can E-dash out","Hit level 6, buy Oblivion Orb, and burst him with the R stun-lock before Kingslayer heals","Close the game on your 6 and first-item spike and pivot to teamfights before his scaling and stolen ults take over"],"foe":["Heal your poke back with Kingslayer and refuse to fight until he out-sustains the chip","Bait or out-range your Slicing Maelstrom and steal it with R, then turn your own storm on you","Reach 2+ items where Kingslayer healing and a stolen ultimate out-trade your fragile short-cooldown burst"]},"early":"Sylas sits in the wave and heals your poke off with Chain Lash and Kingslayer, so don't trade into a full-health Sylas expecting damage to stick — it won't, and an early Oblivion Orb is what fixes that. Farm with max-range Q (Thundering Shuriken) and commit a stun only when he steps up to melee a minion: a Q-mark plus an Electrical Surge auto, then E-in for the third stack. Watch Abscond (E, 13s) — E onto him while it is up and he dashes free, then heals the trade back even.","mid":"This is your window. Your Q poke chips faster than Kingslayer heals once Electrical Surge on-hit is running, and at 6 your Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him for a kill before he heals it off. The catch that makes this lane real: Hijack steals YOUR ultimate from 950 range on 80s at rank 1. If he takes it first he gets his own Slicing Maelstrom — so bait it with a fake E-in, or commit only while those 80 seconds run. With Hextech Alternator your Q-W-E-R blows up his squishy body outright.","late":"Once Sylas hits 2+ items the lane flips — Kingslayer out-heals your burst on a 6s cooldown, Abduct chains him straight back onto you the moment you walk away, and a stolen ultimate gives him a second game-changing button you have no answer to. You're a fragile short-cooldown caster who gets focused the moment your R is down. Win this on your 6 and first-item spike, take plates and a kill, and pivot to teamfighting where your AoE R peels — never 1v1 a fed Sylas in the sidelane.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 — you have one Q poke and no stun, he has Q-W drain but no fight in him yet, so it's a farm-and-set-up stage.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a three-mark stun if he steps into Q range to last-hit, and his drain can't heal a stun through.","Your Q chip now outpaces his Q-W drain in a short trade, and an E-in third-mark stun punishes him before his E-dash is up to escape.","You keep the poke edge and own the wave — bait his E-dash, then stun-and-burst while his drain can't sustain the chip you stack with Q.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him for a kill before Kingslayer heals it, but commit only while Hijack's 80s is running or he takes your storm.","Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes your full Q-W-E-R combo into a kill faster than his drain can out-sustain it — force every all-in now.","Full-build Sylas out-heals your burst with Kingslayer, chains himself back onto you with Abduct, and a stolen ultimate outscales your fragile caster — the lane is his."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"tahmkench","win":["Skill","Skill","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench","Kennen","Tahm Kench","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge lets you land a quick double-mark on him, but Thick Skin banks that chip and heals it back before a third stack lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom is your one real kill window — Q-W-E-Flash-R chains the stun-lock and bursts him before Thick Skin and Abyssal Dive answer."},{"when":"Lvl 3+","text":"Tahm Kench's threat: at three An Acquired Taste stacks Tongue Lash stuns you, or he spends them to Devour you — every E-in to stack marks feeds those stacks."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His MR bruiser build (Spirit Visage / Kaenic) plus a Thick Skin shield made of your own poke beats your Alternator burst — poke stops killing."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke from max range and stack a level 2-3 double-mark stun before his grey health regens it","Hit Level 6 and burn Flash to land the full R stun-lock all-in while he has no MR yet","Roam and use your global R presence to win 2v2 dives and fights away from his sustain"],"foe":["Bait your E-in, land his third stack, then stun with Tongue Lash or Devour your low-HP body","Bank grey health off your poke with Thick Skin and stack MR (Spirit Visage) to out-last your kit","Survive to 2 items where health-scaled damage and stored healing make him unkillable"]},"early":"Thick Skin (E) is the whole problem early — your Q chip and Electrical Surge on-hit turn into grey health he regenerates out of combat or converts straight into a shield, so you rarely reach a third Mark of the Storm stack. At levels 2-3 you can land a fast double-mark off Q plus W and force him off the wave, but count HIS stacks while you do it: Tongue Lash only stuns at three stacks of An Acquired Taste, and at three he can spend them to Devour you instead. Poke from the very edge of 950 range, keep his stacks off you, and accept this is a farm-and-chip lane rather than a kill lane.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — your poke edge means nothing against stored grey health and he is already enormous, so don't commit. Level 6 is your one real window: Slicing Maelstrom plus the Q-W-E-Flash-R chain stun-locks him and burns his HP before Thick Skin and Abyssal Dive can answer, and he has no MR yet. If you win this lane, win it on this spike or in a 6+ 2v2 dive — bait Tongue Lash first, then E in and R once it is down.","late":"This is where Tahm Kench takes the lane back outright. Once he has Spirit Visage and a single MR or HP item, his health-scaled damage and stored grey health shrug off your Alternator burst, and the moment your R is down three stacks let him stun or Devour your frame for free. Remember Slicing Maelstrom is only 550 radius — he answers it by walking out. Don't out-duel him in a sidelane; pivot to a teamfight engager and let your team handle the blob.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — your single Q and Surge autos just bank grey health inside Thick Skin, so neither commits.","Your level-2 double-mark off Q plus W can shove him in, but Thick Skin regenerates that chip out of combat before you reach the stun.","By level 3 Thick Skin's stored healing out-lasts your poke, and Tongue Lash reaches 900 to slow you out of any mark setup.","His health-scaled damage out-lasts your chip-and-respect window, and Abyssal Dive lands from 1000 range on any over-step you make.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that bursts him before Thick Skin's shield can answer — your one owned window, with no MR on him yet.","His first MR/HP item plus a Thick Skin shield built from your own poke beat your Alternator burst, so the R combo stops killing.","At two items his health-stacked sustain makes him unkillable, and three An Acquired Taste stacks let him stun or Devour your squishy body once R is down."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"teemo","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Skill","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade and even a two-spell mark stun if he steps up to last-hit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom turns a Q-mark + E-in into a full stun-lock all-in that blows him up before his blind cooldown returns."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Liandry's cashes the R combo into a one-rotation kill on his squishy body."},{"when":"Late","text":"Noxious Trap walls off your E paths and Move Quick plus the blind let him chip you out once your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke at max range and stack Mark of the Storm without eating a blinded auto","Hit Level 6 and convert a Q-mark into E-in plus R stun-lock before his blind resets","Buy Mercury's Treads early so his E poison plus blind harass does not snowball you out"],"foe":["Hold Q blind for the exact moment you E-in or autos so your on-hit Electrical Surge whiffs","Kite with Move Quick (W) and chip with Toxic Shot to deny your mark stacking","Survive to two items and shroom every chokepoint so your E engage is walled off"]},"early":"Blinding Dart is the problem child — it shuts off your autos and the Electrical Surge on-hit mark, one of your four mark sources, so a blind delays three stacks rather than preventing them. The flip side: 950 range against his 680 means you poke from outside his answer and stack Mark of the Storm where a blind does nothing to a skillshot. At levels 2-3 you get your cleanest window — a second Q plus W on an already-marked target lands a two-spell stun if he oversteps to CS.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are a respect stretch — he kites with Move Quick (W) and Toxic Shot chips you while you wait, so don't force without your stun ready. Level 6 is your window: hold a Q mark, then E-in and cast Slicing Maelstrom — the AoE storm restacks marks fast and the third-stack stun locks him with no dash to escape. Blind cannot stop that: it denies your autos only, so Q, W-active and the storm all keep applying Mark of the Storm.","late":"This is where he reclaims the lane. Once he hits two items his mushrooms wall off every E engage path and blind plus Move Quick let him whittle your squishy body whenever your R is down. You can't sit in a straight 1v1 here — pivot to roaming and teamfighting where your R stun-locks a clump instead of chasing one kiting Teemo. Sweep before any all-in: Guerrilla Warfare keeps him invisible while he moves through brush.","whys":["You out-range him but your fragile body and his blind cancel each other out — last-hit at Q range and don't over-commit without a stun.","Your second Q plus W on-hit lands a real poke trade he can't sustain, and a two-spell mark stun if he steps up.","With Q-W chaining you can stun-lock an overstepping Teemo through the mark before his blind resets the trade.","He kites with Move Quick (W) and chips with Toxic Shot while your hard-commit window isn't open — chip and respect.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-in is a full stun-lock all-in with no escape for him — your single biggest window.","Your Alternator/Liandry's R combo bursts his squishy body, but Move Quick walks him clear of your 550 storm.","Noxious Trap walls your E paths and blind-and-kite grinds down your short-cooldown caster once R is down — teamfight instead."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"trundle","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Trundle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three marks for the stun if he steps up to last-hit under your shuriken poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into E-in stun-locks him through his sustain and your magic damage ignores the armor he stole with Subjugate."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your mark combo into a kill before King's Tribute heals him off the dying wave."},{"when":"Late","text":"His R steals your resistances and heals huge, and Frozen Domain plus Pillar let him run you down once your R is on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke him off the wave with Q so he can't freely Q-bite your AD and farm","Land the three-mark stun at level 2-3 or your level-6 R combo before his sustain stabilizes","Close the game on your 6/first-item burst spike since your magic ignores his stacked armor"],"foe":["Reset his auto with Chomp to sap your AD and chunk you while you stack marks","Drop his Pillar (E) under you to body-block your E-in and break your spacing","Use Frozen Domain (W) move speed and Subjugate (R) resist-steal to run you down and out-sustain late"]},"early":"Trundle's whole early game is Chomp — a 300-range auto reset on 3.5s that saps your attack damage, so the wind-up animation is your cue to step back, not the cast. Poke with Thundering Shuriken (Q) from 950 and chip with Electrical Surge on-hits only when you can disengage. The good news: your damage is magic, so the armour he builds does nothing, and at level 2-3 a second Q plus an activated W on a marked target stacks the third Mark of the Storm for a real stun if he oversteps to CS. Mind your fragile HP bar — one greedy step and he walks you down.","mid":"This is your window. At 6, Slicing Maelstrom (R) stun-locks him through his healing, and E-in (Lightning Rush) closes the gap while applying a mark — his armour stack is irrelevant to magic burst. Bait Pillar of Ice (E): it is 21s at rank 1, so once he spends it you walk around it, R, and chunk him before Frozen Domain (W) heal-stacking matters. Remember Lightning Rush passes through units but never through his pillar.","late":"Past two items Trundle reclaims this lane: Subjugate steals a chunk of your resistances and health, and the theft doubles over four seconds, so a squishy caster has nothing left once your own R is down. Frozen Domain raises his healing from every source while he stands on it, so without Grievous Wounds you cannot out-damage it in a long 1v1. Close on your 6/first-item spike or pivot to teamfights, where your AoE R peel matters far more than dueling him in the sidelane.","whys":["You both have weak level-1s — one Q poke chips but you can't commit, and his Q-bite steals your AD if you auto, so just farm at shuriken range.","Your second Q plus W on-hit can chain three Mark of the Storm stacks for a stun if he steps up to last-hit, and his armor does nothing against magic.","You own the wave here — poke him off CS with Q and his only answer is to bite-trade, which loses to your range while he's still low on sustain.","He hits his bite-and-Pillar rhythm and your hard-commit windows shrink, so it's a chip-and-respect stretch where neither of you can cleanly all-in.","Slicing Maelstrom into E stun-locks him through Frozen Domain heals, and your magic burst ignores every point of armor he's stolen — your biggest spike.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your mark combo into a kill before King's Tribute and Frozen Domain heal it back — force the all-in.","Subjugate steals your resistances and heals off your max HP, and a squishy short-cooldown caster can't out-trade a drain-tank once your R is down — play to teamfight instead."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"tryndamere","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Tryndamere","Kennen","Skill","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk him before his Fury bar fills — your cleanest poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom + Q-W-E mark stun-locks him; the one window his R can't save him, because the storm is still burning when Undying Rage expires at 1 HP."},{"when":"Lvl 4-5","text":"Spinning Slash closes 650 on a 12s cooldown, and Mocking Shout slows you only while your back is turned — his strongest early kill threat."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once his crit and Undying Rage come online he tanks your full R and survives at 1 HP, then spins you down — you lose the extended duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun before he closes the gap","Hit your Level 6 Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock while his Fury and crit are still low","Use E (Lightning Rush) to disengage his spin the instant your stun is down, not to chase"],"foe":["Build Battle Fury for crits, then Spinning Slash in and Mocking Shout your retreat","Bait your R and E cooldowns, then all-in when your stun chain is unavailable","Survive your Level 6 burst with Undying Rage and out-sustain you into 2 items"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — your single Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip, but you have no stun yet and a glass body, so don't step into his E range to throw it. Levels 2-3 are your window: a second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade and even a two-spell mark stun if he walks up to last-hit, all before his Fury bar is built and his autos start critting. Chunk him here, but never burn your E to chase — that's his whole game-plan, to bait it and E-in on your cooldown.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his, not yours: Spinning Slash closes 650 the second your mark stun goes on cooldown and his Fury-stacked crits now hurt, so chip from range — and remember Mocking Shout only slows you while your back is turned. Then at 6 you reclaim the lane: Slicing Maelstrom plus a Q-W-E mark chain stun-locks him, and the storm keeps burning while Undying Rage ticks away. Hold Flash for the R all-in and time your burst for the moment his immunity ends — that duel is yours cleanly while his crit items are still unfinished.","late":"This is where it slips. Once his crit items and Fury are online he tanks your entire R combo, survives on Undying Rage, then Bloodlust heals the whole thing back on a 12-second cooldown and he spins you down — and without Grievous Wounds your squishy caster body cannot out-damage that. You will not out-duel a fed Tryndamere in the sidelane, so stop trying. Pivot to grouping: your AoE R and global threat make you a teamfight engager, and that is where you cash a lead.","whys":["No stun yet and a glass body — his E and crit potential mean you only poke with Q, never commit at level 1.","Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk him before his Fury bar fills and his autos crit.","A full Q-W mark chain can stun an overstepping Tryndamere here while his early autos still lack crit punch.","Spinning Slash closes 650 and Mocking Shout slows you only while your back is turned, so running is what kills you here.","Slicing Maelstrom plus Q-W-E stun-locks him, and starting the burn as Undying Rage expires kills him from the 1 HP it leaves.","Your Hextech/Liandry's spike still threatens kill pressure, but his Fury crits answer it — genuinely even here.","Fed crit plus Undying Rage tanks your full R and survives at 1 HP, then spins you down — you lose the extended duel, so group instead."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"urgot","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you mark-stun an Urgot who steps up to last-hit with his shotgun legs."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-lock blows up an Urgot who has spent Disdain (E) and cannot flip out of your storm."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a kill before his Purge percent-HP shred can answer."},{"when":"Late","text":"His W shotgun legs and R fear-execute punish you the moment you get caught at low HP off cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Poke with Q from outside his W (Purge) shotgun-leg range and never trade inside it","Stack three marks for the stun, then E-in or R to lock him with no dash to escape","Stay above his R execute threshold so his fear-execute has nothing to finish"],"foe":["Land Q (Corrosive Charge), then flip you with Disdain (E) into Purge range","Stack W percent-max-HP shots on your squishy body in a sustained DPS fight","Drop you low so his R fear-and-execute can interrupt your channel and finish you"]},"early":"Urgot has no dash and a slow E-flip, so this is your kind of immobile melee — chip him with Q from max range and walk away before he can shotgun-leg (W Purge) you. The one thing to respect is his E (Corrosive Charge): if it lands it slows you into Purge range where his percent-max-HP shots shred your low HP, so dodge it and don't sit still after you poke. At 2-3 a second Q and an Electrical Surge auto can land a real mark-stun if he oversteps to CS.","mid":"This stretch is yours as long as you keep distance. Keep stacking Q marks and never walk into a W trade he can win with percent-HP. At 6, Slicing Maelstrom is the kill, but bait Disdain (E) first: it shields him and hurls you out. With it down 16s, Q-W-E in, mark-stun, R, and he melts. Track his R too — a fear mid-channel ends the all-in.","late":"Close this on your 6 and first-item spike — that is your peak and where his shotgun legs can't out-DPS your burst. Past two items the math shifts: his W percent-max-HP scales into your build and his R fear-execute deletes you the instant you get caught low off cooldown. Don't sidelane-duel a tanky Urgot late; pivot to teamfights where your AoE R stun-locks his whole team and your range keeps you out of Purge.","whys":["Both of you are weak level 1 — one Q chips but you have no stun and a fragile body, and his W Purge punishes any commit, so respect the lane.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit lands a real poke trade or a mark-stun on an Urgot who steps into shotgun-leg range to CS.","You out-range him — mark with Q from outside Purge; his only step-up is Disdain (E), down 16s at rank 1.","You hold a clear poke edge; dodge his Q (Corrosive Charge) so its slow can't drag you into Purge percent-HP range.","Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks Urgot once Disdain (E) is spent — Q-W-E-R bursts him before Purge ramps up.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill before his shotgun-leg percent-HP can out-DPS you.","His W percent-max-HP scales into your build and his R fear-execute deletes a caught, low-HP you — take fights only in teamfights, not a sidelane duel."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"vayne","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade or even a two-spell mark stun before she has tumble spacing down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock — you melt a no-MR Vayne who has no R-dash to break the channel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into a clean one-rotation kill on her sub-1000-HP body."},{"when":"Late","text":"Past two items Silver Bolts' true damage and Final Hour's Tumble invisibility kite you forever while your 120s R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun before she can tumble away","Hit your level 6 and E-Flash-R stun-lock her low-HP body before she has items","Snowball the 6/first-item spike and end before her W true damage and lifesteal come online"],"foe":["Tumble (Q) to dodge your Thundering Shuriken and reset her attack while kiting back","Condemn (E) you mid-channel to break your R or pin you for her jungler","Survive lane to 2+ items where Silver Bolts true damage and invis melt you"]},"early":"Vayne at levels 1-3 is just a farming target for your Q — she has no tumble spacing yet and her autos chip for nothing. Land Thundering Shuriken on her and stack Mark of the Storm with Electrical Surge autos; at 2-3 a clean Q-into-W mark trade or even a two-spell stun punishes her hard if she steps up to last-hit. Watch her Q (tumble) — she'll use it to dodge your shuriken and reset an auto, so throw your Q when she's committed to a CS animation, not on cooldown into open space.","mid":"This is your takeover. At 6 your Slicing Maelstrom turns every all-in lethal — E-in or Flash onto her, R channels the stun-lock, and a Vayne with no Mercs and no R-dash simply can't break it before she dies. Bait her Condemn (E): if she walls you mid-channel she can interrupt your R, so save E (Lightning Rush) to dodge it or force it before you commit. First item (Alternator/Rocketbelt) is your peak — her body is under 1000 HP and your full rotation deletes it.","late":"Past two items the lane flips and you cannot stop it. Silver Bolts deals percent-max-HP true damage that ignores any HP you stack, Final Hour makes every Tumble an invisibility to break your target lock, and Condemn knocks you clean out of a Slicing Maelstrom channel. Your only answer is to have already won: close on your 6 and first-item spike, take plates and top-side skirmishes, and pivot to a teamfight engager. If it goes long, never duel her — group and R the carries.","whys":["You're both weak at level 1 — one Q chips, but with no stun don't commit: Tumble (Q) is an auto reset, so the wind-up is the tell.","Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade she can't sustain through this early.","Three marks stun-lock her — a level-3 Kennen owns the wave against a Vayne with no tumble spacing or escape window.","You keep the Q poke edge and she has no all-in answer pre-6, so you chip her down freely.","Slicing Maelstrom plus E-Flash stun-locks her no-MR body — she has no R-dash to break the channel and dies.","Alternator/Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a one-rotation kill on her sub-1000-HP frame — force every all-in here.","She out-scales hard: Silver Bolts' true damage ignores your HP and Final Hour hides her Tumble while your R sits on a 120s cooldown."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"vladimir","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Vladimir","Kennen","Kennen","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack three Marks of the Storm and stun a Vlad who steps up to last-hit before Sanguine Pool exists."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stacks marks instantly and stun-locks Vlad through pool's cooldown — your single best kill window all lane."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a real kill, but bait Sanguine Pool first or the whole burst whiffs on an untargetable body."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"Rylai's plus Riftmaker Vlad out-sustains your poke and pools your stun chain — he reclaims the lane and the teamfight as the unkillable scaler."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack three Marks of the Storm with Q and Electrical Surge to stun him before he can Sanguine Pool out","Hit your Level 6 R all-in and bait Sanguine Pool BEFORE you commit the Q-W-E-Flash chain","Close the game on your 6 and first-item spike before his Rylai's drain-tank scaling takes over"],"foe":["Use Sanguine Pool to go untargetable and dodge your third-stack stun and your R channel","Sustain your Q poke with Transfusion and farm safely to two AP items","Stack Rylai's and Riftmaker to out-drain your burst and become the unkillable teamfight threat"]},"early":"Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s in the game, but so is your fragile body, so neither of you commits — Q poke at max range and chip with Electrical Surge autos while you bank energy. Your real window is levels 2-3: a second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land three Marks of the Storm for the stun, and crucially he has no Sanguine Pool yet to dodge it. Punish every time he steps up to last-hit, but never dive past his Transfusion sustain — his Q heal eats your poke if you trade for free.","mid":"Levels 4-5 he hits his stride: Transfusion sustain and E pool-poke heal back your chip, and you concede the hard-commit window, so play for marks and respect his drain. Then level 6 flips it back to you — Slicing Maelstrom plus your Q-W-E stacks three marks in a blink and stun-locks him through pool's cooldown, your hardest all-in of the lane. The whole kill hinges on baiting Sanguine Pool first: if he pools your R channel or your third-stack stun, your entire combo vanishes into an untargetable puddle.","late":"This is where Vlad takes the lane and never gives it back — once Rylai's and Riftmaker come online he out-sustains your poke, pools your stun chain, and his W makes him untargetable through your entire R. As a squishy short-cooldown caster you can't out-duel a drain-tank with your burst on cooldown, so stop trying to 1v1 him in the sidelane. Close the game on your 6/first-item spike, then pivot to a teamfight engager — your AoE R peeling and stun-locking his carries matters far more than losing a hopeless splitpush to an unkillable Vlad.","whys":["Vlad is one of the weakest level-1s, but your fragile caster body is too — neither of you commits, so it reads even.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge stacks three Marks of the Storm for a stun, and he has no Sanguine Pool yet to escape it.","You own the wave and the mark-stun trade against a pre-pool Vlad whose only answer is to back off and Transfusion the chip.","He hits his Transfusion rhythm and heals your poke back; keep minions between you, since Tides of Blood is blocked by enemy units.","Slicing Maelstrom into Q-W-E stun-locks him through pool's cooldown — your single cleanest kill window all game.","Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt turns your R combo into a real kill, as long as you bait Sanguine Pool before committing.","Full-AP Vlad with Rylai's and Riftmaker out-sustains your burst and pools your stun — he out-scales you hard, so let your team handle him."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"volibear","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Volibear"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke trade or a two-spell mark stun if he walks up for a W-bite — your cleanest early window before his sustain ramps."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom turns the lane: Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-locks him through his E channel and bursts him before his W heal can out-sustain it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator/Liandry's cashes the R combo into a real kill — your peak window, and magic damage ignores the armor he stacks."},{"when":"Lvl 6+ (his)","text":"Sky Splitter (E) slows you from 1200 range and shields him if he stands in the blast, and Frenzied Maul heals through your poke once he has items — his all-in beats yours late."}],"wants":{"you":["Chip him with Q from max range and stack Mark of the Storm before he closes — never trade inside his W-bite range","Hit level 6 with full HP and force the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock through his E channel before his sustain takes over","Convert your 6 and first-item spike into a kill or huge plate lead — close the game before he out-scales you 1v1"],"foe":["Land Sky Splitter (E) to slow you and shield himself, then Thundering Smash (Q) to stun you as he closes","Out-sustain your poke with W-bite healing and a passive heal so your chip never converts to a kill","Scale past your 6 with armor/HP, then walk you down once your R is on cooldown and you can't kite the dash"]},"early":"Volibear is a slow immobile target pre-6, so this is exactly the body you abuse — hit him with max-range Q (Thundering Shuriken) every time he steps to last-hit and stack Mark of the Storm. The trap is his W (bite): it slows and heals him, so never trade standing inside its range. Bait him to walk up for a W, then E-in on contact for the mark and back out, or W-activate (Electrical Surge) on already-marked targets to pop the third-stack stun on an overstep. His passive heal at low HP means your chip won't kill — it sets up the level-6 all-in.","mid":"At levels 4-5 respect his combo (Thundering Smash's stun into Frenzied Maul into passive procs out-damages your trade), so chip-and-back rather than committing. Then 6 is your window: Slicing Maelstrom plus the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock holds him and bursts him before Frenzied Maul's heal out-sustains it, so have Grievous Wounds first. Watch Sky Splitter (E): from 1200 range it slows you and shields him if he stands in the blast, so bait that shield out or dodge with Lightning Rush before you commit.","late":"This is where he reclaims the lane. Volibear stacks HP and armor and his W-bite heal plus passive out-sustains a squishy caster, so once your R is on cooldown he simply walks you down — his Q dash closes the gap your kite can't open, and his E interrupts any re-engage. Your magic ignores his armor, but he out-EHPs your burst at two items. You must have closed the game on your 6/first-item spike; if it goes long, stop sidelane-dueling him and pivot to teamfights where your AoE R and global threat peel for your team instead of feeding his dive.","whys":["Level 1 is even — one Q poke and Electrical Surge autos chip him, but with no stun and a fragile body you can't punish his W-bite trade yet.","Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you land a real poke or a two-spell mark stun on an overstepping Volibear before his sustain ramps.","You own the wave against an immobile bruiser here — max-range Q stacks marks while he can't dodge or close, and a third-stack stun chunks him.","He hits his Thundering Smash-into-Frenzied Maul combo and heals your chip back, so poke and back off — anti-heal before you commit to anything.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that beats his pre-item all-in — force Sky Splitter's shield out first, then commit.","Hextech Alternator/Liandry's cashes the R combo into kill pressure and your magic ignores the armor he builds — your peak relative strength.","He out-scales hard: Frenzied Maul healing and stacked HP out-last your burst, and Stormbringer leaps on you with your R down — play teamfights, not sidelane."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"warwick","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Warwick","Kennen","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you chunk him before his Q heal scales — your cleanest pure-poke window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Q-W-E-Flash-R with R first stuns him before Infinite Duress leaps — Riot lists that suppress as interruptible by CC."},{"when":"Warwick 6+","text":"His R suppress (Infinite Duress) is a point-and-click channel-interrupt on your fragile body — get caught and you die before R finishes."},{"when":"2+ items","text":"His drain passive heals harder the lower you push him, so your burst stalls and he out-sustains every extended trade."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q-W mark stuns at level 2-3 to chip him before his Q heal and passive sustain come online","Keep E ready to dodge his Infinite Duress suppress and his W move-speed gap-close","R FIRST in any all-in so your stun-lock starts before he can lock you with R"],"foe":["Use W (Blood Hunt) move speed to close your kite range and force you into melee","Out-sustain your poke with Q heal and his low-HP-bonus drain passive","Land Infinite Duress to suppress-cancel your R channel and delete your squishy body"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are your only clean poke window, so use them: Q-poke from max range and let Electrical Surge on-hit chip when he steps up to last-hit. The catch is his passive — your chip heals back the lower he is, and his Q (Jaws of the Beast) is a heal on you, so single Q pokes barely stick. Stack a real mark stun at level 2-3 with Q plus W on an overstep, then back off. Never sit in melee: his W move speed will catch you and he out-trades you the moment your kite ends.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his to bully — he hits his sustain stride and his W chase closes the gap your poke needs, so respect and chip, don't commit. Level 6 is your one flip: Q-W-E in, Flash if needed, and R FIRST so your stun-lock and mark-chain start before he can land Infinite Duress. If you out-tempo his ult you delete him; if he R-suppresses you mid-channel, your R cancels and your squishy body dies. Bait or save E to dodge the suppress.","late":"This is where the lane slips away — his drain passive heals harder the more you chunk him, so at 2+ items your burst stalls and he out-sustains every extended fight while his W runs you down. Your R is a 2v2 and teamfight weapon, not a 1v1 trump card here once it's on cooldown. Don't sidelane-duel him: group, use R to peel and engage skirmishes, and let your AoE burst matter where he can't drain back to full off you alone.","whys":["Level 1 is even — your one Q poke and Surge autos chip, but his passive heals it back and your fragile body can't commit.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lands a real poke trade before his Q heal and drain sustain scale up.","At level 3 a Q-W mark stun on an overstep is your hardest pre-6 punish — chip him while his sustain is still weak.","Levels 4-5 he hits his sustain stride and Blood Hunt's speed closes your kite range under 50% HP, so he out-trades you.","At 6 you R FIRST: land the mark stun before Infinite Duress leaps and the suppress never starts — your best window.","Your first item cashes the R combo into kill pressure, but his drain heal off your chip keeps the trade genuinely even.","His low-HP drain passive out-sustains your burst and his W runs you down — group and play R as a teamfight tool, not a duel."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"wukong","win":["Skill","Kennen","Skill","Wukong","Kennen","Kennen","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three marks and stun him if he steps up to last-hit through your poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom into a marked Wukong is your hardest all-in and stun-locks him through his W clone window."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the Q-W-E-R combo into a kill before his armor stacking matters."},{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"His level-3 Q-E-R combo is his threat window — the knockup interrupts your R channel and his clone bait turns your engage."}],"wants":{"you":["Stack three Marks of the Storm with Q and W on-hit to stun him before he reaches you","Hit level 6 and burn his W clone with R, then stun-lock through the channel","Close on your 6 / first-item spike before his armor and bruiser items come online"],"foe":["Q-shred your armor and trade in melee where your squishy body loses extended fights","Land R spin knockup to interrupt your R channel and your E-in engage","Bait your all-in onto his W clone and stack armor to flatten your magic burst"]},"early":"Wukong's whole early game is the Q armor-shred auto-attack and his W clone, so don't blow your stun chain onto a decoy. Poke with Thundering Shuriken at max range and let Electrical Surge on-hit chip when he steps to last-hit — at level 2-3 you can land a real two-spell mark stun if he overextends to shred you. Respect his level-3 Q-empowered-AA into E-dash combo, though; if he gets on top of you with his armor up, his melee trade beats your fragile body, so don't sit in his face hunting a third mark you can't safely land.","mid":"Level 6 is your window — Slicing Maelstrom stacks marks fast and stun-locks him through the W clone if you R the real Wukong, so bait the decoy first, then Q-W-E-R when he commits. The danger is his R spin knockup interrupting your channel: if he saves it, your R does nothing and he flips the all-in, so force the fight when his ult is down. Levels 4-5 before your 6 are a respect stretch — his level-3 combo out-trades you, so chip and wait for your spike rather than dueling him even.","late":"Wukong reclaims this lane once he stacks armor and bruiser items — your all-magic kit is exactly what his armor counters, and his W clone plus E-dash mean he survives your stun window and out-trades your short-cooldown squishy body. You can't sit in a sidelane and duel a fed Wukong, so cash your 6 and first-item burst into a lead, then pivot to teamfights where Slicing Maelstrom catches him and his team in AoE. Close the game on your spike or his armor and R spin out-scale your single-target burst.","whys":["Level 1 is even-to-weak for both — one Q chips, but you have no stun and Crushing Blow (Q) is an auto reset, so the wind-up is your cue to step back.","Your second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three marks and stun him if he oversteps to last-hit — your cleanest early window.","His level-3 Q-empowered-AA into E-dash and clone trade out-damages your fragile body, and he can survive your mark chain — even at best.","He hits his hard-commit combo and you concede it — his armor-up melee trade beats you, so chip and respect rather than duel.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your full Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that wins this pre-item duel — R the real Wukong and burst through the clone.","Hextech Alternator or lethality cashes your R combo into a kill before his armor stacking blunts your magic — your peak relative strength.","He out-scales hard: stacked armor counters your all-magic kit, his W clone and E survive your stun window, and his R interrupts your burst."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"yasuo","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit chips him whenever Wind Wall is down — the wall blocks every projectile, but only for 4 seconds."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom (R): the moment he uses Sweeping Blade to dash in, E-Flash onto him and ult — the storm is not a projectile, so Wind Wall cannot block it and it stun-locks him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's: your R combo now blows up a pre-Shieldbow Yasuo outright — this is your hardest kill window, force it before he finishes two crit items."},{"when":"Late","text":"At 2+ items Shieldbow plus crit means he survives your R, Windwalls your Q burst, and his R knockup punishes you the instant your storm is down — your squishy body loses the extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Throw Q only when his Windwall (W) is on cooldown so the mark actually lands and starts your stun chain","Hit Level 6 and E-Flash-R when he commits his E dash, stun-locking him before his crit and R knockup come online","Cash your Level 6 / first-item burst spike into kills and end before Shieldbow and crit reclaim the duel"],"foe":["Hold Wind Wall for your Q poke so four seconds of shurikens and your Mark stacks simply evaporate","Stack flow with E dashes through the wave and scale to two crit items plus Shieldbow before you can close","Catch you with E-Q knockup or R after your Slicing Maelstrom ends and your squishy body has no peel"]},"early":"Level 1 is a wash — you both have fragile bodies, and Wind Wall eats your Q the second you telegraph it, so don't waste your only poke into a held wall. Last-hit at max Q range and fire it when he is mid-Sweeping Blade or the wall is on its 25-second cooldown. From Level 2-3 your Electrical Surge on-hit autos and Lightning Rush stack Mark of the Storm with no projectile for the wall to block, and he has no sustain to heal the chip — so bait the wall, then re-Q.","mid":"This is your lane. Through Levels 4-5 keep chipping with Q on his Windwall cooldown and respect his E-Q-flow-AA combo, but don't let him free-stack flow on the wave. At 6 you own the window outright: when he E-dashes onto you, E-Flash on top of him and drop Slicing Maelstrom — the storm restacks marks to the third-stack stun faster than Windwall can answer and locks him through his own combo. With Hextech Alternator or Liandry's the same all-in straight-up kills a Yasuo who hasn't finished two crit items yet.","late":"You win the lane, but he is the textbook scaler who reclaims the game after two items. Once Shieldbow and crit are online he eats your R burst with the shield, Windwalls your Q, and the moment your storm ends his E-Q knockup or R blows up your squishy body before you re-stack. Close this out on your 6-and-first-item spike, take plates and pressure side, and pivot to teamfights where your AoE R peels for your carries instead of dueling him in a sidelane you can't win late.","whys":["You are both weak level-1s and his Windwall (W) blocks your only real tool — your Q — so neither of you commits and it reads even.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-chips him whenever Wind Wall is down — 25 seconds at rank 1 — and he cannot heal it back.","Electrical Surge and Lightning Rush are not projectiles, so Wind Wall cannot stop your third-stack stun once he oversteps.","You keep the poke edge while respecting his E-Q knockup combo — chip him on the Windwall cooldown and refuse to feed him flow.","Slicing Maelstrom restacks marks through Windwall and stun-locks him when he E-dashes in — your hardest pre-item all-in wins outright.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's turns the E-Flash-R combo lethal against a Yasuo who lacks Shieldbow and a second crit item.","He out-scales hard: Shieldbow eats your R, crit out-DPSes you, and his knockup punishes your squishy body the instant your storm is down — close before this window."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"yone","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Yone","Kennen","Kennen","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lands a real poke trade — force Spirit Cleave's shield out first, on its 14s timer."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom plus the full Q-W-E-Flash mark stun-lock is your hardest all-in window — burst him before he can E-rewind out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator into Liandry's cashes your R combo into a kill, but you must catch his E (Soul Unbound) on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Mortal Steel's dash, Fate Sealed's pull and a stacking Spirit Cleave shield let him live your stun window and out-duel you."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and stack Mark of the Storm while he's stuck farming, then cash the third-mark stun","Hit your level 6 all-in with R + E-in while his E rewind is on cooldown","Bait his Q3 knockup/dash, then burst him before he reaches his 2-item duelist spike"],"foe":["Bank his E (Soul Unbound) to rewind out of your Mark stun and R channel","Survive your level 6 burst, then shield through your poke with Spirit Cleave and out-duel you","Scale to 2+ items where his mobility and dueling reclaim the lane outright"]},"early":"Yone's lane is even at level 1 but you get the first real window — Thundering Shuriken reaches 950 against his 450-range Mortal Steel, so chip him at max range and stack Mark of the Storm while he farms. At 2-3 your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you land a genuine poke trade or even a two-mark stun if he oversteps to last-hit. The catch: Spirit Cleave shields off a chunk of your poke every 14 seconds, so chunk-and-back rather than expecting it to stick. Never get caught by his third Mortal Steel knockup-dash with no E to escape.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are his window — he hits his Q-stack combo and W-cleave damage and can trade into your fragile body, so respect the all-in and keep E (Lightning Rush) up to disengage. Then level 6 flips it: Slicing Maelstrom plus your full Q-W-E-Flash mark chain is your hardest all-in, and if you catch his E (Soul Unbound) on cooldown he cannot rewind out of the stun-lock. Force the fight on that timer — your first item (Hextech Alternator into Liandry's) is when your R combo most reliably blows him up.","late":"This is where Yone reclaims the lane and why it only reads even — at 2+ items his Spirit Cleave shield, Mortal Steel mobility and Fate Sealed pull let him survive your stun window and out-duel you once your R is down, and Fate Sealed is 80s to your 120s. You must close on your 6 and first-item spike; if the game goes long, stop trying to solo-duel him in the sidelane and pivot to a teamfight engager where your AoE R catches his whole team instead of his one slippery body.","whys":["Both of you are weak at level 1 — you out-range his Q poke but with no stun and a fragile body, neither commits, so it reads even.","Your second Q plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you start a real Mark of the Storm chain while he's stuck farming with only Mortal Steel.","With Q-W you land a two-mark poke trade or stun an overstepping Yone before Spirit Cleave's shield absorbs it.","He hits his Mortal Steel stacks and Spirit Cleave shield here and out-trades your body — keep Lightning Rush up and concede it.","Slicing Maelstrom plus the Q-W-E-Flash mark stun-lock wins the pre-item all-in, especially if his E rewind is on cooldown.","Hextech Alternator into Liandry's cashes your R combo into a kill — your peak relative strength, so force the all-in now.","At 2+ items Spirit Cleave's shield, his Q dash and Fate Sealed's pull let him live your stun and out-duel you — play teamfights."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"yorick","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Yorick","Kennen","Kennen","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you poke Yorick down before his Maiden is up — the cleanest window to chip his low base HP."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom turns the E-in third-mark stun into a full all-in that beats Yorick before Maiden can swing the duel."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Liandry's cashes your R combo into a kill — burst him through his mist before he hits two items."},{"when":"Late","text":"Dark Procession (W) plus Maiden and the ghoul swarm zone you off the wave and win the splitpush once your R is down."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and Electrical Surge autos to chip Yorick before Maiden spawns at 6","Hit your level 6 and burn Flash-R to stun-lock him through the mist for a kill","Close the game on your 6 / first-item spike and pivot to teamfights, not the sidelane"],"foe":["Spawn Maiden and let ghouls tank your Q poke while he free-farms and zones the wave","Land Mourning Mist (E) to mark and slow you, then wall your escape with Dark Procession (W)","Survive to 2+ items and splitpush — Maiden plus mist out-zone you in the 1v1"]},"early":"Yorick is slow and clunky pre-6, so levels 2-3 are yours: throw Q (Thundering Shuriken) at his face and let Electrical Surge autos stack Mark of the Storm — his low base HP means a third-mark stun into a quick trade chunks him before he can answer. Dodge Mourning Mist (E): it marks and slows you, strips armour and speeds his ghouls straight at you, and Dark Procession (W) then walls off your exit. Don't sit in the wave eating ghoul autos while you poke; back off and reset the marks instead.","mid":"At 4-5 respect him — once Maiden of the Mist is up his ghouls out-DPS your poke and Dark Procession (W) walls you off the wave, so chip and disengage rather than commit. But level 6 flips it hard: Slicing Maelstrom plus the Q-W-E Flash stun-lock is a real kill button that bursts Yorick through his magic-vulnerable body before Maiden's swing decides the fight. Sidestep Mourning Mist first so the ghouls never get their speed, then E-in for the third mark, ult, and blow him up.","late":"This is Yorick's game, not yours. Once he has 2+ items his Maiden, the ghoul swarm and Dark Procession zone you completely off the sidelane wave, and the moment your R is down Last Rites heals him through anything you have left. Don't try to 1v1 him in the side — you lose. Win on your 6 and first-item spike, then group and use your AoE R as a teamfight engager and peel tool while your team answers his splitpush.","whys":["Yorick's level 1 is sluggish and yours is fragile — one Q poke chips but neither of you commits, so it reads even.","Your second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit out-pokes a Maiden-less Yorick and threatens a two-spell mark stun.","You still own the wave here — Q chip and Mark of the Storm punish his clunky melee before ghouls come online.","Maiden's ghouls out-DPS your poke and Dark Procession (W) walls your escape, so he reclaims the commit window.","Slicing Maelstrom plus Flash-R stun-locks and bursts him through his magic-vulnerable body before Maiden swings the duel.","Hextech Alternator / Liandry's turns your R combo into a kill — your burst peaks here while he's still a one-item juggernaut.","Yorick out-scales hard: Maiden, the ghoul swarm and his W wall zone you off the wave and out-trade you once R is down."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"zac","win":["Kennen","Kennen","Kennen","Skill","Skill","Zac","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 2-3","text":"Second Q point plus Electrical Surge on-hit lets you stack three Marks of the Storm and stun him while his blobs are scattered, before his passive blob sustain refills him."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Slicing Maelstrom chains marks on his whole blob body for a guaranteed stun-lock all-in, and an interrupted Zac E sling means he just walks into your storm."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator or Rocketbelt cashes the R combo into real burst that chunks even a tanky Zac through his magic-vulnerable HP pool."},{"when":"Late","text":"Zac's E sling engage and four passive blobs of healing let him survive your R window and outlast you, especially through Mercs and MR he buys against your all-magic kit."}],"wants":{"you":["Land Q poke and Electrical Surge autos to stack Mark of the Storm and stun him before his blobs heal it back","Hit your level 6 Slicing Maelstrom all-in while his E sling and Q/W CC are on cooldown","Save Lightning Rush to dodge the sling or to close and stun-lock him, never to facecheck a bush"],"foe":["Sling in with Elastic Slingshot, then chain the Q knock-up and Unstable Matter into a kill","Collect his four passive blobs after every trade to heal back all your poke damage","Interrupt your R channel with E knock-up or Q/W CC and survive your stun window into the late game"]},"early":"Zac is one of the few tanks who can't simply walk through your poke unpunished early, but respect his sustain. Chip with Q Thundering Shuriken and stack Mark of the Storm with Electrical Surge autos at levels 2-3, where a clean two-spell mark or a third-stack stun on an overstepping Zac is your cleanest window. The key: never trade after his Q knock-up and W combo land, and watch for his passive blobs splitting off after he takes damage. If you poke before he reclaims them, his blob sustain can't refill the chip you dealt.","mid":"This stays roughly even through levels 4-5 because Zac can E-sling onto your squishy body and his blobs out-heal your poke if you commit lazily. Then level 6 flips it your way. Slicing Maelstrom rips marks onto his whole body for a stun-lock all-in, and because his only real escape is the E sling, a stun mid-engage means he can't reposition out of your storm. Bait his E first, then E in, W to mass-mark, R, and his blob sustain can't out-pace your burst inside a stun.","late":"This is where Zac reclaims the lane, which is why the matchup reads even overall. His four passive blobs and E sling let him eat your R window and simply walk away to heal, and once he buys Mercs and MR your all-magic kit gets blunted hard. You can't out-duel a fed tank as a squishy short-cooldown caster once your R is down. Pivot to a teamfight engager: use your global R threat and AoE stun-lock to peel and burst his carries instead of trying to solo-kill Zac in the sidelane.","whys":["Level 1 is yours at range: Thundering Shuriken chips from 950 while Unstable Matter needs 350 to hurt you, so poke, then step away before he closes and reabsorbs his blobs.","Second Q point plus W on-hit lets you stack three Marks and stun an overstepping Zac before his blob sustain refills, and magic damage ignores his tank armor.","With Q-W marking you own the wave and out-poke his slow blob regen — keep him off his passive pickups and the chip sticks.","It's a chip-and-respect stretch: he hits his level-3 E sling commit and out-sustains lazy trades, so poke but don't hard-commit without a stun ready.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks the Q-W-E-Flash-R stun-lock that locks his blob body in place — his E sling can't escape a stun mid-channel.","Your Alternator or Rocketbelt burst spikes here, but his blob sustain and the first MR he buys mean the stage still belongs to him, not you.","Zac out-scales you here: his four blobs and E sling survive your R window, and Mercs plus MR blunt your all-magic kit — pivot to teamfighting."]},
  {"a":"kennen","b":"ziggs","win":["Ziggs","Skill","Skill","Ziggs","Kennen","Skill","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Bouncing Bomb bounces past its 850 range on a 6s cooldown — he chips you for free before a single Mark of the Storm lands."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your only real window: E in, Q-W to triple-stack Mark of the Storm, Flash-R to stun-lock and burst him before he can W you away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Hextech Alternator / Rocketbelt cashes your R combo into a kill — but Ziggs' first item turns his minefield into a wall you can't walk through."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once your R is down Ziggs kites with Satchel knockback and E mines and out-ranges you forever — you become useless on the sidelane."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge his bouncing Q, hold E, and stack Mark of the Storm only when you can commit the full stun","Reach 6 and land E-Q-W-Flash-R to stun-lock and delete him before W knocks you out","Roam with R and snowball a side lane before his artillery items make you unreachable"],"foe":["Land Q at max range every wave and keep you below half so you can never E in","Hold Satchel Charge to knock you out of your own storm and reset the gap","Wall off chokes with E minefield and siege you out of lane while scaling"]},"early":"Ziggs' Bouncing Bomb (Q) bounces past its 850 cast range and returns every 6 seconds, so he wins the chip war even though Thundering Shuriken reaches 950 — eat the minimum, last-hit from max range, and do NOT walk up to auto with Electrical Surge or you'll take two bombs for one mark. You have no stun and a paper body here, so don't burn E chasing a single mark; you can't three-stack him before Satchel Charge knocks you back. Save E entirely as a gap-closer for level 6, not as poke.","mid":"Level 6 is your one real swing: when Satchel Charge is on its 20-second cooldown, E onto him, Q-W to slam Mark of the Storm to the third-stack stun, then Flash-R so Slicing Maelstrom stun-locks him through the burst. If you don't kill on that combo you lose — his minefield and Satchel reset the gap and you're back to eating Q poke with R down. Track that 20 seconds religiously; if it is up he knocks you clean out of your own storm and walks away.","late":"This is where Ziggs reclaims the lane for good. Once your R is on cooldown he kites you forever with Satchel knockback and E mines, out-ranges every tool you own, and sieges you off the wave — your squishy short-cooldown caster body has no answer to artillery range. Don't try to solo him; pivot to flank R engages in teamfights and group, because a 1v1 sidelane against a scaled Ziggs is unwinnable for you.","whys":["Bouncing Bomb costs him a 6-second cooldown and bounces past its 850 range, so he chips you for free before a Mark ever lands.","You get a second Q point but still can't reach him; trade only if he steps up into your Electrical Surge auto range.","Even with W on-hit you can't three-stack the stun through his range, but you can punish a greedy minefield placement — this stage is genuinely even.","He hits his combo cadence and his Satchel knocks you out of any commit; you concede the hard-engage window and just chip.","Slicing Maelstrom unlocks your full E-Q-W-Flash-R stun-lock — on his W cooldown this is the one all-in that beats him pre-item.","Your Alternator/Rocketbelt spike cashes the R combo into a kill, but his first item walls chokes with the minefield — even race.","R down, he kites with Satchel and E mines and out-ranges everything you have — a scaled Ziggs makes your squishy caster body useless on the sidelane."]}
