window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"kennen","b":"locke","win":["Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Locke","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Your poke levels 1-5","text":"Range and marks win every exchange, but he endures chip by design — build a slow HP lead, do not force a kill that is not there."},{"when":"Locke 6 + first item","text":"Purgatory plus dive threat against your zero sustain — the one stage he owns. Stay above execute range at all times."},{"when":"Your two-plus items","text":"Item poke and your teamfight R bring it back level — group, flank, and match his picks with won fights."},{"text":"Purgatory falls from 120 seconds at rank 1 to 80 at rank 3 — his pick is no longer a once-a-fight event, so stop walking side lanes alone and take fights grouped, where your R answers his.","when":"R rank 3"}],"wants":{"you":["Poke on cooldown, never all-in","Bank HP before his item spike","Match his picks with teamfight R"],"foe":["Absorb chip and farm through it","All-in at 6 plus first item","Execute you before your stun lands"]},"early":"You out-range him, and shurikens plus mark-stacking win every individual trade — but he is built to endure exactly this chip, so nothing here is free. Poke him on cooldown, keep your spacing so his level-3 dash never lands clean, and do not burn E chasing a kill the lane has not offered pre-6.","mid":"At 6 the stat check is even and execution decides the first fight — but his first item changes that: Purgatory plus dive threat punishes the sustain you simply do not have. Respect the window hard: stay above half HP, keep the wave on your side of the river, and buy your own item before trading again.","late":"Post-items it levels back out into a skill test — his pick threat against your teamfight ult. Play the flanks, stun-lock the fight he tries to start, and never wander alone where one Purgatory pick decides everything; grouped up, your R is worth more than his.","whys":["Level 1 is a patience test: your shuriken range and mark poke win the trades, but he is built to absorb chip — even.","Level 2 stays even — you keep out-poking him, but he plays around your cooldowns to keep it survivable.","Level 3 stays balanced: careful spacing around your shurikens lets him farm through the pre-6 window.","Levels 4-5 stay neutral — neither side commits fully while your stun threat keeps his trades honest.","At 6 the raw stats are even; the all-in tools tilt on execution, so skill decides the first real fight.","At first item his Purgatory-plus-dive punishes your total lack of sustain — his clear all-in edge.","Late stays a skill test — your teamfight R matches his pick potential in the fight phase."]});
