window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"kennen","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Zaahen","Kennen","Zaahen","Skill","Kennen","Kennen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Your level 3","text":"Q poke plus E stun-stacking comes online — free chunks at range while his engage cannot answer."},{"when":"Zaahen levels 4-5","text":"His all-in window: once Lightning Rush is down, Aureate Rush closes and he wins — track your own 10s E."},{"when":"Your first item","text":"Liandry's poke and self-peel flip the lane — he can no longer afford to walk at you."},{"when":"Full build","text":"You flank, stun-kite, and delete him before his lock ever lands — teamfights are yours."}],"wants":{"you":["Chunk from range with Q and marks","Keep E up whenever he can engage","Kite his engage with item speed"],"foe":["Punish your spent cooldowns at 4-5","Force you to burn R just to survive","Lock you down before your stun stacks"]},"early":"The lane breathes in waves: level 2 is his — your stun setup is not stacked yet, so give him nothing — but level 3 flips it as Q poke and E stun-stacking start chunking him for free. Then respect the 4-5 window: once your E is spent his gap-close all-in beats your squishy frame, so poke only with everything up.","mid":"At 6 be honest about your ult: it is a long-cooldown teamfight tool, and spending it just to peel his engage is a real cost, so the stage sits even. First item is your true spike — Liandry's poke plus movement speed means you whittle him down and kite the very all-in he used to win with.","late":"Two-plus items and you own it: flank the fight, stun-stack him inside your storm before his lockdown ever lands, and delete him. In side lanes keep max range and never let him engage first — a Kennen who starts the fight wins it; one who eats the engage does not.","whys":["Level 1 is even farm before either of you has a combo online.","At level 2 he edges the trades while your stun setup is not stacked yet.","Level 3 is yours: Q poke and E stun-stacking chunk him for free at range.","In the 4-5 window Aureate Rush closes on you the moment your Lightning Rush is spent.","Level 6 is even — your R is a long-cooldown teamfight tool you are forced to spend just to peel him.","At first item your Liandry's poke and self-peel let you kite and out-whittle him.","By two-plus items you flank, stun-kite, and delete him before he can lock you down."]});
